hUVehUxuErvHr6icFrvvyNkmQZu9DwU9or5OktNoTck2RGyBIBZQfnED_v0lIiwdWbLeX11XmlMVGgiwx6FOoXy-nt8psOafhJQFDRQl4IXqOgvJaHvigjc9-NIn9SH6GSpNq0vl-6mW_qrldDg28ptLNtPCf1lAjn5Fr6XO3IHOTnLoJojSmDak_wVESntOdqtOBZjI5gikYzmsg7hvM0JsDMI7KRWVYj0EgGyVXXGEJrQUBlbHQ1yk_iF6WlOo3DKCrgiTnBh32G0phekSKB1BTVGAMh9Ceqt53AV9joyPaM43xfpbFvXCbdkGEX8q8_T5uTx8bIr3k7C52LkU5QI3hohDbGgZ9EqtYpigmrjwjUCjowoFe3QhskJrFj9_PYUBW3RWkmReUZpcrvCUtl7zLcsSj3TafIQofAElzA259zvGmroMtU7JStxVMSxAr1GbhTiYvxGKlhyV6ulQTSjeF0G2mfA6-fJ5bYdUH_VCnrL9g=\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47071ed487d190ff5056a5d60bde\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Clarifying account needs**\\n\\nI should consider whether the accounts are for personal or business use and what specific features matter most. Asking about things like opening deposits and ongoing balances could help me check for any fees or requirements. I think it’s better not to promise that one option will meet all needs since there are still unknowns. Instead, I’ll say something like, “I’ll narrow down the options for you.” I want to make my questions warm and nice.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"logprobs\":[],\"text\":\"{\\\"message\\\":\\\"Absolutely—I can do the comparison for you and recommend a checking account and a savings account, explaining the key fees and requirements in plain language before you decide.\\\\n\\\\nWhat are your specific must-haves for each account? It would also help to know:\\\\n• Whether these are for personal or business use.\\\\n• Roughly how much you plan to deposit initially and keep in each account.\\\\n• Any deal-breakers, such as monthly fees, minimum balances, or withdrawal restrictions.\\\\n\\\\nEstimates are fine—we can take it one step at a time.\\\"}\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc470f4f8487d186a25f7f8fc4019d\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"content\":\"Thank you—yes, please do it one step at a time.\\n\\nThese would be **personal** (not business) accounts.\\n\\nFor the **new checking account**, my biggest issue is travel: I travel internationally pretty often—Japan and Europe for client work, maybe **3–4 trips a year**—and I end up using ATMs abroad constantly. Those ATM fees really eat into my budget. **Is there any way to get those reimbursed?**\",\"role\":\"user\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"personal checking account international ATM fee reimbursement travel foreign ATMs\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_W2LOfjo344yjcVwAcJAVnsM4\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc4714c1b487d191462ba35a96cc1d\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_W2LOfjo344yjcVwAcJAVnsM4\",\"output\":\"1. Bluest Account exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_003\\n   Score: 19.9597\\n   Content: ## What you get with Bluest Account\\n\\n- Higher yield on your checking balance: 2.25% APY\\n- Complimentary domestic outgoing wires each month: 10\\n- Incoming domestic wires at no charge: $0.00\\n- Dedicated personal banker assigned: Yes\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates, up to: $50\\n- Complimentary personal check orders per year: 3\\n- Safe deposit box rental discount: 75.0%\\n- Stop payment requests at no charge: $0\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00\\n- Boosts on linked savings:\\n  - Silver Savings APY boost: 0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings APY boost: 0.7%\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Included |\\n|---|---|\\n| Checking APY | 2.25% |\\n| Free domestic outgoing wires (per month) | 10 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Dedicated personal banker | Yes |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly cap) | $50 |\\n| Complimentary check orders (per year) | 3 |\\n| Safe deposit box discount | 75.0% |\\n| Stop payment fee | $0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Silver Savings APY boost | 0.45% |\\n| Bronze Savings APY boost | 0.7% |\\n\\n## Referral rewards\\n\\nShare the Bluest experience and earn rewards:\\n- Referrer bonus: $75 per successful referral\\n- New member bonus: $50 for the person you refer\\n- Annual limit: 8 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n- Qualifying requirement: Referred person must deposit $2,000 within 90 days\\n- Eligibility: Referrers must have established their Rho-Bank checking relationship at least 60 days prior.\\n\\n## How to use your benefits\\n\\n### Complimentary wire transfers\\n- Send up to 10 domestic wire transfers per calendar month at no charge.\\n- Incoming domestic wires post with a $0.00 fee.\\n\\n### Dedicated personal banker\\n- A dedicated banker is assigned to your account (Yes). Use this single point of contact for complex transactions, expedited support, and account planning.\\n\\n### ATM fee rebates\\n- When you incur third-party ATM fees, you are rebated up to $50 per monthly statement cycle.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Withdraw from ATMs abroad with no Rho-Bank fee: $0.00. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n### Complimentary check orders\\n- Place up to 3 personal check orders each year at no cost.\\n\\n### Safe deposit box discount\\n- Receive a 75.0% discount on an eligible safe deposit box rental.\\n\\n### Stop payments\\n- Submit stop payment requests with a waived fee of $0.\\n\\n### Enhanced yields\\n- Earn 2.25% APY on your Bluest Account balance.\\n- Link eligible savings to activate boosts:\\n  - Silver Savings: +0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings: +0.7%\\n\\n2. Navy Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_009\\n   Score: 18.7381\\n   Content: ## Where ATM fees apply for Navy Blue\\n- Out-of-network usage: Any transaction at a non‑Rho ATM is assessed a per‑transaction fee of $2.50.\\n- International usage: ATM cash withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs are assessed a fee of 3% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $5.00.\\n- Operator surcharges: The ATM owner may charge an additional surcharge at the terminal. This surcharge is separate from Rho fees.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\n| Scenario | Fee | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Domestic out‑of‑network ATM transaction | $2.50 per transaction | Applies at non‑Rho ATMs in the U.S. |\\n| International ATM cash withdrawal | 3% of withdrawal amount (min. $5.00) | Applies at foreign ATMs outside the U.S. |\\n| Monthly rebates for out‑of‑network usage | Up to $10 per calendar month | Rebates are capped at the monthly limit. |\\n\\n## How international ATM withdrawal fees are calculated\\n- Calculation: The fee equals the greater of:\\n  - 3% of the cash withdrawal amount, or\\n  - $5.00 (minimum)\\n- Threshold for the minimum to apply: The minimum applies when the withdrawal amount is less than or equal to $5.00 divided by 3%.\\n\\n## When fees can combine\\n- If you use an international ATM that is also out‑of‑network, both the $2.50 out‑of‑network fee and the international withdrawal fee of 3% (minimum $5.00) can apply.\\n- ATM operator surcharges, if any, are in addition to the above.\\n\\n## Monthly rebate details\\n- Rho rebates up to $10 in out‑of‑network ATM fees per calendar month.\\n- The monthly cap is the maximum total rebated; fees above this amount are your responsibility after the cap is reached.\\n\\n## Tips to minimize ATM costs\\n- Use Rho ATMs whenever possible to avoid the out‑of‑network fee of $2.50.\\n- For international cash needs, consider making larger, less frequent withdrawals to reduce the impact of the $5.00 minimum relative to the withdrawal amount.\\n- Always review any on‑screen ATM operator surcharge disclosures before completing a transaction.\\n\\n3. Why am I being charged a fee on my Lime Green Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_008\\n   Score: 18.6411\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you may see a fee\\n\\nYou may see one or more of the following fees on your Lime Green Account:\\n\\n- Monthly maintenance fee if your balance does not meet the waiver threshold\\n- Fees for sending domestic or international wire transfers\\n- Fees for using non‑Rho ATMs, including percentage‑based fees for foreign ATM withdrawals\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Fee type | When it’s charged | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | Your balance does not meet the waiver threshold | $25.00 |\\n| Domestic wire transfer | You send a domestic wire | $10.00 |\\n| International wire transfer | You send an international wire to a foreign bank | $25.00 |\\n| Non‑Rho ATM (U.S.) | You withdraw cash at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | You withdraw cash at an international ATM | 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $2.50 |\\n\\n## Monthly maintenance fee\\n\\n- You are charged $25.00 when your account balance does not meet $15,000.\\n- To avoid this fee, maintain a balance at or above $15,000.\\n\\n## Wire transfer fees\\n\\n- Domestic wires: Each outgoing domestic wire you send incurs a fee of $10.00.\\n- International wires: Each outgoing international wire to a foreign bank incurs a fee of $25.00.\\n\\n## ATM‑related fees\\n\\n- Non‑Rho ATMs in the U.S.: You are charged $1.00 per withdrawal when using a non‑Rho ATM.\\n- Foreign (international) ATMs: You are charged 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum fee of $2.50.\\n  - How to estimate: Multiply your withdrawal amount by 1.5% and compare the result to $2.50. The higher number is the fee.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Review your transaction history for a separate fee line item (for example, a description referencing maintenance, wire, or ATM).\\n2. Match the amount to one of the following:\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $10.00\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $1.00\\n   - For foreign ATM withdrawals, the greater of:\\n     - 1.5% of your withdrawal amount, or\\n     - $2.50\\n\\n## Ways to avoid or reduce fees\\n\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $15,000 to waive $25.00.\\n- Use Rho‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.\\n- Plan international cash needs to minimize the number of foreign ATM withdrawals subject to 1.5% (minimum $2.50).\\n\\n## If you believe a fee is incorrect\\n\\n- Gather details (date, amount, and description of the fee; related transaction, if any).\\n- Contact support with these details so we can review and correct any errors promptly.\\n\\n4. World Blue: Free International ATM Access\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_009\\n   Score: 17.0100\\n   Content: ## What you pay at foreign ATMs\\n\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% (minimum $0.00)\\n- Foreign ATM fee rebates: Up to $100 per calendar month for fees charged by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals\\n\\nYou will not be charged a Rho fee for international ATM withdrawals. If the foreign ATM operator adds its own fee, we rebate those fees automatically up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n### Snapshot of foreign ATM costs\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 0% |\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee minimum | $0.00 |\\n| Maximum monthly rebate for foreign ATM fees | $100 |\\n\\n## Monthly rebate rules\\n\\n- Coverage: Rebates apply to fees assessed by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals.\\n- Cap: We rebate up to a total of $100 in a calendar month. Fees above this amount will not be reimbursed for that month.\\n- Posting: Rebates are issued automatically after the withdrawal and associated fee post to your account. No enrollment or receipt submission is required.\\n\\nTip: Keep your ATM receipt when a foreign ATM displays or charges a fee; it’s useful for reference if you need to follow up.\\n\\n## How to make a fee-free withdrawal abroad\\n\\n1. Use your card at an international ATM that accepts it.\\n2. When prompted, select a withdrawal from checking.\\n3. If asked about currency choice, choose to be charged in the local currency rather than having the ATM convert the amount.\\n4. Complete your withdrawal. If the ATM charges a fee, it will typically display it before you confirm.\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n- You withdraw the equivalent of $200 at a foreign ATM.\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% with a $0.00 minimum, so you pay $0 to Rho.\\n- The ATM operator charges a $5 fee. We automatically rebate $5, counting toward your $100 monthly cap.\\n\\n5. Lime Green Account: ATM Access and Fee Rebates\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_007\\n   Score: 16.7008\\n   Content: ## ATM Access\\n\\n- You can use out-of-network ATMs for cash withdrawals. Each out-of-network ATM transaction is assessed a fee of $1.00.\\n- International (foreign) ATM withdrawals incur a fee equal to 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50 per withdrawal.\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM transaction fee (domestic) | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 1.5% of amount; minimum $2.50 |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebate cap (out-of-network usage) | Up to $25 per month |\\n\\n## ATM Fee Rebates\\n\\n- Your account provides monthly rebates of eligible fees from out-of-network ATM usage, up to $25 per month.\\n- Rebates are applied until the monthly cap is reached; any eligible fees above the cap are your responsibility.\\n- You do not need to take additional action for eligible rebates—fees and corresponding credits will appear as separate line items on your account activity once processed.\\n\\n### What counts toward the monthly cap\\n\\n- Fees assessed for out-of-network ATM usage that are charged to your account are counted toward the $25 monthly rebate limit.\\n\\n## How fees are calculated\\n\\n- Domestic out-of-network usage: Each withdrawal is charged $1.00.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals: The fee is 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50. If the percentage-based amount is less than $2.50, the $2.50 minimum applies.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, multiple withdrawals:\\n  - If you make several out-of-network withdrawals in a month, each is charged $1.00. Eligible out-of-network ATM fees will be rebated up to a total of $25 for that month.\\n\\n- Foreign withdrawal:\\n  - For a single international withdrawal, your fee is calculated at 1.5% of the withdrawn amount, subject to a $2.50 minimum. The applicable amount is charged at the time the transaction is processed.\\n\\n## Tips to reduce fees\\n\\n- Consolidate cash needs into fewer withdrawals to limit per-transaction charges of $1.00.\\n- Monitor your monthly total of out-of-network ATM fees to understand how close you are to the $25 rebate cap.\\n\\n6. World Blue: Traveling Abroad with Your Business Account\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_005\\n   Score: 16.4103\\n   Content: ## Using Your Account Abroad: Cash, Payments, and Controls\\n\\nTraveling internationally with World Blue is straightforward. The following guidance covers how to access cash, move money, and manage team permissions while you’re on the road.\\n\\n### Accessing Cash at Foreign ATMs\\n\\n- You can withdraw local currency abroad without a foreign ATM fee from us.\\n- Our foreign ATM withdrawal fee is 0% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $0.00.\\n\\nATM fee policy summary:\\n- Rho foreign ATM fee: 0% (minimum $0.00)\\n- Rebate of ATM operator surcharges: Up to $100 per month\\n\\nBest practices when withdrawing:\\n- Choose to be charged in the local currency and decline “dynamic currency conversion” on the ATM to access low‑margin FX rates.\\n- Prefer bank‑branded ATMs; avoid independent kiosks in tourist areas when possible.\\n- Keep ATM receipts until your statement closes in case you need to reference fees.\\n- If multiple employees are traveling, consider setting withdrawal limits and time‑of‑day windows via role permissions.\\n\\n### Sending and Receiving Payments While Abroad\\n\\n- You can send and receive cross‑border payments in $140 countries/regions via SWIFT and, where eligible, SEPA.\\n- Use SEPA for euro‑area beneficiaries when available; use SWIFT for other destinations and currencies.\\n\\nTo send an international payment on the road:\\n1. Add or select the beneficiary.\\n2. Choose the payment network (SEPA where eligible, otherwise SWIFT).\\n3. Select the funding currency from your multi‑currency balances or convert before sending.\\n4. Enter amount and review the overview screen for currency and network details.\\n5. Submit and monitor delivery status in your activity feed.\\n\\nReceiving payments while abroad:\\n- Share the correct currency‑specific receiving details from your account profile with overseas payers.\\n- If a payer requests network preference, provide SEPA details for euro payments within the SEPA area; otherwise provide SWIFT details.\\n\\n### Depositing Funds While Traveling\\n\\n- Mobile check deposit is available up to $20,000 per day.\\n- Tips for smooth deposits while abroad:\\n  - Use clear, well‑lit images on a flat, dark background.\\n  - Endorse checks as required and include any instructed phrases in the endorsement.\\n  - Retain the physical check securely until the deposit is confirmed.\\n\\n### Managing Team Access and Approvals on the Road\\n\\nUse tiered permissions to keep control while enabling travel flexibility:\\n- Create a “Travel” role with only the capabilities your travelers need (e.g., ATM withdrawals, card spend, or initiating—but not approving—international wires).\\n- Set per‑user spend limits and require approvals for high‑value SWIFT payments.\\n- Restrict who can add new international beneficiaries; require a second approver before first‑time payments.\\n\\n### Pre‑Trip Checklist\\n\\n- Confirm each traveler’s ATM PIN and test a small withdrawal before departure.\\n- Set or review withdrawal and spend limits appropriate for the trip’s costs.\\n- Pre‑add frequent international beneficiaries and verify their details.\\n- Ensure the right approvers will be available across time zones for urgent payments.\\n\\n7. True Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_011\\n   Score: 16.2181\\n   Content: ## Fees at a glance\\n\\n| Transaction type | Where it applies | Fee |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal | Domestic (U.S.) non-Rho ATMs | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM cash withdrawal | International ATMs | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 per withdrawal |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebates (cap) | Out-of-network ATM usage | Up to $30 per month |\\n\\nNote: ATM owners may assess their own surcharges on out-of-network transactions. Those surcharges are separate from Rho’s fees.\\n\\n## Domestic out-of-network ATM usage (U.S.)\\n\\n- When you use a non-Rho ATM domestically, you are charged $1.00 per transaction.\\n- The ATM owner may also charge a separate surcharge at the terminal; you can accept or cancel the transaction after the surcharge is disclosed.\\n\\nExample:\\n- If you complete 5 out-of-network withdrawals in a month, Rho’s fees would total 5 × $1.00. Any ATM owner surcharges would be in addition to this amount.\\n\\n## International ATM withdrawals\\n\\n- For cash withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs, the fee is 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00 per withdrawal.\\n- The percentage is applied to each withdrawal; if the calculated amount is below $3.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- $100 withdrawal: 2% = $2.00, which is below the $3.00 minimum, so the fee is $3.00.\\n- $200 withdrawal: 2% = $4.00, so the fee is $4.00.\\n\\n## Monthly ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You can receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network ATM usage.\\n- The cap is applied on a monthly basis; once total eligible ATM fees reach $30 for the month, no additional ATM fee rebates are provided for that month.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $12, up to $12 may be rebated (within the $30 cap).\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $36, the maximum rebate is $30.\\n\\n## Tips to manage costs\\n\\n- Prefer Rho ATMs to avoid the $1.00 out-of-network fee.\\n- Abroad, consider fewer, larger withdrawals to reduce the impact of the $3.00 per-withdrawal minimum.\\n- Track your monthly ATM fees so you know when you are approaching the $30 cap.\\n\\n8. Hunter Green Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_hunter_green_010\\n   Score: 15.7402\\n   Content: ## Fee Summary\\n\\n- Out-of-network (non‑Rho) ATM transactions (domestic): $2.00 per transaction\\n- International ATM withdrawals: 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00 per withdrawal\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates for out-of-network usage: Up to $20 per month\\n\\nNote: ATM owner/operator surcharges are set by the ATM and are separate from Rho fees.\\n\\n## How Fees Apply\\n\\n### Domestic out-of-network usage\\n- Each cash withdrawal at a non‑Rho ATM incurs a $2.00 fee.\\n- Any surcharge displayed by the ATM owner/operator will be charged in addition to the Rho fee.\\n- Eligible out-of-network ATM fees are automatically rebated until you reach the monthly cap of $20.\\n\\n### International ATM withdrawals\\n- Each withdrawal outside the U.S. incurs a fee of 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum charge of $4.00 per withdrawal.\\n- If the international withdrawal is made at a non‑Rho ATM, the $2.00 out-of-network fee also applies.\\n- ATM owner/operator surcharges at foreign ATMs may also be charged.\\n- Eligible out-of-network ATM fees are rebated up to the monthly maximum of $20.\\n\\n## Calculating Your Total Cost\\n\\nFor each ATM withdrawal:\\n1. Add any ATM owner/operator surcharge shown at the terminal.\\n2. If the ATM is non‑Rho, add $2.00.\\n3. If the withdrawal is international, add 2.5% of the withdrawal amount (minimum $4.00).\\n4. Subtract any applicable rebates, up to a total of $20 per month.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, non‑Rho ATM, $100 withdrawal:\\n  - Rho out-of-network fee: $2.00\\n  - Plus any ATM owner surcharge\\n  - Rebated up to your remaining monthly $20 cap\\n\\n- International ATM, $100 withdrawal:\\n  - International fee: 2.5% of $100 = $2.50, but minimum applies → $4.00\\n  - Out-of-network fee (if the ATM is non‑Rho): $2.00\\n  - Plus any ATM owner surcharge\\n  - Rebated up to your remaining monthly $20 cap\\n\\n- International ATM, $400 withdrawal:\\n  - International fee: 2.5% of $400 = $10.00\\n  - Out-of-network fee (if the ATM is non‑Rho): $2.00\\n  - Plus any ATM owner surcharge\\n  - Rebated up to your remaining monthly $20 cap\\n\\n## Posting and Visibility\\n\\n- Fees and any related rebates appear as separate line items on your account activity and statements.\\n- You can track how much of the $20 monthly rebate you have used by reviewing your statement or recent transactions.\\n\\n9. Why am I being charged a fee on my True Blue Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_010\\n   Score: 15.3054\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you’re seeing a fee\\n\\nBelow are the most common fee types that can appear on a True Blue account and why they’re charged.\\n\\n| Fee type | When you’ll see it | Amount posted |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your qualifying balance did not meet the waiver threshold for the applicable evaluation period | $75.00 (waived when balance requirement of $50,000 is met) |\\n| Domestic Wire Transfer Fee | You sent a domestic wire from your account | $5.00 per outbound domestic wire |\\n| Out-of-Network ATM Fee | You completed a transaction at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at an international (non‑U.S.) ATM | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 |\\n\\n### Example for foreign ATM fee\\n- If you withdraw $200 at a foreign ATM, the fee is 2% of $200 ($4). Because $4 exceeds the minimum $3.00, $4 would post.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Check your latest statement or transaction history for the fee line item and posted amount.  \\n2. Match the posted amount to the fees above:\\n   - $75.00 typically indicates the Monthly Maintenance Fee.\\n   - $5.00 typically indicates a Domestic Wire Transfer Fee.\\n   - $1.00 typically indicates an Out-of-Network ATM Fee.\\n   - A calculated amount equal to 2% of your ATM withdrawal (or $3.00, whichever is higher) indicates a Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee.\\n3. For the Monthly Maintenance Fee, compare your balance during the billing period to the waiver threshold of $50,000.\\n\\n## How to reduce or avoid future fees\\n\\n- Maintain at least $50,000 to have the $75.00 waived.  \\n- Use Rho in‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.  \\n- When abroad, be aware that each cash withdrawal will incur 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00.  \\n- Send domestic wires only when necessary to limit paying $5.00 per wire.\\n\\n## Need help?\\n\\nIf you believe a fee was posted in error, gather the transaction date, amount, and any related activity (e.g., wire reference or ATM withdrawal details) and contact support for a review.\\n\\n10. Business Gold Rewards Card: Travel Perks and Concierge Services\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_business_gold_rewards_card_008\\n   Score: 15.1366\\n   Content: ## Travel Credits\\n- Your account provides annual credits totaling $200.\\n- Use your card for eligible travel bookings; credits apply automatically once the charge is identified as eligible.\\n\\n## Concierge Services\\n- Concierge included: Yes.\\n- Request support for itinerary planning, complex multi-stop trips, dining reservations, and urgent changes. Initiate requests from your account’s concierge portal.\\n\\n## International Advantage\\n- Foreign transaction fee: 0%. This enables international purchases without added foreign transaction charges from this fee.\\n\\n## Tips to Maximize Value\\n- Verify a travel purchase qualifies for credits before booking.\\n- For complex itineraries, submit concierge requests early with preferred dates, cabin classes, and flexibility parameters.\\n- Keep confirmation emails accessible in case the concierge or credits team requests verification.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEcYy_oxIYS3gBFxMBMOttrGyqbaaJE9TwmF7taJjGc6NYM4zqseY7pQGnDNdvj12xbDX70uTfWvclF8u4YQ45BmJvmSuS9Vr6NTMM9RQkQssyRlvo15ixPiNQ535IkgYlyAWLutnlKh4sXZtvyNYd4zaCpzpllmzXkRSzCQM6jNUofbhS2feTIfFkyp_XV5vBrbDPMUK5F3j_jCgvn9Nsbi7Ri_CwVhy3TMqqybgOVk6qU8ns5jr8qSRuQ1P-pGZFfFsxJDrczgIlNOcLQi2X9Cq-9LHNnhf7pRGZWCFJyOk3e_EkHyLK_KrQL6TO0-B0rrclTllCOeZST49RqCJgT544I8CaRigrKgcl_YqAlYNtYEXYb1pceXaeB1R56IsdLrO8zNNPfd6a5omX-F0GVOoFGRT8E7tQr1jazO5zfvwLrepmwdOIJ4XPsy3UWmji5Pd8culXVZKc1ziWU6hGNDfLvj2fWZ99n10b5yAuPZfbj7suQYyN1LHO9gB46Lu_wagiypLspevJkZD2k30qALKr_KPMLhLF_h6yBfZdI-7wZhNYSu49Yv1gztPM24v47VYCjs8IGn5cCePL61o2mnQW4vXmqgOmzFNAxsZlZ1O7ZCSj-zD-6eDFLisTC5LFjCuyBvAyOhG2HjYOgWgX1q_GjIFrjvWDRyi3Tp9nGkbgb4LEItXCU6WDtPsfmjWJTtbH4ha09ox3vEyRKLLKFSfyrnaaJp9AuMUkKtBK0I0H1UjUBe-Gn52tnsrBs7BBJ0p5-UISxj65JxXV1Jymfhj-FuW6otQfup_qC0vMkStxW4vuJay9ix92aFPIM907XV2MnCxD8dAHgUVWaBDxnCOBoQPMQggdCNgw32SEV4wNQ47hMzZOcwGMRlex4l8MoJ1DKxCuIdJsZz2zZ_vGSiLrDSTMD9zxvWKenHq-5Nx10YGtWbiKqxz-RazcyxNfTUjYEne4tSIfNqU6YXHS3FlYJhjSEGiXAw0MxRvHKkjpiXIgOX3pYcFDUnxM9TZyTqDcEcVkIXpFlibi5MlcG7RBqGuQ1-ynMFRIQ5MAeBibzWqRmWbB5J6Q2o7TWbJ4CetllmhQy1lz6VZFGY_pLAb3RzUEsTejIL-z2hUvdnH3_ddOe84mmccoelviocb43CTL7nfDOHeimue_-5iyCTxMmD8VCh_4qgxGHzNjhsAKDBHn6j8aDTt1CC_74li-M71A_E2MSEV-pVCpca0rNphIxXEvko25SQw8ww9AWPTW_CugHKIJcBYK_NLKijyN5ltUXdm7nHKyq-I8QNyuBWwYg1_fk7-E1R50fkvYOWvgmmaSSv9tsOoo4xvO56EYS1wHoKfWgUdXOHQRqQsG2l-dQJsi8xMejE7yBZ6Pi4O_V5uHCOrQb_GFD-KiBolLysjGBf8fmDNoDWDesslCv9mCQ2b6mMj6jX2q3CMCSiw2SOj1s0_pl04qIf8U6kq0Y6CBehx3S4WnQPJ7fI4Xnl7f_qkTWsprPakZVDr34hHnQ-0neYZiB_EzwYMlnJRx1Es7DNST_5SZ6F3GuwBmYCdQ==\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47168ae887d1aa9489e7d1dbdaab\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"checking accounts international ATM fees rebates personal Blue Bluest Purple Evergreen\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_GukL6NwMyXPQ7arAmqgs7vB3\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc4717fda487d1971fd2618bf7e1cc\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_GukL6NwMyXPQ7arAmqgs7vB3\",\"output\":\"1. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 29.2190\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n2. Bluest Account exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_003\\n   Score: 22.2200\\n   Content: ## What you get with Bluest Account\\n\\n- Higher yield on your checking balance: 2.25% APY\\n- Complimentary domestic outgoing wires each month: 10\\n- Incoming domestic wires at no charge: $0.00\\n- Dedicated personal banker assigned: Yes\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates, up to: $50\\n- Complimentary personal check orders per year: 3\\n- Safe deposit box rental discount: 75.0%\\n- Stop payment requests at no charge: $0\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00\\n- Boosts on linked savings:\\n  - Silver Savings APY boost: 0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings APY boost: 0.7%\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Included |\\n|---|---|\\n| Checking APY | 2.25% |\\n| Free domestic outgoing wires (per month) | 10 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Dedicated personal banker | Yes |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly cap) | $50 |\\n| Complimentary check orders (per year) | 3 |\\n| Safe deposit box discount | 75.0% |\\n| Stop payment fee | $0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Silver Savings APY boost | 0.45% |\\n| Bronze Savings APY boost | 0.7% |\\n\\n## Referral rewards\\n\\nShare the Bluest experience and earn rewards:\\n- Referrer bonus: $75 per successful referral\\n- New member bonus: $50 for the person you refer\\n- Annual limit: 8 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n- Qualifying requirement: Referred person must deposit $2,000 within 90 days\\n- Eligibility: Referrers must have established their Rho-Bank checking relationship at least 60 days prior.\\n\\n## How to use your benefits\\n\\n### Complimentary wire transfers\\n- Send up to 10 domestic wire transfers per calendar month at no charge.\\n- Incoming domestic wires post with a $0.00 fee.\\n\\n### Dedicated personal banker\\n- A dedicated banker is assigned to your account (Yes). Use this single point of contact for complex transactions, expedited support, and account planning.\\n\\n### ATM fee rebates\\n- When you incur third-party ATM fees, you are rebated up to $50 per monthly statement cycle.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Withdraw from ATMs abroad with no Rho-Bank fee: $0.00. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n### Complimentary check orders\\n- Place up to 3 personal check orders each year at no cost.\\n\\n### Safe deposit box discount\\n- Receive a 75.0% discount on an eligible safe deposit box rental.\\n\\n### Stop payments\\n- Submit stop payment requests with a waived fee of $0.\\n\\n### Enhanced yields\\n- Earn 2.25% APY on your Bluest Account balance.\\n- Link eligible savings to activate boosts:\\n  - Silver Savings: +0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings: +0.7%\\n\\n3. Using ATMs worldwide\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_004\\n   Score: 19.9720\\n   Content: ## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your Purple Account debit card has a daily ATM withdrawal limit of $1,000. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals worldwide within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## How ATM rebates work\\n- You are eligible for refunds of ATM operator fees up to a monthly cap of $30.\\n- Rebates apply after eligible ATM fees post to your account and are credited up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n## Best practices when withdrawing cash abroad\\n- Choose the checking account option on the ATM when prompted.\\n- Retain the ATM receipt if it shows a surcharge to help with any rebate review.\\n- Avoid optional dynamic currency conversion at the ATM if you prefer to be billed in the local currency.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n- If you believe a rebate is missing, verify whether your monthly total rebates have reached $30 and confirm that the charge was coded as an ATM operator fee.\\n\\n4. ATM fee rebates for Bluest\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_007\\n   Score: 19.6001\\n   Content: ## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your Bluest Account debit card has a daily ATM withdrawal limit of $1,500. This applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## Monthly rebate cap\\n- You are eligible for ATM fee rebates up to $50 per month.\\n\\n### How rebates are applied\\n- Rebates are credited until you reach the monthly maximum of $50.\\n- If your aggregate ATM fees exceed $50 in a given month, the excess will not be rebated.\\n\\n### Tips for maximizing rebates\\n- Keep track of your cumulative ATM fees during the month to stay within the $50 cap.\\n- Consider using fee-free ATMs once you approach the monthly cap.\\n\\n5. Navy Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_009\\n   Score: 18.9277\\n   Content: ## Where ATM fees apply for Navy Blue\\n- Out-of-network usage: Any transaction at a non‑Rho ATM is assessed a per‑transaction fee of $2.50.\\n- International usage: ATM cash withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs are assessed a fee of 3% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $5.00.\\n- Operator surcharges: The ATM owner may charge an additional surcharge at the terminal. This surcharge is separate from Rho fees.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\n| Scenario | Fee | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Domestic out‑of‑network ATM transaction | $2.50 per transaction | Applies at non‑Rho ATMs in the U.S. |\\n| International ATM cash withdrawal | 3% of withdrawal amount (min. $5.00) | Applies at foreign ATMs outside the U.S. |\\n| Monthly rebates for out‑of‑network usage | Up to $10 per calendar month | Rebates are capped at the monthly limit. |\\n\\n## How international ATM withdrawal fees are calculated\\n- Calculation: The fee equals the greater of:\\n  - 3% of the cash withdrawal amount, or\\n  - $5.00 (minimum)\\n- Threshold for the minimum to apply: The minimum applies when the withdrawal amount is less than or equal to $5.00 divided by 3%.\\n\\n## When fees can combine\\n- If you use an international ATM that is also out‑of‑network, both the $2.50 out‑of‑network fee and the international withdrawal fee of 3% (minimum $5.00) can apply.\\n- ATM operator surcharges, if any, are in addition to the above.\\n\\n## Monthly rebate details\\n- Rho rebates up to $10 in out‑of‑network ATM fees per calendar month.\\n- The monthly cap is the maximum total rebated; fees above this amount are your responsibility after the cap is reached.\\n\\n## Tips to minimize ATM costs\\n- Use Rho ATMs whenever possible to avoid the out‑of‑network fee of $2.50.\\n- For international cash needs, consider making larger, less frequent withdrawals to reduce the impact of the $5.00 minimum relative to the withdrawal amount.\\n- Always review any on‑screen ATM operator surcharge disclosures before completing a transaction.\\n\\n6. Cobalt Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_010\\n   Score: 15.6937\\n   Content: ## Summary of ATM Fees\\n\\n- Domestic out-of-network ATM withdrawal: $2.00 per transaction\\n- International ATM withdrawal: 2.5% of the withdrawal amount (minimum $4.00 per transaction)\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: Up to $15 in out-of-network ATM fee rebates per month\\n\\nNote: ATM owners/operators may charge additional surcharges that you will see at the terminal before you complete the transaction.\\n\\n## Domestic Out-of-Network ATM Usage\\n\\nWhen you use an ATM outside the in-network system within the United States:\\n- You are charged $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Some ATM owners add their own surcharge. You can choose to cancel the transaction if you do not want to accept an operator surcharge.\\n- You can receive up to $15 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network usage. These rebates can offset qualifying out-of-network ATM fees you incur, up to the monthly cap.\\n\\nTips to minimize domestic fees:\\n- Combine cash needs into fewer withdrawals to reduce per-transaction fees.\\n- Check the ATM’s on-screen disclosure for any operator surcharges before accepting.\\n\\n## International ATM Withdrawals\\n\\nFor withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs:\\n- You are charged 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00 per transaction.\\n- Local ATM owners may add their own surcharges at the terminal.\\n- Exchange rates and any third-party conversion choices at the ATM can affect your total cost.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- Withdraw $200: 2.5% of $200 = $5.00; the fee is $5.00 (exceeds the $4.00 minimum).\\n- Withdraw $100: 2.5% of $100 = $2.50; the $4.00 minimum applies, so the fee is $4.00.\\n\\n## Monthly ATM Fee Rebates\\n\\n- You can receive up to $15 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network ATM usage.\\n- The rebate limit applies on a monthly basis; once you reach $15, additional out-of-network ATM fees will not be rebated that month.\\n\\nExample:\\n- If you make two domestic out-of-network withdrawals, your bank-assessed fees would be 2 × $2.00. Up to $15 of qualifying out-of-network ATM fees may be rebated that month.\\n\\n7. Hunter Green Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_hunter_green_010\\n   Score: 15.1925\\n   Content: ## Fee Summary\\n\\n- Out-of-network (non‑Rho) ATM transactions (domestic): $2.00 per transaction\\n- International ATM withdrawals: 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00 per withdrawal\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates for out-of-network usage: Up to $20 per month\\n\\nNote: ATM owner/operator surcharges are set by the ATM and are separate from Rho fees.\\n\\n## How Fees Apply\\n\\n### Domestic out-of-network usage\\n- Each cash withdrawal at a non‑Rho ATM incurs a $2.00 fee.\\n- Any surcharge displayed by the ATM owner/operator will be charged in addition to the Rho fee.\\n- Eligible out-of-network ATM fees are automatically rebated until you reach the monthly cap of $20.\\n\\n### International ATM withdrawals\\n- Each withdrawal outside the U.S. incurs a fee of 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum charge of $4.00 per withdrawal.\\n- If the international withdrawal is made at a non‑Rho ATM, the $2.00 out-of-network fee also applies.\\n- ATM owner/operator surcharges at foreign ATMs may also be charged.\\n- Eligible out-of-network ATM fees are rebated up to the monthly maximum of $20.\\n\\n## Calculating Your Total Cost\\n\\nFor each ATM withdrawal:\\n1. Add any ATM owner/operator surcharge shown at the terminal.\\n2. If the ATM is non‑Rho, add $2.00.\\n3. If the withdrawal is international, add 2.5% of the withdrawal amount (minimum $4.00).\\n4. Subtract any applicable rebates, up to a total of $20 per month.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, non‑Rho ATM, $100 withdrawal:\\n  - Rho out-of-network fee: $2.00\\n  - Plus any ATM owner surcharge\\n  - Rebated up to your remaining monthly $20 cap\\n\\n- International ATM, $100 withdrawal:\\n  - International fee: 2.5% of $100 = $2.50, but minimum applies → $4.00\\n  - Out-of-network fee (if the ATM is non‑Rho): $2.00\\n  - Plus any ATM owner surcharge\\n  - Rebated up to your remaining monthly $20 cap\\n\\n- International ATM, $400 withdrawal:\\n  - International fee: 2.5% of $400 = $10.00\\n  - Out-of-network fee (if the ATM is non‑Rho): $2.00\\n  - Plus any ATM owner surcharge\\n  - Rebated up to your remaining monthly $20 cap\\n\\n## Posting and Visibility\\n\\n- Fees and any related rebates appear as separate line items on your account activity and statements.\\n- You can track how much of the $20 monthly rebate you have used by reviewing your statement or recent transactions.\\n\\n8. True Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_011\\n   Score: 15.0588\\n   Content: ## Fees at a glance\\n\\n| Transaction type | Where it applies | Fee |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal | Domestic (U.S.) non-Rho ATMs | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM cash withdrawal | International ATMs | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 per withdrawal |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebates (cap) | Out-of-network ATM usage | Up to $30 per month |\\n\\nNote: ATM owners may assess their own surcharges on out-of-network transactions. Those surcharges are separate from Rho’s fees.\\n\\n## Domestic out-of-network ATM usage (U.S.)\\n\\n- When you use a non-Rho ATM domestically, you are charged $1.00 per transaction.\\n- The ATM owner may also charge a separate surcharge at the terminal; you can accept or cancel the transaction after the surcharge is disclosed.\\n\\nExample:\\n- If you complete 5 out-of-network withdrawals in a month, Rho’s fees would total 5 × $1.00. Any ATM owner surcharges would be in addition to this amount.\\n\\n## International ATM withdrawals\\n\\n- For cash withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs, the fee is 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00 per withdrawal.\\n- The percentage is applied to each withdrawal; if the calculated amount is below $3.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- $100 withdrawal: 2% = $2.00, which is below the $3.00 minimum, so the fee is $3.00.\\n- $200 withdrawal: 2% = $4.00, so the fee is $4.00.\\n\\n## Monthly ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You can receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network ATM usage.\\n- The cap is applied on a monthly basis; once total eligible ATM fees reach $30 for the month, no additional ATM fee rebates are provided for that month.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $12, up to $12 may be rebated (within the $30 cap).\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $36, the maximum rebate is $30.\\n\\n## Tips to manage costs\\n\\n- Prefer Rho ATMs to avoid the $1.00 out-of-network fee.\\n- Abroad, consider fewer, larger withdrawals to reduce the impact of the $3.00 per-withdrawal minimum.\\n- Track your monthly ATM fees so you know when you are approaching the $30 cap.\\n\\n9. Lime Green Account: ATM Access and Fee Rebates\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_007\\n   Score: 14.6488\\n   Content: ## ATM Access\\n\\n- You can use out-of-network ATMs for cash withdrawals. Each out-of-network ATM transaction is assessed a fee of $1.00.\\n- International (foreign) ATM withdrawals incur a fee equal to 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50 per withdrawal.\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM transaction fee (domestic) | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 1.5% of amount; minimum $2.50 |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebate cap (out-of-network usage) | Up to $25 per month |\\n\\n## ATM Fee Rebates\\n\\n- Your account provides monthly rebates of eligible fees from out-of-network ATM usage, up to $25 per month.\\n- Rebates are applied until the monthly cap is reached; any eligible fees above the cap are your responsibility.\\n- You do not need to take additional action for eligible rebates—fees and corresponding credits will appear as separate line items on your account activity once processed.\\n\\n### What counts toward the monthly cap\\n\\n- Fees assessed for out-of-network ATM usage that are charged to your account are counted toward the $25 monthly rebate limit.\\n\\n## How fees are calculated\\n\\n- Domestic out-of-network usage: Each withdrawal is charged $1.00.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals: The fee is 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50. If the percentage-based amount is less than $2.50, the $2.50 minimum applies.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, multiple withdrawals:\\n  - If you make several out-of-network withdrawals in a month, each is charged $1.00. Eligible out-of-network ATM fees will be rebated up to a total of $25 for that month.\\n\\n- Foreign withdrawal:\\n  - For a single international withdrawal, your fee is calculated at 1.5% of the withdrawn amount, subject to a $2.50 minimum. The applicable amount is charged at the time the transaction is processed.\\n\\n## Tips to reduce fees\\n\\n- Consolidate cash needs into fewer withdrawals to limit per-transaction charges of $1.00.\\n- Monitor your monthly total of out-of-network ATM fees to understand how close you are to the $25 rebate cap.\\n\\n10. World Blue: Free International ATM Access\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_009\\n   Score: 14.1501\\n   Content: ## What you pay at foreign ATMs\\n\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% (minimum $0.00)\\n- Foreign ATM fee rebates: Up to $100 per calendar month for fees charged by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals\\n\\nYou will not be charged a Rho fee for international ATM withdrawals. If the foreign ATM operator adds its own fee, we rebate those fees automatically up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n### Snapshot of foreign ATM costs\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 0% |\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee minimum | $0.00 |\\n| Maximum monthly rebate for foreign ATM fees | $100 |\\n\\n## Monthly rebate rules\\n\\n- Coverage: Rebates apply to fees assessed by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals.\\n- Cap: We rebate up to a total of $100 in a calendar month. Fees above this amount will not be reimbursed for that month.\\n- Posting: Rebates are issued automatically after the withdrawal and associated fee post to your account. No enrollment or receipt submission is required.\\n\\nTip: Keep your ATM receipt when a foreign ATM displays or charges a fee; it’s useful for reference if you need to follow up.\\n\\n## How to make a fee-free withdrawal abroad\\n\\n1. Use your card at an international ATM that accepts it.\\n2. When prompted, select a withdrawal from checking.\\n3. If asked about currency choice, choose to be charged in the local currency rather than having the ATM convert the amount.\\n4. Complete your withdrawal. If the ATM charges a fee, it will typically display it before you confirm.\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n- You withdraw the equivalent of $200 at a foreign ATM.\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% with a $0.00 minimum, so you pay $0 to Rho.\\n- The ATM operator charges a $5 fee. We automatically rebate $5, counting toward your $100 monthly cap.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEccAxz0TNm2RersEFOy2P75bJlXs2r8XEY_tOgX2Sg1XdWYr38eyo1nPYyPa0qtxl4ZYns3Zor9P4z_1vANpgKERABRZRKmRwlXq8Qi6ucZ9dC_l-8_kLMYApEA-q2iABQnFoEseMo4QsIPtSivtg9Im4B9OpWrh90S6yLsCjO6owfeCxTJrxhDqBf8CIf-GJIJlL2u1a8GMDkX4pePGU8pdqcxAFZpucGHQMuhCx7cmYgr9HPHtiGFPTKF29-KY9htuY7EREHwmh5masGpX_ocCMAD8M-apUPbLRHCYA_bhvd-AYf2dkJLK9J3weSACiqVunmKCDO5FpRpm9D_4rfmHiPjXbLX8BDFvYuwjaCX8LhEG5cBV5Ir4JetJiNBy4YIfmAa2Nx-TL0Qo82wDYU364JdU8sjNBrETCI6w9fYEYoQ14COEtgDgvRqpihTHxXwbbaaAmbYGzaeAoy5rvL3dYiC3f69L0jVpEePSm7uoluvQxFB8Ht8Kp6zUJYkjAzIWeoY6zWvtFOq5NvDpFTY3ZjaOu6TkZjt4xmQCq6iDCYSNcbQGbQdqz4Ct_ty1dGDnfpr9nzCU9Apf1PUTKVi5y9YNwgqg3J33ikSVKQR9rzIBz6zpUrSLct_fgc_G9B18pR1mlQC02RcK7H1szo-T9LYSN6C4T8Cger2YvZGQodsq_DGhH5nPA3JbSuucEC5V7rCseO0QS69g2FfMBG9RFD8JTurik6BrfOaMw_BmiqUJGR8Aiclu-Gf9JifSxkogoYrHFXSFeKwqzI4lKEboIms4rhQK08suK14QB9xvpM8d_WYlIwuJEx-ErYE64Qc56YvPvVEwQpjNvYypmrf3fpXfi7KqP3iuLkanN6wRH1vcke0xIa_KGLvNaqH0KsvQYgb3zQ6vwoyoO6OpC_n-aoBf3ycYAJMdgpeMgwResHjwQVTJpSthBj0x01yuHxyo8sXHHodpJoKs0ezLspTuAYRZm-0O5C2vqU6vYIfL26MBkjHlQ3tTYafmc8ZOvmtifC8rHI3y7MS5e-fMWSbfGCnSWKFgQsv2qdDb70pRFYkHWVDZ4GYYncAotcds_xk4Qh9i4-RESGL0yB0ZZQWTrQUbnJkR1Mf-ZvIIGAiJNP47BynRe2u5t5rXVgWutAU2y_FRMUex_iQ3552kI09mbTyAtOebAXHCMtUKjO-DMbRRx0KrJopM45V6DeRrwCoaPtqcJQ3ntpjCLkBAhra21haKhqRVT3pP4lsa_KEcNh6Lutyh4TqM11Z9ToaKeD9xuI0ZPdf1MuJT3Vk_sC8DpDIhQwCwyuU8AO-ZQRZKzlAyhGnIhCgCKp3zJPJ8zdB7dKRvbj4BJgFjRka32Ne8oCOphj0Ny1nfwWaA8K6zlg=\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc471a66b887d1bccb8f0faf82e1ee\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Comparing fees and benefits**\\n\\nI'm thinking about how to answer the question regarding the Bluest monthly fee while ensuring I balance the information I give. It seems important to avoid overwhelming with too much detail. I plan to search for Bluest's monthly fee and then compare it to the benefits of Purple. It’ll help me provide a clearer and more effective response without going overboard.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Bluest Account monthly maintenance fee minimum balance opening deposit\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_RjKr8m5jwKE8eykMTbLfZyGS\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc471c38a087d1bb15c371c159797c\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_RjKr8m5jwKE8eykMTbLfZyGS\",\"output\":\"1. Bluest Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_002\\n   Score: 17.5836\\n   Content: ## Opening and maintaining your account\\n\\n### Opening requirement\\n- Deposit at least $75,000 to open your account.\\n\\n### Ongoing balance requirement\\n- Maintain a daily balance of $112,500 to keep all account benefits active.\\n\\n## Fees and limits\\n- Monthly maintenance fee if below the required daily balance: $75.00.\\n- Returned deposit fee (when a deposited check is returned unpaid): $0.00.\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $15,000.\\n\\n### Tips to stay in good standing\\n- Keep your daily balance at or above $112,500 to avoid the monthly maintenance fee of $75.00.\\n- Monitor large purchase activity to remain within the $15,000 daily card limit.\\n\\n2. Bronze Savings Account: Complete Guide\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_bronze_account_001\\n   Score: 17.4854\\n   Content: ## Key rates and fees\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Annual Percentage Yield (APY) | 2.0% |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $0.00 |\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $0 |\\n\\n## Opening your account\\n- Fund your account with at least $0.\\n- You can add funds immediately after the account is opened.\\n\\n## Earning interest\\n- You earn interest at an APY of 2.0% on your balance.\\n- Interest accrues automatically once your account is funded; no additional action is required.\\n\\n## Fees\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $0.00. If this value is $0, no monthly maintenance fee will be charged.\\n\\n## Practical tips\\n- Keep the account funded to consistently earn 2.0% APY.\\n- Review your statements to confirm posted interest and any fees.\\n\\n3. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 16.4336\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n4. Gold Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_003\\n   Score: 16.2067\\n   Content: ## Account requirements\\n- Opening deposit minimum: $5,000\\n- Ongoing minimum balance: $10,000\\n\\n## Transaction and usage limits\\n- Monthly withdrawal limit: 20\\n\\n## Interest characteristics\\n- Interest is compounded daily.\\n\\n## Alerts and rebates\\n- Large balance alert threshold: $50,000\\n- ATM fee rebate cap per month: $30\\n\\n## Summary table\\n| Specification | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Opening deposit minimum | $5,000 |\\n| Minimum balance | $10,000 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 20 |\\n| Interest compounding | daily |\\n| Large balance alert threshold | $50,000 |\\n| ATM fee rebate per month | $30 |\\n\\n5. Evergreen Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_evergreen_account_002\\n   Score: 15.8199\\n   Content: ## Fees and waivers\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $6.00\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your minimum daily balance is at least $500\\n\\n## Earnings on balances\\n- Annual Percentage Yield on your Evergreen Account balance: 0.05%\\n\\n## Statements\\n- Paper statements incur a monthly fee of $7.50\\n\\n## Transaction-related fees\\n- Returned deposit fee: $17.00\\n- Incoming domestic wire transfer fee: $12.50\\n\\n## Purchase and withdrawal limits\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $4,500\\n- Daily ATM withdrawal limit: $750\\n\\n## Keeping your account in good standing\\n- Maintain a minimum daily balance of $500 to avoid the monthly maintenance fee of $6.00\\n- Choose e‑statements to avoid the paper statement fee of $7.50\\n- Review deposited items promptly to minimize the chance of a returned deposit fee of $17.00\\n\\n6. How to avoid monthly fees\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_bronze_account_004\\n   Score: 14.4644\\n   Content: ## No monthly maintenance fee\\nGreat news! The Bronze Savings Account has no monthly maintenance fee. The monthly maintenance fee is $0.00 and the minimum balance requirement is 0. Unlike other savings accounts that require minimum balances to waive fees, the Bronze Account is completely fee-free for monthly maintenance. You will never be charged a monthly maintenance fee on this account, regardless of your balance. This makes it an ideal starter savings account for customers who want to begin saving without worrying about maintaining a minimum balance.\\n\\n7. Bluest Account exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_003\\n   Score: 13.8208\\n   Content: ## What you get with Bluest Account\\n\\n- Higher yield on your checking balance: 2.25% APY\\n- Complimentary domestic outgoing wires each month: 10\\n- Incoming domestic wires at no charge: $0.00\\n- Dedicated personal banker assigned: Yes\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates, up to: $50\\n- Complimentary personal check orders per year: 3\\n- Safe deposit box rental discount: 75.0%\\n- Stop payment requests at no charge: $0\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00\\n- Boosts on linked savings:\\n  - Silver Savings APY boost: 0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings APY boost: 0.7%\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Included |\\n|---|---|\\n| Checking APY | 2.25% |\\n| Free domestic outgoing wires (per month) | 10 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Dedicated personal banker | Yes |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly cap) | $50 |\\n| Complimentary check orders (per year) | 3 |\\n| Safe deposit box discount | 75.0% |\\n| Stop payment fee | $0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Silver Savings APY boost | 0.45% |\\n| Bronze Savings APY boost | 0.7% |\\n\\n## Referral rewards\\n\\nShare the Bluest experience and earn rewards:\\n- Referrer bonus: $75 per successful referral\\n- New member bonus: $50 for the person you refer\\n- Annual limit: 8 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n- Qualifying requirement: Referred person must deposit $2,000 within 90 days\\n- Eligibility: Referrers must have established their Rho-Bank checking relationship at least 60 days prior.\\n\\n## How to use your benefits\\n\\n### Complimentary wire transfers\\n- Send up to 10 domestic wire transfers per calendar month at no charge.\\n- Incoming domestic wires post with a $0.00 fee.\\n\\n### Dedicated personal banker\\n- A dedicated banker is assigned to your account (Yes). Use this single point of contact for complex transactions, expedited support, and account planning.\\n\\n### ATM fee rebates\\n- When you incur third-party ATM fees, you are rebated up to $50 per monthly statement cycle.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Withdraw from ATMs abroad with no Rho-Bank fee: $0.00. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n### Complimentary check orders\\n- Place up to 3 personal check orders each year at no cost.\\n\\n### Safe deposit box discount\\n- Receive a 75.0% discount on an eligible safe deposit box rental.\\n\\n### Stop payments\\n- Submit stop payment requests with a waived fee of $0.\\n\\n### Enhanced yields\\n- Earn 2.25% APY on your Bluest Account balance.\\n- Link eligible savings to activate boosts:\\n  - Silver Savings: +0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings: +0.7%\\n\\n8. Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_003\\n   Score: 13.8004\\n   Content: ## Key Features\\n- No overdraft fees on the account\\n- Waivable monthly maintenance fee: $20.00; waived when your minimum daily balance is at least $625\\n\\n## Optional Add-On\\n### Overdraft Protection Transfers\\n- If you opt in to overdraft protection, each transfer from a linked account to cover a negative balance incurs a $12.50 fee\\n- No overdraft fees are charged by the account itself\\n\\n## Fees\\n| Item | Amount | When it applies |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $20.00 | Charged monthly; waived with a minimum daily balance of $625 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $2.50 | Per month if you choose mailed paper statements |\\n| Returned deposit | $15.00 | Per deposited item returned unpaid |\\n| Incoming domestic wire transfer | $12.50 | Per incoming domestic wire |\\n| Stop payment on a check | $30 | Per stop payment request |\\n\\n## Linked Savings APY Boosts\\n- When linked to a Silver Plus Savings Account: +0.35% APY boost\\n- When linked to a Platinum Savings Account: +0.8% APY boost\\n\\n## Ways to Reduce or Avoid Fees\\n- Maintain a minimum daily balance of $625 to waive the $20.00 monthly maintenance fee\\n- Choose e-statements to avoid the $2.50 paper statement fee\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid out-of-network ATM fees\\n- Only enable overdraft protection if you need it, as each transfer incurs a $12.50 fee\\n\\n9. Platinum Plus Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_platinum_plus_account_001\\n   Score: 13.5334\\n   Content: ## Opening requirements\\n- Initial deposit to open: $50,000\\n\\n## Ongoing balance and activity\\n- Minimum balance to maintain the account: $100,000\\n- Monthly withdrawal limit: -1 (no cap on the number of withdrawals)\\n\\n## Interest compounding\\n- Interest is compounded: daily\\n\\n### Notes\\n- If your balance or activity changes, standard account terms apply based on these requirements.\\n\\n10. Gold Plus Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_plus_account_001\\n   Score: 13.3577\\n   Content: ## Key specifications\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Opening deposit minimum | $10,000 |\\n| Minimum balance to maintain | $25,000 |\\n| Interest compounding frequency | daily |\\n| Automatic investment sweep threshold | $50,000 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 25 withdrawals |\\n\\n## Requirements to open and maintain\\n\\n- Fund the account with at least $10,000 at opening.\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $25,000 to keep account benefits active.\\n- When your end-of-day available balance exceeds $50,000, excess funds may be moved automatically to your linked investment account according to sweep settings.\\n- Plan cash flows so you do not exceed 25 withdrawals in a month.\\n- Interest accrues daily; keeping funds on deposit helps you benefit from compounding.\\n\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEcmbgR_5CRRujI7d5RAk_TBaGG38MV8Y4tcxo0KEfLUh-Lde-9y8ehitpz8Gt6sXiQ2GWRzA9Jz3CYGnZ1lPsEa2f3u9igajAYpm4-hGMPMOWtor-IZPoSfBiCOn6LV1DtlS8WrCYhQWwacYBomLKjkkiDaoWGK6M4g4AtmN7QydT2AISq0PnhOFJgKKTMWnSu5IrRb-61R_7T5YOBYQ1YwvYq7-IiXDIeHsV0CWkjDirQ94I6BaCn4GJMw0NyPAMZNAx8__0msn35rqTb2TCu9WV8Pz4ELd8J6JJNOcwwTMJRa7BzJQr6StOMU6OJBZoJz0Hzo0qv1SxA_QAO-ORrkUtgtbKotsuYQ8kWFwW4Fr88odVqV6YLKG3vtI6pQxVM24wpGVJDl22t4zbclyVPJgpLneOsuJLLlVbz_9VhUEIMMbxzsSWlIECoFeA4n46iPfOg_tsY7JPYQlx2HNFfyef1j9JKSf8vn4364Vphk1OMEWBUhcRkRoRAYR1jTo8w8t8XNKjHYQaIfVtgWASLOj6-O_RRGycbXh_aQ0Zk2jU9Ww8zTs7vyNz9Nhcc6kj0FWXOugELwtrOvie3bt1v2FCgsWpBQSarom6H0u_9v_V3tAFsOe_bPWkHgQPzD32yJqzTf7i4IUzUNwjIQgmnNhqN-vY_yYC_kFnr4inEpw6SywNP9bh5i753-fU3_lfWo_tOw6QZoXQw4QPMGrPXeN19fHJxDFlK2btqznoup_VttOnyH23yQgwi9FqQnBFsptZpETejBSfQMkfTKNXjSAXLNAxS6GsTEAjHBGb2EQV6Lk4SyRsCyatjz_RLjbiWNHCxFktHLhcOFMgW2K6jXt9d_fyDMg-cSFSctw4FRpVL8dqn5IVbUnBbgFrraMb-3Vd9pjHRCkUJc_e6hSA7aYYHwZnCDDF1vfZfYVdfaYMYdE1OG499-B5bGouvbxVzW3xPCAz1STcyb3gxezU1evDa83zpIraMzMERgEIDAJRkj-Qm41hdbdcD805ECC78blmdkCazvX872hKuRgqQy6bjvHj1f7mjBoJsXqQW-rRyEFTdQKPgDBxay_7tZrkNdQpyb1ReIE8vJfUu5xOA28SWFdikeJWE7wOdmgffMvFAbg8-QcAuImIduhI--n1ONl7Fr0f2uW-yJu2vqw2RNHuy9o4jj8J27zhpiprQHeeEZiuwgWfpIAjwHzwlEMs1GfsiZNVeqC3nQynLXWg5I7jmtxiHUh75otSTPt-cr_3GtUhjPWrPOdpIXf3tHOGeBjoidHUDJ4NYTExirl4btEK