iMBfNG97nxn6iV3mW-p2dD8skiL3cPzpCvvOThSWt207GClDqTqxBU4nqCs9rOhd2C5EuxchM010rH_9tJRQ9XpUs940YnW1oKlosp3QSCo-p2mNiZLaNOBcI3mYUg1mGVE_9AgLPnFa-lO5c2ioL_fBj1PquwFzr8cgtk5tpKXzcEP4TdanYUXfvPY2F-aAzgodTtJxnhkuQmOk5cd7XPYhTBk77JOJY-J6g7L4UY6KwLMjiiyWa_o8i664JJFD6REA2vX-LMfe4gXfgdg44dhxCYpLTvrhrBRCxfLD3kJBA7AEFvED9220S_iyfLTsMYuIFdsQoiozi72u6qfiIDvV4DIN85Q8=\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc4735869487d1829e33d3a61592df\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Evaluating account options**\\n\\nI think we have enough basic information for now, but we need to balance caution with recommendations. It seems like the Purple Account is promising for travel, but there's a catch regarding fees. I want to ask if keeping at least $3,750 after withdrawals is comfortable for the user, as it might stretch their budget. Plus, I need to mention the currency conversion markup. I wonder why we're not checking other options, as Purple clearly fits if they can manage that amount daily.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"},{\"text\":\"**Assessing travel account options**\\n\\nI see the user mainly needs travel options without any constraints on fees for now. The Purple Account seems promising, but I’m hesitant to call it a final recommendation. I might suggest focusing on it with an important caveat to highlight. It's crucial to mention potential catches. The user doesn't want to compare too much, so I should simplify. Additionally, I’m concerned about unnecessary documents that may not be relevant anymore. It might be best to streamline my recommendations moving forward.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"logprobs\":[],\"text\":\"{\\\"message\\\":\\\"That helps. The Purple Account looks promising for your travel needs, but there’s an important balance requirement to check:\\\\n\\\\n• It reimburses ATM operator fees worldwide up to $30 per month; fees above that aren’t reimbursed.\\\\n• Rho charges $0 for foreign ATM withdrawals.\\\\n• Its $15 monthly maintenance fee is waived only if you maintain a minimum daily balance of $3,750.\\\\n• Currency conversion has a separate 0.5% markup above the interbank rate.\\\\n\\\\nSince your balance might dip to $3,000, I wouldn’t call it a clear fit yet. Would keeping at least $3,750 in the account—even after travel withdrawals—be comfortable, or would that stretch your budget?\\\"}\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc473dab5887d182caea5ddf967bfe\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"content\":\"Yeah, that would be a stretch. I *might* hover around that sometimes, but I can’t promise I’d stay above **$3,750 minimum daily** consistently—especially during trips when I’m pulling cash out a lot.\\n\\nAlso, while we’re on travel: I really hate **foreign transaction fees** when I use my card abroad. **Is there an account without those?**\\n\\nAnd one more thing: I sometimes get paid in **yen or euros**—it’d be amazing if I could **hold those currencies** instead of converting right away.\",\"role\":\"user\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"personal checking foreign transaction fees multi-currency wallet yen euros monthly fee\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_1tD2gOEPTKXb8Abf4779u0Qk\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc4743e90487d1b2e9a0cd01c2986d\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_1tD2gOEPTKXb8Abf4779u0Qk\",\"output\":\"1. Purple Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_001\\n   Score: 21.6787\\n   Content: ## Key numbers\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Foreign transaction fee | 0% |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Global ATM fee rebates | Up to $30 per month |\\n| Currency conversion markup | 0.5% above interbank rate |\\n| Multi-currency wallet | Yes |\\n| Supported wallet currencies | 30 |\\n| Complimentary airport lounge visits | 6 per year |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Mobile check deposit limit (daily) | $5,000 |\\n| Early direct deposit | 2 days early |\\n| APY boost with Platinum Plus Savings | +0.3% |\\n| APY boost with Gold Savings | +0.1% |\\n\\n## Travel-friendly highlights\\n\\n- No foreign transaction fees: 0%\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00 per withdrawal (third-party ATM operator fees may still apply)\\n- Global ATM fee rebates: up to $30 monthly worldwide\\n- Real-time currency conversion with a markup of 0.5% over the interbank rate\\n- Multi-currency wallet: Yes with up to 30 supported foreign currencies\\n- Complimentary airport lounge access: 6 visits per year\\n- Travel insurance benefits included\\n\\n## Everyday banking essentials\\n\\n- $0.00 fee for receiving domestic wire transfers\\n- Mobile check deposit up to $5,000 per day\\n- Get paid up to 2 days early with eligible direct deposits\\n- Earn boosted yields when linked:\\n  - Platinum Plus Savings: +0.3% APY\\n  - Gold Savings: +0.1% APY\\n\\n2. FAQ: Purple Account\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_011\\n   Score: 18.0109\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions\\n\\n- Q: What is the monthly maintenance fee?\\n  A: The monthly maintenance fee is $15.00.\\n\\n- Q: How can I get the monthly maintenance fee waived?\\n  A: Maintain a minimum daily balance of $3,750 to waive the fee.\\n\\n- Q: What are the foreign transaction fees?\\n  A: Foreign currency transactions are charged at 0%.\\n\\n- Q: How much travel insurance coverage is included?\\n  A: Your account includes up to $30,000 in coverage.\\n\\n- Q: How long does emergency card replacement take when I'm abroad?\\n  A: Replacements typically arrive within 2 days, depending on location and delivery conditions.\\n\\n- Q: Does this account include a multi-currency wallet?\\n  A: Multi-currency wallet support is Yes.\\n\\n- Q: Do I get complimentary airport lounge access?\\n  A: Yes. You receive up to 6 complimentary visits per year.\\n\\n- Q: What happens if a deposited check is returned unpaid?\\n  A: A returned deposit fee of $20.00 applies.\\n\\n- Q: Is there a fee to receive a domestic wire transfer?\\n  A: The incoming domestic wire fee is $0.00.\\n\\n- Q: Does the Purple Account have a referral program?\\n  A: Yes. When you refer someone to open a Purple Account, you earn $45 and the person you refer receives $35.\\n\\n- Q: What does someone need to do to qualify me for the referral bonus?\\n  A: The referred person must deposit at least $1,000 within 60 days of account opening.\\n\\n- Q: How many people can I refer per year?\\n  A: You can earn up to 6 referral bonuses per calendar year.\\n\\n- Q: How long do I need to have my account before I can refer others?\\n  A: Participation requires 45 days of checking account history with Rho-Bank.\\n\\n3. Multi-currency wallet features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_005\\n   Score: 15.5002\\n   Content: ## Availability\\n- Multi-currency wallet support for this account is Yes.\\n\\n## Holdings and supported currencies\\n- You can hold balances in up to 30 foreign currencies.\\n\\n## Conversions\\n- Currency exchanges execute at the interbank rate plus a markup of 0.5%.\\n\\n## Sending money with EveryonePay\\n- You can send funds using EveryonePay up to $5,000 per day. If your payment requires a conversion from a non‑USD balance, the exchange uses the markup noted above.\\n\\n4. Bluest Account exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_003\\n   Score: 14.1634\\n   Content: ## What you get with Bluest Account\\n\\n- Higher yield on your checking balance: 2.25% APY\\n- Complimentary domestic outgoing wires each month: 10\\n- Incoming domestic wires at no charge: $0.00\\n- Dedicated personal banker assigned: Yes\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates, up to: $50\\n- Complimentary personal check orders per year: 3\\n- Safe deposit box rental discount: 75.0%\\n- Stop payment requests at no charge: $0\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00\\n- Boosts on linked savings:\\n  - Silver Savings APY boost: 0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings APY boost: 0.7%\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Included |\\n|---|---|\\n| Checking APY | 2.25% |\\n| Free domestic outgoing wires (per month) | 10 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Dedicated personal banker | Yes |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly cap) | $50 |\\n| Complimentary check orders (per year) | 3 |\\n| Safe deposit box discount | 75.0% |\\n| Stop payment fee | $0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Silver Savings APY boost | 0.45% |\\n| Bronze Savings APY boost | 0.7% |\\n\\n## Referral rewards\\n\\nShare the Bluest experience and earn rewards:\\n- Referrer bonus: $75 per successful referral\\n- New member bonus: $50 for the person you refer\\n- Annual limit: 8 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n- Qualifying requirement: Referred person must deposit $2,000 within 90 days\\n- Eligibility: Referrers must have established their Rho-Bank checking relationship at least 60 days prior.\\n\\n## How to use your benefits\\n\\n### Complimentary wire transfers\\n- Send up to 10 domestic wire transfers per calendar month at no charge.\\n- Incoming domestic wires post with a $0.00 fee.\\n\\n### Dedicated personal banker\\n- A dedicated banker is assigned to your account (Yes). Use this single point of contact for complex transactions, expedited support, and account planning.\\n\\n### ATM fee rebates\\n- When you incur third-party ATM fees, you are rebated up to $50 per monthly statement cycle.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Withdraw from ATMs abroad with no Rho-Bank fee: $0.00. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n### Complimentary check orders\\n- Place up to 3 personal check orders each year at no cost.\\n\\n### Safe deposit box discount\\n- Receive a 75.0% discount on an eligible safe deposit box rental.\\n\\n### Stop payments\\n- Submit stop payment requests with a waived fee of $0.\\n\\n### Enhanced yields\\n- Earn 2.25% APY on your Bluest Account balance.\\n- Link eligible savings to activate boosts:\\n  - Silver Savings: +0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings: +0.7%\\n\\n5. Green Rewards Card: Apply for a Sustainable Business Credit Card\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_green_rewards_card_001\\n   Score: 13.2190\\n   Content: ## Eligibility\\n- Personal credit: You should meet a minimum FICO threshold of $690.\\n- Business credit: Established businesses are evaluated using a PAYDEX threshold of 42 in addition to personal credit history.\\n- Newer businesses: If you have limited business credit history, your personal profile can support your application.\\n\\n## Costs and Rates\\n| Cost or Rate | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Annual fee | $100.00 |\\n| Purchase APR | 19.99% |\\n| Foreign transaction fee | 1.0% |\\n\\n## Credit Limits\\n- Approved credit lines are assigned within a range from $14,000 to $75,000.\\n- Your limit is determined by factors such as revenue consistency, existing obligations, and overall credit profile.\\n\\n## Employee Cards\\n- You can issue up to 15 employee cards to team members.\\n- Set category-level controls, customize spending rules, and monitor transactions in real time.\\n\\n## What You Need to Apply\\n- Business legal name and structure, tax identification, and operating address\\n- Beneficial owner and authorized officer details\\n- Recent business financial information and estimated monthly card spend\\n- Agreement to a personal guaranty where applicable\\n\\n## How to Apply\\n- Complete the application in your online banking portal.\\n- Provide business and owner details, upload requested documents, and review disclosures.\\n- Submit your application for credit review. You will be notified when a decision is reached.\\n\\n## After You Submit\\n- If approved, activate your card and set controls for any employee cards.\\n- Review your assigned limit and applicable pricing, including $100.00, 19.99%, and 1.0%.\\n- Add the card to your digital wallet and configure expense categories for smoother reconciliation.\\n\\n6. EcoCard: Apply for a Sustainable Rewards Credit Card\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_ecocard_001\\n   Score: 12.9946\\n   Content: ## Eligibility and Requirements\\n- Minimum credit score required to apply: 0 (0 indicates no credit score requirement).\\n- You must provide standard identity and income information during the application.\\n\\n## How to Apply\\n1. Complete the online application with your personal and financial details.\\n2. Review the pricing and terms, including fees and interest rates listed below.\\n3. Submit the application and, if approved, activate your card upon receipt to begin using it.\\n\\n## Credit Limits Upon Approval\\n- Initial credit lines are determined at approval and typically range from $5,000 to $50,000.\\n- Credit line increases may be reviewed over time based on account history and usage.\\n\\n## Rates and Fees You Agree To\\n- Purchase APR on carried balances: 19.99%.\\n- Annual fee: $50.00.\\n- Foreign transaction fee (international purchases): 1.0%.\\n- Late payment fee (if you miss the due date): $32.50.\\n\\n## New-Customer Bonus at Sign-Up\\n- Spend $5,000 in eligible purchases within your first month to earn $2,000 sustainability points.\\n- Bonus points are awarded once the threshold is met and the qualifying period closes.\\n\\n## After You Apply\\n- You will receive a decision or a request for additional documentation.\\n- If approved, set up your online account and add your card to a digital wallet to start using it immediately after activation.\\n\\n7. Lime Green Account: ATM Access and Fee Rebates\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_007\\n   Score: 11.6489\\n   Content: ## ATM Access\\n\\n- You can use out-of-network ATMs for cash withdrawals. Each out-of-network ATM transaction is assessed a fee of $1.00.\\n- International (foreign) ATM withdrawals incur a fee equal to 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50 per withdrawal.\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM transaction fee (domestic) | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 1.5% of amount; minimum $2.50 |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebate cap (out-of-network usage) | Up to $25 per month |\\n\\n## ATM Fee Rebates\\n\\n- Your account provides monthly rebates of eligible fees from out-of-network ATM usage, up to $25 per month.\\n- Rebates are applied until the monthly cap is reached; any eligible fees above the cap are your responsibility.\\n- You do not need to take additional action for eligible rebates—fees and corresponding credits will appear as separate line items on your account activity once processed.\\n\\n### What counts toward the monthly cap\\n\\n- Fees assessed for out-of-network ATM usage that are charged to your account are counted toward the $25 monthly rebate limit.\\n\\n## How fees are calculated\\n\\n- Domestic out-of-network usage: Each withdrawal is charged $1.00.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals: The fee is 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50. If the percentage-based amount is less than $2.50, the $2.50 minimum applies.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, multiple withdrawals:\\n  - If you make several out-of-network withdrawals in a month, each is charged $1.00. Eligible out-of-network ATM fees will be rebated up to a total of $25 for that month.\\n\\n- Foreign withdrawal:\\n  - For a single international withdrawal, your fee is calculated at 1.5% of the withdrawn amount, subject to a $2.50 minimum. The applicable amount is charged at the time the transaction is processed.\\n\\n## Tips to reduce fees\\n\\n- Consolidate cash needs into fewer withdrawals to limit per-transaction charges of $1.00.\\n- Monitor your monthly total of out-of-network ATM fees to understand how close you are to the $25 rebate cap.\\n\\n8. World Blue: Free International ATM Access\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_009\\n   Score: 11.1014\\n   Content: ## What you pay at foreign ATMs\\n\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% (minimum $0.00)\\n- Foreign ATM fee rebates: Up to $100 per calendar month for fees charged by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals\\n\\nYou will not be charged a Rho fee for international ATM withdrawals. If the foreign ATM operator adds its own fee, we rebate those fees automatically up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n### Snapshot of foreign ATM costs\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 0% |\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee minimum | $0.00 |\\n| Maximum monthly rebate for foreign ATM fees | $100 |\\n\\n## Monthly rebate rules\\n\\n- Coverage: Rebates apply to fees assessed by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals.\\n- Cap: We rebate up to a total of $100 in a calendar month. Fees above this amount will not be reimbursed for that month.\\n- Posting: Rebates are issued automatically after the withdrawal and associated fee post to your account. No enrollment or receipt submission is required.\\n\\nTip: Keep your ATM receipt when a foreign ATM displays or charges a fee; it’s useful for reference if you need to follow up.\\n\\n## How to make a fee-free withdrawal abroad\\n\\n1. Use your card at an international ATM that accepts it.\\n2. When prompted, select a withdrawal from checking.\\n3. If asked about currency choice, choose to be charged in the local currency rather than having the ATM convert the amount.\\n4. Complete your withdrawal. If the ATM charges a fee, it will typically display it before you confirm.\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n- You withdraw the equivalent of $200 at a foreign ATM.\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% with a $0.00 minimum, so you pay $0 to Rho.\\n- The ATM operator charges a $5 fee. We automatically rebate $5, counting toward your $100 monthly cap.\\n\\n9. Why am I being charged a fee on my Lime Green Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_008\\n   Score: 10.8520\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you may see a fee\\n\\nYou may see one or more of the following fees on your Lime Green Account:\\n\\n- Monthly maintenance fee if your balance does not meet the waiver threshold\\n- Fees for sending domestic or international wire transfers\\n- Fees for using non‑Rho ATMs, including percentage‑based fees for foreign ATM withdrawals\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Fee type | When it’s charged | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | Your balance does not meet the waiver threshold | $25.00 |\\n| Domestic wire transfer | You send a domestic wire | $10.00 |\\n| International wire transfer | You send an international wire to a foreign bank | $25.00 |\\n| Non‑Rho ATM (U.S.) | You withdraw cash at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | You withdraw cash at an international ATM | 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $2.50 |\\n\\n## Monthly maintenance fee\\n\\n- You are charged $25.00 when your account balance does not meet $15,000.\\n- To avoid this fee, maintain a balance at or above $15,000.\\n\\n## Wire transfer fees\\n\\n- Domestic wires: Each outgoing domestic wire you send incurs a fee of $10.00.\\n- International wires: Each outgoing international wire to a foreign bank incurs a fee of $25.00.\\n\\n## ATM‑related fees\\n\\n- Non‑Rho ATMs in the U.S.: You are charged $1.00 per withdrawal when using a non‑Rho ATM.\\n- Foreign (international) ATMs: You are charged 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum fee of $2.50.\\n  - How to estimate: Multiply your withdrawal amount by 1.5% and compare the result to $2.50. The higher number is the fee.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Review your transaction history for a separate fee line item (for example, a description referencing maintenance, wire, or ATM).\\n2. Match the amount to one of the following:\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $10.00\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $1.00\\n   - For foreign ATM withdrawals, the greater of:\\n     - 1.5% of your withdrawal amount, or\\n     - $2.50\\n\\n## Ways to avoid or reduce fees\\n\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $15,000 to waive $25.00.\\n- Use Rho‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.\\n- Plan international cash needs to minimize the number of foreign ATM withdrawals subject to 1.5% (minimum $2.50).\\n\\n## If you believe a fee is incorrect\\n\\n- Gather details (date, amount, and description of the fee; related transaction, if any).\\n- Contact support with these details so we can review and correct any errors promptly.\\n\\n10. No foreign transaction fees explained\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_003\\n   Score: 10.7733\\n   Content: ## What this means for you\\n- Purchases and withdrawals in a non‑USD currency do not incur a foreign transaction fee. Your rate is 0% for foreign currency transactions.\\n\\n## Where this applies\\n- Card purchases processed in a foreign currency\\n- Online transactions charged in a foreign currency\\n- International ATM withdrawals, as they relate to the foreign transaction fee\\n\\n## What is not included\\n- Local ATM operator surcharges and network fees are separate from the foreign transaction fee policy.\\n- Check-related services are not part of foreign transaction fees. For example, placing a stop payment carries a fee of $25.\\n\\n### Tips\\n- If a merchant offers to charge you in USD rather than the local currency, that is a separate service and may have its own costs set by the merchant or processor.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEdIo4A_QLQGh_mTJ5JMYQv7WLJQfMAy5nYonh09wloC7w5xYgfWuyEg_0ncce8JzFhJ1EWdpglKyHQHnYQKCKSgyPd_7SyoBJDNEMbRgp1v3B_ZQ0rHMHVsyVPP8SgKlnBreRS1XMp_CettNv6VEG_-fXvysGD9yc_M5P8edocVDvZVc86PQjqIZP7CHF8y_MHxBjTpYchQzzQMLUrV1O6mjJkQcbsMWZDbzE9rIyLVz6-dw4HNoTVwrFup7akgdftsWswARvC9rxc0hnzDD5FbPaeTnIZh5xEDF0Bzsno0xgGnT8vyWGhTcjpIeKeU2gXsiFxNQZn-kWOTiqCUTLJoaTFNeKlMy7AzORuo2Xp1-IfA0sR-tMsHsq84Xb8na1z04j57IHxnsglL4EGCeZRLswxKOKw8CvlgC8qXjNTe6oRXVWk71J54qtzVLeL7dHLeLJMXVQzFZ8NLrd6PlqPyXla1Wu5i7VSu4sCTh6fBVbTETBVWEvDtEJY1Dw3lrVidDtQRMZF4dyrfQO4Mc2CAybPTD3YxjbLN-ooEOek3eG87tG41EbFTp6LhAbGjN3Ycff3xzkuengGttcZ8V6QFTT64QYalaaBSIuwTQd1eS-rlwLkY7m46Hb27wlIYqKvu1v9D2MFk9zeMeeK-j59J5cCpD25dkZecs1kd5YcnpXB3_UFx3F8t5HrAj3y4H8TLt_kHwRqHVqPwpEI86p2TLYlgWAlhG4QzJKFLaY9iRIdrLlt20v4ltQY5pu8HJxO4qFKIQvL7b6hQtYxvEkRF1xL3cEskYQ8XN7y8X5LgE4rIR1oIBB8EanrD6ZNRjBCzLtJt5Q40mX5KF6xPWBL-YeOD1VWP6k2Gt6ax4pD42oAzo26YizCspqlFBc_50QLROw_rgh_Lq6XMalF9Yy96ZghWPbwqy2QJSc5TxN7mCxRSv0pmpxilTfyJwujRE5DDS-18sa-UkvbN7A-5B45qiSH9MGgxge8zMpU_061NZ8_hMGQo0Zl3kgJw5pwDRYkbtSp7F-38qwz42hCdDtaawro5yRNcpxuAJ5p7f4BO1xvIiDE40Bt0_SzTuroIj2D0NyeSl8uQDhFkVMXjiqJO4x1BwlJQ78suBkQbZk6vHorIFjsoJc10IPIWFZk-_E_l5XhaX-sEG-B-2_rvEkMQkTEDg5u5NHpYZaVnOy2RNdXERT7Di1LZry4X0mMA66YcrHfeNEk4t0-as1tSbIgFqGpFFuGngcxf0sNuAoqQddhGWROtbJrAq75gl6MqE2XoUsiloUp19wMZYwHFLhKinTvjUW4ftudTIve6lzRLQAbAYT974YQ8nFyA0DPooePqTujmXp5I-SdCO_MIvGatEA==\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47467bf487d190833b24e6e299a4\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"personal checking multi-currency wallet supported currencies JPY EUR yen euros\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_eHi61n82zEWpO3ovjjQ4Z25W\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47487a5087d19855b13289f200d3\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"personal checking no foreign transaction fee low balance monthly maintenance fee ATM rebates\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_apPc2g8kOXhtCRYI07Dz7YL9\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47487a6487d194c41e2ed71eeb2f\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_eHi61n82zEWpO3ovjjQ4Z25W\",\"output\":\"1. Multi-currency wallet features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_005\\n   Score: 23.3344\\n   Content: ## Availability\\n- Multi-currency wallet support for this account is Yes.\\n\\n## Holdings and supported currencies\\n- You can hold balances in up to 30 foreign currencies.\\n\\n## Conversions\\n- Currency exchanges execute at the interbank rate plus a markup of 0.5%.\\n\\n## Sending money with EveryonePay\\n- You can send funds using EveryonePay up to $5,000 per day. If your payment requires a conversion from a non‑USD balance, the exchange uses the markup noted above.\\n\\n2. Purple Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_001\\n   Score: 22.5209\\n   Content: ## Key numbers\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Foreign transaction fee | 0% |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Global ATM fee rebates | Up to $30 per month |\\n| Currency conversion markup | 0.5% above interbank rate |\\n| Multi-currency wallet | Yes |\\n| Supported wallet currencies | 30 |\\n| Complimentary airport lounge visits | 6 per year |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Mobile check deposit limit (daily) | $5,000 |\\n| Early direct deposit | 2 days early |\\n| APY boost with Platinum Plus Savings | +0.3% |\\n| APY boost with Gold Savings | +0.1% |\\n\\n## Travel-friendly highlights\\n\\n- No foreign transaction fees: 0%\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00 per withdrawal (third-party ATM operator fees may still apply)\\n- Global ATM fee rebates: up to $30 monthly worldwide\\n- Real-time currency conversion with a markup of 0.5% over the interbank rate\\n- Multi-currency wallet: Yes with up to 30 supported foreign currencies\\n- Complimentary airport lounge access: 6 visits per year\\n- Travel insurance benefits included\\n\\n## Everyday banking essentials\\n\\n- $0.00 fee for receiving domestic wire transfers\\n- Mobile check deposit up to $5,000 per day\\n- Get paid up to 2 days early with eligible direct deposits\\n- Earn boosted yields when linked:\\n  - Platinum Plus Savings: +0.3% APY\\n  - Gold Savings: +0.1% APY\\n\\n3. Navigating Currency Conversions on World Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_003\\n   Score: 15.6927\\n   Content: ## Before you convert\\n- Ensure your requested conversion amount meets the minimum of $100\\n- Confirm the currencies involved are among the 35 supported options\\n\\n## How quotes work\\n- Conversion quotes include a low-margin markup of 1.5% over the prevailing wholesale rate\\n- Your final trade ticket will display the effective rate and the converted amount before you submit\\n\\n## Converting funds step by step\\n- Choose the source wallet and target currency\\n- Enter an amount that is at least $100\\n- Review the quote, which reflects the markup of 1.5%\\n- Submit the conversion and note the confirmation details for reconciliation\\n\\n## Best practices\\n- Time conversions to your cash flow so you are not forced to convert during periods of reduced liquidity\\n- If you have multiple small needs, consider consolidating into fewer conversions so each meets $100\\n- Record the conversion reference alongside related invoices or payouts to streamline audits\\n\\n## Conversion parameters\\n\\n| Parameter | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| FX markup | 1.5% |\\n| Minimum conversion amount | $100 |\\n| Currencies supported | 35 |\\n\\n\\n4. Getting Started with World Blue International Checking\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_001\\n   Score: 15.6836\\n   Content: ## Quick checklist before you begin\\n- Confirm you can maintain at least $10,000 across currencies to keep the account in good standing\\n- Be aware of the monthly maintenance fee of $50.00\\n- Decide which of the up to 35 supported currencies you plan to hold and transact in\\n- Verify that your intended counterparties and destinations are within the $140 supported regions for sending and receiving payments\\n\\n## Initial setup steps\\n- Fund your account so you can meet ongoing balance needs\\n- Add the currency wallets you will use for operations and settlements\\n- Set a primary operating currency for reporting and reconciliation\\n- Configure payee profiles for your frequent counterparties within the supported regions\\n- Review user access and prepare to assign permissions based on roles and responsibilities\\n\\n## Key thresholds and limits at a glance\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $50.00 |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $10,000 |\\n| Supported currencies | 35 |\\n| Supported regions for payments | $140 |\\n\\n## First-week best practices\\n- Keep an operating buffer above $10,000 to avoid service interruptions\\n- Start with a small set of currency wallets and expand as your payment flows stabilize\\n- Validate a test payment to a known counterparty in one of the supported regions and confirm posting and reconciliation\\n- Set alerts and reports aligned to your treasury cadence to monitor balances and activity\\n\\n## Referring other businesses to World Blue\\n\\nAs a Rho-Bank checking account holder, you can refer other businesses to World Blue. To be eligible to refer:\\n- You must have maintained checking account status with Rho-Bank for at least 90 days\\n\\nFor a referral to qualify:\\n- The referred business must open a World Blue account\\n- They must deposit at least $25,000 within 90 days of account opening\\n\\n\\n5. Crypto-Cash Back: Supported Cryptocurrencies and Wallets\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_crypto-cash_back_003\\n   Score: 13.0958\\n   Content: ## Availability Overview\\n- Crypto redemptions on this program: Yes.\\n- Number of cryptocurrencies supported for redemption: up to 12.\\n\\n## Supported Wallet Connections\\n- Direct wallet integration supported: Yes.\\n- If direct integration is not supported, you can use manual wallet address entry.\\n\\n## Selecting a Cryptocurrency\\n- You can choose from a curated list of up to 12 cryptocurrencies during redemption.\\n- The list may change over time based on liquidity, security, and network considerations.\\n\\n## Wallet Compatibility Guidance\\n- If Yes is True:\\n  - Link your wallet directly within the app and select it at checkout during redemption.\\n- If Yes is False:\\n  - Paste your compatible public wallet address for the selected asset during redemption and verify it carefully.\\n\\n## Best Practices\\n- Confirm that your wallet supports the network of the selected cryptocurrency.\\n- Use a new address only after validating it with a small test transfer in your external wallet, when possible.\\n\\n6. Crypto-Cash Back: Linking Your Crypto Wallet to Your Account\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_crypto-cash_back_004\\n   Score: 12.8753\\n   Content: ## Determine Your Connection Method\\n- Direct wallet integration availability: Yes.\\n\\n## If Direct Integration Is Supported\\n1. Go to Settings > Crypto Wallets in your app.\\n2. Choose Add Wallet and select your wallet provider.\\n3. Authenticate with your wallet provider and approve permissions.\\n4. Set this wallet as your default destination for crypto redemptions.\\n5. Complete a verification step if prompted (e.g., signing a message).\\n\\n## If Direct Integration Is Not Supported\\n1. Navigate to Rewards > Redeem to Crypto.\\n2. Select your cryptocurrency and choose Manual Address.\\n3. Paste your public wallet address and, if applicable, the required memo/tag.\\n4. Verify the address format and network before saving.\\n5. Save the address for future redemptions and consider labeling it for clarity.\\n\\n## Verification Tips\\n- Always verify the network (e.g., native chain vs. tokenized variants) matches your wallet’s expected format.\\n- Test with a small redemption after setup to ensure proper delivery before sending larger amounts.\\n\\n7. FAQ: Purple Account\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_011\\n   Score: 10.9891\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions\\n\\n- Q: What is the monthly maintenance fee?\\n  A: The monthly maintenance fee is $15.00.\\n\\n- Q: How can I get the monthly maintenance fee waived?\\n  A: Maintain a minimum daily balance of $3,750 to waive the fee.\\n\\n- Q: What are the foreign transaction fees?\\n  A: Foreign currency transactions are charged at 0%.\\n\\n- Q: How much travel insurance coverage is included?\\n  A: Your account includes up to $30,000 in coverage.\\n\\n- Q: How long does emergency card replacement take when I'm abroad?\\n  A: Replacements typically arrive within 2 days, depending on location and delivery conditions.\\n\\n- Q: Does this account include a multi-currency wallet?\\n  A: Multi-currency wallet support is Yes.\\n\\n- Q: Do I get complimentary airport lounge access?\\n  A: Yes. You receive up to 6 complimentary visits per year.\\n\\n- Q: What happens if a deposited check is returned unpaid?\\n  A: A returned deposit fee of $20.00 applies.\\n\\n- Q: Is there a fee to receive a domestic wire transfer?\\n  A: The incoming domestic wire fee is $0.00.\\n\\n- Q: Does the Purple Account have a referral program?\\n  A: Yes. When you refer someone to open a Purple Account, you earn $45 and the person you refer receives $35.\\n\\n- Q: What does someone need to do to qualify me for the referral bonus?\\n  A: The referred person must deposit at least $1,000 within 60 days of account opening.\\n\\n- Q: How many people can I refer per year?\\n  A: You can earn up to 6 referral bonuses per calendar year.\\n\\n- Q: How long do I need to have my account before I can refer others?\\n  A: Participation requires 45 days of checking account history with Rho-Bank.\\n\\n8. Purple Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_002\\n   Score: 10.8427\\n   Content: ## Fees and thresholds\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $15.00\\n- Minimum daily balance to waive the monthly maintenance fee: $3,750\\n- Returned deposit fee: $20.00 per item returned unpaid\\n- Incoming domestic wire transfer fee: $0.00\\n\\n## Usage limits\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $10,000\\n- Supported foreign currencies that can be held in the wallet: 30\\n\\n### Important\\n- Maintain the minimum daily balance listed to avoid the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Card purchase activity above the daily limit will be declined until the next day.\\n\\n9. Internal: Opening Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_001\\n   Score: 10.0790\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a personal checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer is at least 18 years old.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 4 personal checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no checking accounts closed for cause in the past 6 months.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Personal checking account_class options must use the full official name ending with 'Account' (e.g., 'Blue Account', 'Green Account (checking)').\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n10. Internal: Opening Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_002\\n   Score: 8.9545\\n   Content: ## Scope and Focus\\n\\nProcedure for opening personal savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one active Rho-Bank checking account, 3) Cannot have more than 5 personal savings accounts, 4) Must not have any accounts in collections or with negative balances, 5) Must have held their checking account for at least 14 days. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer, 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account (note: account_class must use the full official name ending with 'Account', e.g., 'Silver Plus Account', 'Gold Account'), 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements (Internal Checklist)\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified in our systems.\\n- Customer has at least one active Rho-Bank checking account.\\n- Customer currently holds fewer than 5 personal savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts in collections and no negative balances.\\n- The customer’s checking account tenure is at least 14 days.\\n\\nDo not proceed if any item above is not met.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify identity\\n- Authenticate the customer and confirm identity verification status on file.\\n\\n2) Check eligibility\\n- Confirm an active checking account exists and meets the 14-day tenure requirement.\\n- Count existing personal savings accounts; ensure the customer is below the 5 limit.\\n- Review account status; there must be no collections activity and no negative balances.\\n\\n3) Confirm account selection\\n- Discuss available personal savings account options with the customer.\\n- Capture the exact account_class string. It must be the full official name ending with “Account” (for example, “Silver Plus Account”, “Gold Account”).\\n\\n4) Open the savings account (agent action)\\n- Use the open_bank_account_4821 tool with account_type set to 'savings' and the confirmed account_class.\\n\\n5) Arrange opening deposit\\n- Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now.\\n  - If yes: use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount from the customer’s checking account to the newly opened savings account.\\n  - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n6) Confirm completion\\n- Provide the new account details and confirm the funding status or the funding deadline.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Usage (Internal Only)\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not ask the customer to call tools or provide tool parameters.\\n\\n- Tool: open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n  - When to call: After steps 1–3, once eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected an account_class.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - user_id: the authenticated customer’s user identifier.\\n    - account_type: 'savings' for personal savings accounts.\\n    - account_class: the full official account name ending with 'Account' exactly as confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Creates a new personal savings account for the customer.\\n\\n- Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n  - When to call: In step 5, only if the customer authorizes an immediate transfer for the opening deposit.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - source_account_id: the customer's Rho-Bank checking account to be debited.\\n    - destination_account_id: the newly opened personal savings account to be credited.\\n    - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Moves funds from checking to savings to complete the opening deposit.\\n\\n## Decision Points and Handling\\n\\n- Exceeds savings account limit: If the customer already has 5 personal savings accounts, do not open a new one. Inform the customer they have reached the maximum.\\n- Insufficient checking tenure: If the checking account has been open fewer than 14 days, advise the customer when they will become eligible.\\n- Collections or negative balances: Resolve these issues first; do not proceed until all accounts are in good standing.\\n- Customer defers funding: Clearly communicate the 30-day funding window and the consequence of closure if unfunded. Document the acknowledgment in the interaction notes.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_apPc2g8kOXhtCRYI07Dz7YL9\",\"output\":\"1. Bluest Account exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_003\\n   Score: 24.0614\\n   Content: ## What you get with Bluest Account\\n\\n- Higher yield on your checking balance: 2.25% APY\\n- Complimentary domestic outgoing wires each month: 10\\n- Incoming domestic wires at no charge: $0.00\\n- Dedicated personal banker assigned: Yes\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates, up to: $50\\n- Complimentary personal check orders per year: 3\\n- Safe deposit box rental discount: 75.0%\\n- Stop payment requests at no charge: $0\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00\\n- Boosts on linked savings:\\n  - Silver Savings APY boost: 0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings APY boost: 0.7%\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Included |\\n|---|---|\\n| Checking APY | 2.25% |\\n| Free domestic outgoing wires (per month) | 10 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Dedicated personal banker | Yes |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly cap) | $50 |\\n| Complimentary check orders (per year) | 3 |\\n| Safe deposit box discount | 75.0% |\\n| Stop payment fee | $0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Silver Savings APY boost | 0.45% |\\n| Bronze Savings APY boost | 0.7% |\\n\\n## Referral rewards\\n\\nShare the Bluest experience and earn rewards:\\n- Referrer bonus: $75 per successful referral\\n- New member bonus: $50 for the person you refer\\n- Annual limit: 8 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n- Qualifying requirement: Referred person must deposit $2,000 within 90 days\\n- Eligibility: Referrers must have established their Rho-Bank checking relationship at least 60 days prior.\\n\\n## How to use your benefits\\n\\n### Complimentary wire transfers\\n- Send up to 10 domestic wire transfers per calendar month at no charge.\\n- Incoming domestic wires post with a $0.00 fee.\\n\\n### Dedicated personal banker\\n- A dedicated banker is assigned to your account (Yes). Use this single point of contact for complex transactions, expedited support, and account planning.\\n\\n### ATM fee rebates\\n- When you incur third-party ATM fees, you are rebated up to $50 per monthly statement cycle.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Withdraw from ATMs abroad with no Rho-Bank fee: $0.00. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n### Complimentary check orders\\n- Place up to 3 personal check orders each year at no cost.\\n\\n### Safe deposit box discount\\n- Receive a 75.0% discount on an eligible safe deposit box rental.\\n\\n### Stop payments\\n- Submit stop payment requests with a waived fee of $0.\\n\\n### Enhanced yields\\n- Earn 2.25% APY on your Bluest Account balance.\\n- Link eligible savings to activate boosts:\\n  - Silver Savings: +0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings: +0.7%\\n\\n2. Beige Account: Enterprise ATM Benefits\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_011\\n   Score: 20.8707\\n   Content: ## What’s included with Enterprise ATM access\\n\\n- No Rho out-of-network ATM fee: You pay $0.00 per out-of-network ATM transaction.\\n- Monthly rebates for ATM operator surcharges: Receive up to $50 in rebates each month for fees charged by out-of-network ATM operators.\\n- International ATM withdrawals: A Rho fee of 1% of the withdrawal amount applies at foreign ATMs, with a minimum charge of $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n\\n## Fee summary\\n\\n| Scenario | Rho fee | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM usage (Rho fee) | $0.00 per transaction | ATM operators may charge their own surcharges. |\\n| Rebates for out-of-network ATM operator surcharges | Up to $50 per month | Rebates are capped monthly; once reached, additional surcharges are your responsibility. |\\n| Foreign (international) ATM withdrawal | 1% of withdrawal amount, minimum $2.00 | This Rho fee may apply in addition to any ATM operator surcharge. |\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, out-of-network ATM\\n  - You withdraw $200 and the ATM operator charges a $3 surcharge.\\n  - Rho out-of-network fee: $0.00.\\n  - The $3 operator surcharge counts toward your monthly rebate limit of $50.\\n\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawal\\n  - You withdraw $400 abroad.\\n  - Rho foreign ATM fee: 1% of $400 = $4.00 (meets the $2.00 minimum).\\n  - If the ATM operator adds its own surcharge, it may count toward your monthly rebate limit of $50 for out-of-network usage.\\n\\n## How to maximize your benefits\\n\\n- Consolidate cash needs into fewer withdrawals to reduce multiple operator surcharges.\\n- Track your cumulative ATM operator-fee rebates against the $50 monthly cap.\\n- When traveling internationally, factor in the 1% (minimum $2.00) fee on each withdrawal.\\n\\n## FAQs\\n\\n- Is there a Rho fee for using an out-of-network ATM?\\n  - No. The Rho fee is $0.00 per transaction. ATM operators may still charge their own surcharges.\\n\\n- What happens after I reach the monthly rebate cap?\\n  - Once you reach $50 in rebated out-of-network ATM surcharges for the month, additional surcharges are not rebated.\\n\\n- Do foreign ATM withdrawals have a separate fee?\\n  - Yes. Each foreign ATM withdrawal incurs a Rho fee of 1% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n\\n3. True Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_011\\n   Score: 19.6452\\n   Content: ## Fees at a glance\\n\\n| Transaction type | Where it applies | Fee |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal | Domestic (U.S.) non-Rho ATMs | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM cash withdrawal | International ATMs | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 per withdrawal |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebates (cap) | Out-of-network ATM usage | Up to $30 per month |\\n\\nNote: ATM owners may assess their own surcharges on out-of-network transactions. Those surcharges are separate from Rho’s fees.\\n\\n## Domestic out-of-network ATM usage (U.S.)\\n\\n- When you use a non-Rho ATM domestically, you are charged $1.00 per transaction.\\n- The ATM owner may also charge a separate surcharge at the terminal; you can accept or cancel the transaction after the surcharge is disclosed.\\n\\nExample:\\n- If you complete 5 out-of-network withdrawals in a month, Rho’s fees would total 5 × $1.00. Any ATM owner surcharges would be in addition to this amount.\\n\\n## International ATM withdrawals\\n\\n- For cash withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs, the fee is 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00 per withdrawal.\\n- The percentage is applied to each withdrawal; if the calculated amount is below $3.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- $100 withdrawal: 2% = $2.00, which is below the $3.00 minimum, so the fee is $3.00.\\n- $200 withdrawal: 2% = $4.00, so the fee is $4.00.\\n\\n## Monthly ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You can receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network ATM usage.\\n- The cap is applied on a monthly basis; once total eligible ATM fees reach $30 for the month, no additional ATM fee rebates are provided for that month.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $12, up to $12 may be rebated (within the $30 cap).\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $36, the maximum rebate is $30.\\n\\n## Tips to manage costs\\n\\n- Prefer Rho ATMs to avoid the $1.00 out-of-network fee.\\n- Abroad, consider fewer, larger withdrawals to reduce the impact of the $3.00 per-withdrawal minimum.\\n- Track your monthly ATM fees so you know when you are approaching the $30 cap.\\n\\n4. World Blue: Free International ATM Access\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_009\\n   Score: 19.2302\\n   Content: ## What you pay at foreign ATMs\\n\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% (minimum $0.00)\\n- Foreign ATM fee rebates: Up to $100 per calendar month for fees charged by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals\\n\\nYou will not be charged a Rho fee for international ATM withdrawals. If the foreign ATM operator adds its own fee, we rebate those fees automatically up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n### Snapshot of foreign ATM costs\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 0% |\\n| Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee minimum | $0.00 |\\n| Maximum monthly rebate for foreign ATM fees | $100 |\\n\\n## Monthly rebate rules\\n\\n- Coverage: Rebates apply to fees assessed by foreign ATM operators on cash withdrawals.\\n- Cap: We rebate up to a total of $100 in a calendar month. Fees above this amount will not be reimbursed for that month.\\n- Posting: Rebates are issued automatically after the withdrawal and associated fee post to your account. No enrollment or receipt submission is required.\\n\\nTip: Keep your ATM receipt when a foreign ATM displays or charges a fee; it’s useful for reference if you need to follow up.\\n\\n## How to make a fee-free withdrawal abroad\\n\\n1. Use your card at an international ATM that accepts it.\\n2. When prompted, select a withdrawal from checking.\\n3. If asked about currency choice, choose to be charged in the local currency rather than having the ATM convert the amount.\\n4. Complete your withdrawal. If the ATM charges a fee, it will typically display it before you confirm.\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n- You withdraw the equivalent of $200 at a foreign ATM.\\n- Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 0% with a $0.00 minimum, so you pay $0 to Rho.\\n- The ATM operator charges a $5 fee. We automatically rebate $5, counting toward your $100 monthly cap.\\n\\n5. Lime Green Account: ATM Access and Fee Rebates\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_007\\n   Score: 18.9568\\n   Content: ## ATM Access\\n\\n- You can use out-of-network ATMs for cash withdrawals. Each out-of-network ATM transaction is assessed a fee of $1.00.\\n- International (foreign) ATM withdrawals incur a fee equal to 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50 per withdrawal.\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM transaction fee (domestic) | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 1.5% of amount; minimum $2.50 |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebate cap (out-of-network usage) | Up to $25 per month |\\n\\n## ATM Fee Rebates\\n\\n- Your account provides monthly rebates of eligible fees from out-of-network ATM usage, up to $25 per month.\\n- Rebates are applied until the monthly cap is reached; any eligible fees above the cap are your responsibility.\\n- You do not need to take additional action for eligible rebates—fees and corresponding credits will appear as separate line items on your account activity once processed.\\n\\n### What counts toward the monthly cap\\n\\n- Fees assessed for out-of-network ATM usage that are charged to your account are counted toward the $25 monthly rebate limit.\\n\\n## How fees are calculated\\n\\n- Domestic out-of-network usage: Each withdrawal is charged $1.00.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals: The fee is 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.50. If the percentage-based amount is less than $2.50, the $2.50 minimum applies.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, multiple withdrawals:\\n  - If you make several out-of-network withdrawals in a month, each is charged $1.00. Eligible out-of-network ATM fees will be rebated up to a total of $25 for that month.\\n\\n- Foreign withdrawal:\\n  - For a single international withdrawal, your fee is calculated at 1.5% of the withdrawn amount, subject to a $2.50 minimum. The applicable amount is charged at the time the transaction is processed.\\n\\n## Tips to reduce fees\\n\\n- Consolidate cash needs into fewer withdrawals to limit per-transaction charges of $1.00.\\n- Monitor your monthly total of out-of-network ATM fees to understand how close you are to the $25 rebate cap.\\n\\n6. Purple Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_001\\n   Score: 18.7850\\n   Content: ## Key numbers\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Foreign transaction fee | 0% |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Global ATM fee rebates | Up to $30 per month |\\n| Currency conversion markup | 0.5% above interbank rate |\\n| Multi-currency wallet | Yes |\\n| Supported wallet currencies | 30 |\\n| Complimentary airport lounge visits | 6 per year |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Mobile check deposit limit (daily) | $5,000 |\\n| Early direct deposit | 2 days early |\\n| APY boost with Platinum Plus Savings | +0.3% |\\n| APY boost with Gold Savings | +0.1% |\\n\\n## Travel-friendly highlights\\n\\n- No foreign transaction fees: 0%\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00 per withdrawal (third-party ATM operator fees may still apply)\\n- Global ATM fee rebates: up to $30 monthly worldwide\\n- Real-time currency conversion with a markup of 0.5% over the interbank rate\\n- Multi-currency wallet: Yes with up to 30 supported foreign currencies\\n- Complimentary airport lounge access: 6 visits per year\\n- Travel insurance benefits included\\n\\n## Everyday banking essentials\\n\\n- $0.00 fee for receiving domestic wire transfers\\n- Mobile check deposit up to $5,000 per day\\n- Get paid up to 2 days early with eligible direct deposits\\n- Earn boosted yields when linked:\\n  - Platinum Plus Savings: +0.3% APY\\n  - Gold Savings: +0.1% APY\\n\\n7. Why am I being charged a fee on my True Blue Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_010\\n   Score: 18.4113\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you’re seeing a fee\\n\\nBelow are the most common fee types that can appear on a True Blue account and why they’re charged.\\n\\n| Fee type | When you’ll see it | Amount posted |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your qualifying balance did not meet the waiver threshold for the applicable evaluation period | $75.00 (waived when balance requirement of $50,000 is met) |\\n| Domestic Wire Transfer Fee | You sent a domestic wire from your account | $5.00 per outbound domestic wire |\\n| Out-of-Network ATM Fee | You completed a transaction at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at an international (non‑U.S.) ATM | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 |\\n\\n### Example for foreign ATM fee\\n- If you withdraw $200 at a foreign ATM, the fee is 2% of $200 ($4). Because $4 exceeds the minimum $3.00, $4 would post.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Check your latest statement or transaction history for the fee line item and posted amount.  \\n2. Match the posted amount to the fees above:\\n   - $75.00 typically indicates the Monthly Maintenance Fee.\\n   - $5.00 typically indicates a Domestic Wire Transfer Fee.\\n   - $1.00 typically indicates an Out-of-Network ATM Fee.\\n   - A calculated amount equal to 2% of your ATM withdrawal (or $3.00, whichever is higher) indicates a Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee.\\n3. For the Monthly Maintenance Fee, compare your balance during the billing period to the waiver threshold of $50,000.\\n\\n## How to reduce or avoid future fees\\n\\n- Maintain at least $50,000 to have the $75.00 waived.  \\n- Use Rho in‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.  \\n- When abroad, be aware that each cash withdrawal will incur 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00.  \\n- Send domestic wires only when necessary to limit paying $5.00 per wire.\\n\\n## Need help?\\n\\nIf you believe a fee was posted in error, gather the transaction date, amount, and any related activity (e.g., wire reference or ATM withdrawal details) and contact support for a review.\\n\\n8. Navy Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_009\\n   Score: 18.0134\\n   Content: ## Where ATM fees apply for Navy Blue\\n- Out-of-network usage: Any transaction at a non‑Rho ATM is assessed a per‑transaction fee of $2.50.\\n- International usage: ATM cash withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs are assessed a fee of 3% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $5.00.\\n- Operator surcharges: The ATM owner may charge an additional surcharge at the terminal. This surcharge is separate from Rho fees.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\n| Scenario | Fee | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Domestic out‑of‑network ATM transaction | $2.50 per transaction | Applies at non‑Rho ATMs in the U.S. |\\n| International ATM cash withdrawal | 3% of withdrawal amount (min. $5.00) | Applies at foreign ATMs outside the U.S. |\\n| Monthly rebates for out‑of‑network usage | Up to $10 per calendar month | Rebates are capped at the monthly limit. |\\n\\n## How international ATM withdrawal fees are calculated\\n- Calculation: The fee equals the greater of:\\n  - 3% of the cash withdrawal amount, or\\n  - $5.00 (minimum)\\n- Threshold for the minimum to apply: The minimum applies when the withdrawal amount is less than or equal to $5.00 divided by 3%.\\n\\n## When fees can combine\\n- If you use an international ATM that is also out‑of‑network, both the $2.50 out‑of‑network fee and the international withdrawal fee of 3% (minimum $5.00) can apply.\\n- ATM operator surcharges, if any, are in addition to the above.\\n\\n## Monthly rebate details\\n- Rho rebates up to $10 in out‑of‑network ATM fees per calendar month.\\n- The monthly cap is the maximum total rebated; fees above this amount are your responsibility after the cap is reached.\\n\\n## Tips to minimize ATM costs\\n- Use Rho ATMs whenever possible to avoid the out‑of‑network fee of $2.50.\\n- For international cash needs, consider making larger, less frequent withdrawals to reduce the impact of the $5.00 minimum relative to the withdrawal amount.\\n- Always review any on‑screen ATM operator surcharge disclosures before completing a transaction.\\n\\n9. Cobalt Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_010\\n   Score: 17.8040\\n   Content: ## Summary of ATM Fees\\n\\n- Domestic out-of-network ATM withdrawal: $2.00 per transaction\\n- International ATM withdrawal: 2.5% of the withdrawal amount (minimum $4.00 per transaction)\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: Up to $15 in out-of-network ATM fee rebates per month\\n\\nNote: ATM owners/operators may charge additional surcharges that you will see at the terminal before you complete the transaction.\\n\\n## Domestic Out-of-Network ATM Usage\\n\\nWhen you use an ATM outside the in-network system within the United States:\\n- You are charged $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Some ATM owners add their own surcharge. You can choose to cancel the transaction if you do not want to accept an operator surcharge.\\n- You can receive up to $15 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network usage. These rebates can offset qualifying out-of-network ATM fees you incur, up to the monthly cap.\\n\\nTips to minimize domestic fees:\\n- Combine cash needs into fewer withdrawals to reduce per-transaction fees.\\n- Check the ATM’s on-screen disclosure for any operator surcharges before accepting.\\n\\n## International ATM Withdrawals\\n\\nFor withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs:\\n- You are charged 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00 per transaction.\\n- Local ATM owners may add their own surcharges at the terminal.\\n- Exchange rates and any third-party conversion choices at the ATM can affect your total cost.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- Withdraw $200: 2.5% of $200 = $5.00; the fee is $5.00 (exceeds the $4.00 minimum).\\n- Withdraw $100: 2.5% of $100 = $2.50; the $4.00 minimum applies, so the fee is $4.00.\\n\\n## Monthly ATM Fee Rebates\\n\\n- You can receive up to $15 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network ATM usage.\\n- The rebate limit applies on a monthly basis; once you reach $15, additional out-of-network ATM fees will not be rebated that month.\\n\\nExample:\\n- If you make two domestic out-of-network withdrawals, your bank-assessed fees would be 2 × $2.00. Up to $15 of qualifying out-of-network ATM fees may be rebated that month.\\n\\n10. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 17.7742\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEddJFJLopw6L5WJ2X6lnhOaYi_WvzlpMBbMAFxVxoAOv2yBG5ExE7-C1IrG5inHt9wFwRgS-GhVpENtlo39y6JKpn2ZI2JWMD0pfmIIUu8xGwSx-U-X6JWqPpULjYoCUew45dEVrQXfauSjysgqNOGhgRRCx1KrVQY3GO8aXVemoNb9ePZkS87sAN1