vDeIkkxGcICwZ99pb8nNMcFg5TqRN_Jy4_mNc1V-ySVXsvt3z1BQkutFripNrgj7ksGgoxRNP8VQjbA9nDGhee0Ri8QHfN6eJJyjhPlYgua7UYk-QG0FF63v8afoByfw3tUfGh9AiEdIITYvSVFbw-NDQwJ8DMrSNPnkaHtQNyvvPMGm1XX1zGqMC7nC5uEy5IMVNrvJquvSnpz71NJOUldr74VRdZVjECOfvD6ptZX5qyUg_rO2dF0iXaxtTZaaNWU7bFFpfF5qH5Expj9ga9sexitwsvGBL5EfIksOYMEt61c5w3bvED3Z1SZ4QsungvcwD0g8O1XYkPu5vgYu-q5qp32d1hfX23CnHCMjCuMsuQvhH1OTEtZOobARjM4bsMpLyguNV9mYl3azyoG2UMbISIsGXNoSe_1B65xyGuKAe1Gowu_0_QQPRskOxeQ==\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc474c694887d1b1b2754adce26526\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Clarifying transaction options**\\n\\nI need to confirm that Purple has no foreign transaction fees and a wallet balance of 30. However, I couldn't verify receiving JPY or EUR. There's a $15 monthly fee if the minimum balance isn't maintained, totaling $180 a year. I should ask if the user is okay with that fee or if they need a no-fee option. It's essential to be cautious about pushing the minimum balance too hard and to gather more information on currency support.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"},{\"text\":\"**Evaluating fee acceptance**\\n\\nI could acknowledge that I can’t confirm the full agent feature list, but we can’t commit to a follow-up just yet. It might be useful to eventually offer human assistance if necessary. I want to confirm with the user whether a $15 monthly fee for travel features is acceptable. They noted the minimum balance is a stretch, so it’s important to clarify that they won't need to hold $3,750 just to waive it. I’ll make sure to communicate all this clearly.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"},{\"text\":\"**Clarifying foreign transaction fees**\\n\\nI can confirm that the Purple Account has 0% foreign transaction fees and supports holding up to 30 foreign currencies. However, I can't confirm all the details just yet. I need to ask if avoiding monthly maintenance fees is a firm requirement, as it's crucial for decision-making. It's important to note that the user dislikes additional fees and tradeoffs, so I’ll respond politely while making sure I communicate all necessary details clearly without being patronizing.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"logprobs\":[],\"text\":\"{\\\"message\\\":\\\"Understood—I won’t base the recommendation on you maintaining $3,750 every day.\\\\n\\\\nYes: the Purple Account charges 0% foreign transaction fees on card purchases in foreign currencies. It also lets you hold balances in up to 30 foreign currencies, rather than converting everything immediately. Conversions still carry the separate 0.5% markup.\\\\n\\\\nOne limitation: the information I found doesn’t list the supported currencies or explain receiving payments directly into those balances, so I can’t yet promise that your yen and euro payments would work as you want.\\\\n\\\\nThe trade-off is the $15 monthly maintenance fee in months you don’t meet the balance waiver. Would that fee be a deal-breaker, or would you consider paying it for the travel features?\\\"}\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc475b588487d186d457e6263a2edc\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"content\":\"If I’m being totally honest, I really don’t want to juggle trade-offs myself.\\n\\nCould you just tell me which **ONE** checking account is the best fit overall for what I’ve said (international travel/ATMs, **no foreign transaction fees**, and ideally being able to hold **yen/euros**)—even if it means I might pay a monthly fee sometimes?\\n\\nAlso, small extras (not deal-breakers): I’m kind of eco-conscious—any “green” angle? And I’ve heard about “premium” accounts… if there’s something exclusive that actually makes sense for me, I’m open to it.\\n\\nAnd just to clarify: I’m **33**, so no student/senior accounts.\",\"role\":\"user\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEdlwpunWQo0pdP211dmQuHRZVQruJRYzUsEjgZnZ8FD4NDeHzYO-0Ro9iJ1d9Ogi-xuuf5Y4KRpl6ppB7NgHmQa0yHUtIj9VKIuiZMlyA39-crbrqDB6ikeb2qb3MIxPhyQJMnz8myQq-BkAU1FuVbre2WGG64iAojCeKJWVBq3veE4A4TZLiDZNwtxdN1ee4vJr_5WPwSOsCNBgVhmQ8OoksqemLBy_DlcLDhhnTFXJ5HizE88gEAe7ABsdSZUEMciYjhiNdOMng1IJYmq85KYdIPlUa4tqRYMOx42QqnQcQeJNVsZCOMN5lgCrgXIktxBUkyC4e42CSx1RJUOGpfiikZtDfJioPG-Nv288jNuEKBx5gHiuJJt4u5FiaMnigeImEVHJOiKajZ1SqHKGrTyF7GKk_dJMnU9VVt_ark6pt0N3JJJ_5qyA6J9q7XQPi7RQIK6Ov5Yr36TswBS5o2AaTBPTHOWhH8PouIGG2eTvlIfAOPbT3iTQCi_e1vIoKLanFC7trVRImFhmKKf86_6Kod6_LfqtTyyZhMtdWluqY11RrHtQQJ1f5IWs2CZ_uO9EjON0LEA4r0N0ABlWGzkQ6GHCfKqDeFfy-65NHjFd5OjiXyZTXrRhUh180GEkOnChVsmVyVFqGYjw4hTEn3po1MQNy044as1AKt0_HjMi2zrDeN_fnb5LTwbG5yWXQSTLJvLh36OU7qa0PxWCKNu3QX1WX3TZ2XvBNSQ55Aoejd5tNmOweUrN--raXuojCSawyoPoJay8ZB2BT35f2FxvOWF87_OQwF521JfLOEY9JiRtfdaRn3kShR4mZC7M5g_m7jUffuiqZ5CIX6uiNeQLLPs1EzJ0XihEZ9XRnKgFFRj9syypzE6RQLAcQSLSOf5lh3XsK1VqwmFoAUrfquNjr_QWd2yjrYf1deNoWaSuCbUM1d64p-WgxlaMo-xzUjXmRGovk-ApTZS6Bm1sLVExqo0QsfJuEIRSEwDHtlsiaFIaJi5YofkAje1Vz_snYdo_nR0krQJHNlw6jqt9oksQtbacWfZndVw_X5ED0JSKZ9EDJx_VecV-JbYdAL0_2kAuoCYEwB0KGP1EeWxFeFygTfj0pzfA9S3H2vMO1s7AWaUK64xbF7o1dPnw1iK7iTmlfLIoGAkKn52CIwd66uCgiGl5tLNhWAbva0SEEZxMZEl99nDtB8cGBtuEPMTem3sfbRKRbOpEmr_LMHkLFISb2Nhmo227swk45r8Nq8vJuCrAKeRlIF8hlgwqP0LFXM5Cmj8czaz29aZ5b64kdsPnv_wVVbwLLkdUpMC5qK4WkEXcC0uvx_a2zPa_xhhiUjcsZya0CpOarMY8UHs4mD9rnDlIoIQd0P5Q16Z_rBYbD-oABBmTNnKIM1ihpWnwdbKgNSZxduzTs_36KXznBftawMvSm7zI_Puo9OyFHCitTOQOAG8qopLAcN8cB_xcFU9AgFm5rWDfevskjoPtkfhbukhw5Stru-o4Q9csBBGQvglD1k5CIJ21vc5_IIXjaB8ctV2g-5OWMi61-StLsOHhfT1QqVASzzEcgk-KRnHB-q3sVAbAU-_a4NS6hFQQTjK_RUNCxfRtfdSOPhKPcZ6-lr0me_4Q5YMhCONjntJ7OC_d9L2fcp_dZ-yzmsVcs2J\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47621f5c87d1b9b2347bce3d8a5b\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Searching for Purple banking options**\\n\\nI need to find the best Purple eco premium banks, but with some caveats since the currency is unknown. I should explore how personal promotion priorities might influence the options available. I really want to avoid echoing anything that’s exclusive to Bluest out of range. I'll also need to look into the account rec policy for personal promotions related to Purple eco premium, ensuring I don't mistakenly refer to anything green. Maybe I can search independently in parallel.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"personal checking accounts recommendations promotion priority travel Purple premium green eco-conscious\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_27ZVN60Jc70jny6QgQzoL3Km\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47658bf887d1b39e41b6c3b6f774\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Purple Account eco sustainable recycled premium exclusive benefits eligibility\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_URTCeaANF2TYLaUSG6zecOzc\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47658c1087d1a0324c9e45ae775c\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_27ZVN60Jc70jny6QgQzoL3Km\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - October 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_014\\n   Score: 28.2517\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 10/12/2025 TO 11/12/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Lime Green account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Hunter Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Lime Green nor Hunter Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our premium and eco-conscious business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n2. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 21.1338\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n3. Linked Checking Account APY Boost: Selection Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_046\\n   Score: 17.6448\\n   Content: ## Multiple Checking Account APY Boost Selection Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank checking accounts that each provide an APY boost on their savings account, the boosts do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable checking account APY boost is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank checking accounts linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each checking account, the corresponding APY boost for the savings account type is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST checking account APY boost is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other checking account boosts are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer with a Gold Savings Account holds:\\n- Green Account (checking): +0.75% APY boost\\n- Purple Account (checking): +0.1% APY boost\\n\\nThe customer receives only the Green Account boost of +0.75% (the highest), not the sum of both.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Checking account APY boosts do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, checking account APY boosts DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Credit card APY bonuses (only highest credit card bonus applies)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium checking accounts while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n### Agent Responsibility\\n\\nWhen investigating interest discrepancies for customers with multiple checking accounts, agents must:\\n1. Identify all checking accounts the customer holds\\n2. Determine which checking account provides the highest APY boost for the savings account type\\n3. Verify that the system is applying the highest boost, not a lower one\\n4. If the system selected the wrong checking account, calculate the correct APY and apply an interest correction\\n\\n4. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 17.5644\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n5. Business Platinum Rewards Card: Travel Planning and Booking Assistance Services\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_business_platinum_rewards_card_005\\n   Score: 15.2030\\n   Content: ## Planning and Research\\n- Receive curated flight, hotel, and car options aligned to your corporate travel preferences.\\n- Get recommendations that balance schedule, policy, and overall trip value.\\n\\n## Booking and Management\\n- Request reservations for flights, hotels, cars, and rail according to traveler profiles and loyalty IDs.\\n- Ask for fare rules and cancellation flexibility to match your risk tolerance.\\n\\n## Disruption Handling\\n- Get assistance with delays, cancellations, and rebookings on active itineraries.\\n- Ask the team to monitor critical segments and secure alternatives as needed.\\n\\n## Group and Executive Travel\\n- Coordinate multi-traveler itineraries and meeting blocks with negotiated rates where available.\\n- Request VIP handling for executives including preferred seating and priority arrangements.\\n\\n## Availability\\n- Concierge travel desk availability: Yes\\n\\n6. Internal: Business Savings Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_015\\n   Score: 14.4692\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business savings accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Gold Saver Account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Silver Plus Saver should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Gold Saver Account nor Silver Plus Saver meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our premium and enhanced-tier business savings offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n7. Lime Green Account: Your Dedicated Account Manager\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_003\\n   Score: 13.0498\\n   Content: ## Response commitments\\n- Direct messages receive a response within 2 business hours.\\n- When calling the priority line, the maximum expected wait is 6 minutes.\\n\\n## How to reach your manager\\n- Send a secure message from within your account's support center and select the option to route to your dedicated manager.\\n- For urgent matters, call the priority support line; your call is queued with elevated priority and subject to the 6 minute maximum wait.\\n\\n## Getting the most out of manager support\\n- Provide context upfront:\\n  - The specific transaction or transfer you need help with.\\n  - Any relevant dates and counterparties.\\n  - Screenshots of error messages (if applicable).\\n- Set your preferred contact method so your manager can follow up quickly.\\n- For time-sensitive requests, note the deadline in your initial message; your manager will respond within 2 business hours.\\n\\n## Escalations\\n- If an issue requires faster handling than messaging, use the priority phone line for a live update within the 6 minute window.\\n\\n## Referral program for Lime Green members\\n\\nAs a Rho-Bank checking account holder, you can refer other businesses to Lime Green and earn substantial rewards:\\n\\n- **Your bonus**: $200 for each successful referral\\n- **Their bonus**: $150 welcome bonus for the referred business\\n- **Annual cap**: 12 referrals per year\\n- **Qualification**: Referred business must deposit $15,000 within 90 days\\n- **Eligibility**: You must have maintained checking account status with Rho-Bank for a minimum of 90 days.\\n\\nSpeak with your dedicated account manager for personalized referral strategies and tracking.\\n\\n8. Internal: Opening Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_001\\n   Score: 12.8564\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a personal checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer is at least 18 years old.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 4 personal checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no checking accounts closed for cause in the past 6 months.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Personal checking account_class options must use the full official name ending with 'Account' (e.g., 'Blue Account', 'Green Account (checking)').\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n9. Internal: Checking Account Referral Program Terms and Restrictions\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_047\\n   Score: 11.7531\\n   Content: ## Program overview\\nEach checking account type has its own referral bonus amounts and qualification requirements. This document covers the general terms and restrictions that apply to all checking account referral programs. Before giving any recommendations or information on referral terms, you must check that the user is eligible to submit referrals first, as users who are not eligible to submit referrals while being given recommendations by the agent tend to leave dissatisfactory reviews. \\n\\n## Rolling window limit\\n- You can receive at most 2 referral bonuses in any rolling 9-day window.\\n- If you attempt to receive more than 2 referrals in a single 9-day period, the third referral (and any subsequent referrals in that window) will be automatically denied.\\n- This limit applies across all checking account types; referrals from different accounts count toward the same 9-day cap.\\n- A rolling 9-day window means the count is evaluated based on the exact timestamps of your most recent referral bonuses, not calendar weeks.\\n- Auto-denied referrals due to the limit cannot be reinstated within the same 9-day window.\\n\\n## Eligibility restrictions\\n- The referred person must be a new Rho-Bank customer with no existing checking, savings, or closed accounts within the past 12 months.\\n- The referrer and referred person cannot be registered at the same address.\\n- The referred person must be 18 years or older, except for the Light Green Account which allows minors with a guardian.\\n- For business accounts: The referred business must have a different primary owner than any existing Rho-Bank business account, based on the SSN of the primary authorized signer.\\n\\n## Referrer tenure policy\\n- Every referral program requires the referrer to meet a tenure threshold before participating.\\n- This threshold is calculated from when you first became a Rho-Bank checking customer—specifically, the date your earliest checking account was opened.\\n- The type of account you currently hold is irrelevant to this calculation. Whether you have a basic or premium product, the tenure measurement remains the same.\\n- Consequently, holding one account type does not prevent you from referring someone to a different account type, as long as the duration since your first account meets or exceeds the program's stated minimum.\\n\\n## Bonus conditions\\n- The qualifying deposit must be new money and cannot be transferred from another Rho-Bank account.\\n- The qualifying deposit must remain in the account for at least 30 days after the qualifying period ends.\\n- If the referred account is closed within 90 days of opening, the referral bonus may be reversed (clawback provision).\\n\\n## Stacking restrictions\\n- The referral bonus cannot be combined with other new account promotions or sign-up bonuses.\\n- Only one referral code can be applied per new account.\\n\\n## Referral status definitions\\n- COMPLETE — The referred person has successfully opened a new account and met the criteria to receive the referral bonus.\\n- IN_PROGRESS — The referred person has successfully opened a new account and is working toward meeting the qualifying deposit requirement.\\n- NO_PROGRESS — The referred person has not applied yet; no progress has been made.\\n- APPLIED — The referred person has submitted an application and is awaiting a decision.\\n- REJECTED — The referral has been denied (e.g., rolling window limit exceeded, ineligible referral).\\n- ERROR — A system error occurred during the referral process.\\n\\n## Practical guidance\\n- Track the timing of your last two successful referral bonuses before sending additional referrals.\\n- If a referral is denied for hitting the rolling window limit, wait until enough time has passed to drop under the cap before attempting another.\\n- Both accounts must remain in good standing for bonuses to be paid.\\n\\n10. Internal: Opening Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_002\\n   Score: 11.1311\\n   Content: ## Scope and Focus\\n\\nProcedure for opening personal savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one active Rho-Bank checking account, 3) Cannot have more than 5 personal savings accounts, 4) Must not have any accounts in collections or with negative balances, 5) Must have held their checking account for at least 14 days. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer, 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account (note: account_class must use the full official name ending with 'Account', e.g., 'Silver Plus Account', 'Gold Account'), 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements (Internal Checklist)\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified in our systems.\\n- Customer has at least one active Rho-Bank checking account.\\n- Customer currently holds fewer than 5 personal savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts in collections and no negative balances.\\n- The customer’s checking account tenure is at least 14 days.\\n\\nDo not proceed if any item above is not met.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify identity\\n- Authenticate the customer and confirm identity verification status on file.\\n\\n2) Check eligibility\\n- Confirm an active checking account exists and meets the 14-day tenure requirement.\\n- Count existing personal savings accounts; ensure the customer is below the 5 limit.\\n- Review account status; there must be no collections activity and no negative balances.\\n\\n3) Confirm account selection\\n- Discuss available personal savings account options with the customer.\\n- Capture the exact account_class string. It must be the full official name ending with “Account” (for example, “Silver Plus Account”, “Gold Account”).\\n\\n4) Open the savings account (agent action)\\n- Use the open_bank_account_4821 tool with account_type set to 'savings' and the confirmed account_class.\\n\\n5) Arrange opening deposit\\n- Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now.\\n  - If yes: use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount from the customer’s checking account to the newly opened savings account.\\n  - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n6) Confirm completion\\n- Provide the new account details and confirm the funding status or the funding deadline.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Usage (Internal Only)\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not ask the customer to call tools or provide tool parameters.\\n\\n- Tool: open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n  - When to call: After steps 1–3, once eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected an account_class.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - user_id: the authenticated customer’s user identifier.\\n    - account_type: 'savings' for personal savings accounts.\\n    - account_class: the full official account name ending with 'Account' exactly as confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Creates a new personal savings account for the customer.\\n\\n- Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n  - When to call: In step 5, only if the customer authorizes an immediate transfer for the opening deposit.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - source_account_id: the customer's Rho-Bank checking account to be debited.\\n    - destination_account_id: the newly opened personal savings account to be credited.\\n    - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Moves funds from checking to savings to complete the opening deposit.\\n\\n## Decision Points and Handling\\n\\n- Exceeds savings account limit: If the customer already has 5 personal savings accounts, do not open a new one. Inform the customer they have reached the maximum.\\n- Insufficient checking tenure: If the checking account has been open fewer than 14 days, advise the customer when they will become eligible.\\n- Collections or negative balances: Resolve these issues first; do not proceed until all accounts are in good standing.\\n- Customer defers funding: Clearly communicate the 30-day funding window and the consequence of closure if unfunded. Document the acknowledgment in the interaction notes.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_URTCeaANF2TYLaUSG6zecOzc\",\"output\":\"1. Green Rewards Card: Which Merchants Are Considered Sustainable?\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_green_rewards_card_005\\n   Score: 16.2785\\n   Content: ## How Merchant Eligibility Is Determined\\n- Eligibility is based on merchant classification, environmental certifications, and program criteria.\\n- Merchants aligned with sustainable goods, services, or infrastructure are generally considered.\\n\\n## Examples of Eligible Merchant Types\\n- Renewable energy providers and clean energy marketplaces\\n- Public transit agencies and shared mobility platforms\\n- Electric vehicle charging networks\\n- Certified green hotels and eco-certified lodging providers\\n- Sustainable office supplies and recycled materials vendors\\n- Waste reduction, recycling, and circular economy services\\n- Carbon offset and climate project organizations\\n- Sustainable logistics and low-emissions shipping providers\\n- Community solar and energy efficiency services\\n\\n## Non-Qualifying or Mixed-Category Merchants\\n- General merchandise retailers without clear sustainable classifications\\n- Marketplace transactions where the end merchant category cannot be verified\\n- Cash equivalents and funding transactions, which do not qualify\\n\\n## Verifying Merchant Qualification\\n- Review the merchant category in your transaction details.\\n- Check for sustainability badges in your transaction feed where available.\\n\\n## Rewards Reminder\\n- Purchases at qualifying sustainable merchants earn 3.0% cash back when processed under eligible categories.\\n\\n2. Diamond Vault Account: Exclusive events and benefits\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_diamond_vault_004\\n   Score: 13.0788\\n   Content: ## Invitations to exclusive events\\n- Access status: Yes.\\n- Expect curated business gatherings focused on strategic finance, market insights, and peer networking.\\n- Invitations may be limited; respond promptly to secure attendance.\\n\\n## Partnered estate and succession planning benefits\\n- Preferred pricing on partner services: 22% discount.\\n- Use your account credentials when booking to ensure the discount is applied at engagement.\\n- Coordinate through your banker for introductions to vetted partners aligned with your needs.\\n\\n## How to redeem benefits\\n- Request a partner referral from your banker and confirm eligibility.\\n- Share your account details during scheduling to apply the discount.\\n- Retain engagement confirmations for your records and reconciliation.\\n\\n3. Green Account (savings): Why is paperless required?\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_004\\n   Score: 12.7446\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n- Paperless statements are required for this account: Yes. This reduces paper consumption and aligns your savings activity with the account's sustainability objectives.\\n\\n## How paperless supports transparency\\n- Your environmental impact report is delivered monthly, giving you regular visibility into outcomes tied to your balance and interest.\\n- Digital delivery eliminates printing and transport, further reducing environmental impact.\\n\\n## Complementary sustainable materials\\n- Your debit card is produced from recycled ocean plastic: Yes. Choosing paperless complements this material choice by minimizing waste throughout your banking experience.\\n\\n## Verifying your paperless status\\n- In online or mobile banking, confirm that statement delivery is set to paperless for this account.\\n- If you previously opted into paper delivery for other accounts, ensure this account remains configured for paperless.\\n\\n4. Linked Checking Account APY Boost: Selection Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_046\\n   Score: 12.7151\\n   Content: ## Multiple Checking Account APY Boost Selection Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank checking accounts that each provide an APY boost on their savings account, the boosts do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable checking account APY boost is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank checking accounts linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each checking account, the corresponding APY boost for the savings account type is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST checking account APY boost is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other checking account boosts are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer with a Gold Savings Account holds:\\n- Green Account (checking): +0.75% APY boost\\n- Purple Account (checking): +0.1% APY boost\\n\\nThe customer receives only the Green Account boost of +0.75% (the highest), not the sum of both.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Checking account APY boosts do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, checking account APY boosts DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Credit card APY bonuses (only highest credit card bonus applies)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium checking accounts while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n### Agent Responsibility\\n\\nWhen investigating interest discrepancies for customers with multiple checking accounts, agents must:\\n1. Identify all checking accounts the customer holds\\n2. Determine which checking account provides the highest APY boost for the savings account type\\n3. Verify that the system is applying the highest boost, not a lower one\\n4. If the system selected the wrong checking account, calculate the correct APY and apply an interest correction\\n\\n5. Gold Account: Gold Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_013\\n   Score: 11.4708\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nGold Account holders who also have a Gold Rewards Card receive exclusive benefits that make the account more accessible. The standard minimum balance requirement of $10,000 is reduced to $5,000 for Gold Rewards Card holders. Additionally, you receive a 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base 5.5% rate. Combined with the existing 30 ATM fee rebates and 20 monthly withdrawals, Gold Rewards Card holders enjoy a premium savings experience with lower balance requirements.\\n\\n## Benefits summary for Gold Rewards Card holders\\n\\n- Reduced minimum balance: $5,000 (down from $10,000)\\n- Relationship bonus APY: 0.025% on top of the base 5.5%\\n- ATM fee rebates: Up to $30 per month\\n- Monthly withdrawals: Up to 20 per month\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Gold Rewards Card holder value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $5,000 (standard: $10,000) |\\n| APY rate | 5.5% + 0.025% |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly max) | $30 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 20 |\\n\\n## Reduced minimum balance\\n\\n- If you hold a Gold Rewards Card, your required minimum balance to maintain the Gold Account is automatically reduced to $5,000.\\n- The standard minimum balance for the Gold Account remains $10,000, but the override applies as long as your Gold Rewards Card is active and associated with your account.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Without the card: Minimum balance requirement is $10,000.\\n- With the card: Minimum balance requirement is $5,000.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- Your Gold Account earns the base 5.5% APY.\\n- As a Gold Rewards Card holder, you receive an additional 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base rate.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Base APY: 5.5%\\n- Relationship bonus APY: +0.025%\\n- Total APY with the bonus: 6.0%\\n\\nNotes:\\n- The relationship bonus is additive to the base rate; it is not a multiplier.\\n- The bonus applies while your Gold Rewards Card remains active and associated with your Gold Account.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates and monthly withdrawals\\n\\n- You continue to receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- You are allowed up to 20 withdrawals per month.\\n\\n## How to confirm your benefits are active\\n\\n- Check your account details to verify:\\n  - The minimum balance requirement displays as $5,000.\\n  - The APY displays as 5.5% plus a 0.025% relationship bonus.\\n  - Your monthly limits show up to $30 in ATM fee rebates and up to 20 withdrawals.\\n\\n6. Business Gold Rewards Card: Annual Fee and Premium Benefits Guide\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_business_gold_rewards_card_007\\n   Score: 10.9728\\n   Content: ## Annual Fee\\n- The annual fee for the Business Gold Rewards Card is $200.00. It bills to your primary account each anniversary.\\n\\n## Premium Lounge Access\\n- Your account includes 9 complimentary lounge visits per account year across participating networks.\\n\\n## Travel Credits\\n- You receive annual travel credits totaling $200.\\n- Apply credits to eligible travel purchases by paying with your card; credits post automatically after eligibility checks.\\n\\n## International Purchases\\n- Foreign transaction fee: 0%. Use your card abroad without added currency conversion fees from this charge.\\n\\n## Concierge Services\\n- Concierge service included: Yes.\\n- Access assistance for travel planning, dining arrangements, and time-sensitive business needs through your account’s concierge channel.\\n\\n## Managing Costs and Benefits\\n- Review your statement after the anniversary to confirm the $200.00 charge and the replenishment of 9 visits and $200 credits.\\n- Set alerts for large travel purchases to verify that credits post as expected.\\n\\n7. Silver Rewards Card: Getting Started and Eligibility Requirements\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_silver_rewards_card_001\\n   Score: 10.7703\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n- Minimum credit score: $680\\n- Annual fee: $0.00\\n- Standard APR for carried balances after any promotional period: 18.99%\\n- Introductory APR for new customers (first year): 0%\\n\\n### International Usage\\n- Foreign transaction fee without a premium subscription: 2.75%\\n- Foreign transaction fee with a premium subscription: 0%\\n\\n## Credit Limits\\n- Initial credit limits typically range from $10,000 to $100,000, subject to approval\\n\\n## Included Protections (At a Glance)\\n- Purchase protection: eligible items are protected for 90 days after purchase, up to $3,000 per claim\\n\\n## Rewards Basics When You Get Started\\n- Purchases outside top categories earn 1.0% back\\n\\n## Virtual Card Availability\\n- Virtual card management features are No for this card\\n\\n## How to Apply\\n1. Complete the online application with your personal information and income details\\n2. Consent to a credit check and submit any requested documentation\\n3. Review your preliminary credit limit offer and terms\\n4. Accept the terms to finalize your account setup\\n\\n## After Approval\\n- Activate your physical card upon arrival and add it to your preferred digital wallets\\n- Set up account alerts and autopay to avoid missed payments\\n- Review your benefits summary, including purchase protection and international fee terms noted above\\n\\n8. Beige Account Referral Program\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_012\\n   Score: 10.6434\\n   Content: ## Enterprise referral program\\n\\nRefer other enterprise-level businesses to the Beige Account and earn premium referral rewards.\\n\\n### Premium rewards\\n- **Your reward**: $500 for each qualifying referral\\n- **Their reward**: $350 welcome bonus\\n- **Annual maximum**: 15 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n\\n### Qualification criteria\\nTo earn a referral bonus:\\n1. Referrer tenure requirement: 120 days since opening your first checking account with us.\\n2. The referred enterprise must open a Beige Account\\n3. They must deposit at least $100,000 within 120 days\\n\\n### Referral details\\n| Detail | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Referrer bonus | $500 |\\n| Referred bonus | $350 |\\n| Maximum per year | 15 |\\n| Required deposit | $100,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Minimum tenure | 120 days |\\n\\n### How to participate\\n1. Contact your dedicated relationship manager for referral materials\\n2. Introduce qualified enterprises to the Beige Account benefits\\n3. Your relationship manager can facilitate introductions and track referrals\\n4. Bonuses are credited after all qualification requirements are confirmed\\n\\n### Enterprise considerations\\n- Referrals must be for new Beige Account relationships\\n- Both enterprises must maintain accounts in good standing\\n- Premium referral bonuses reflect the enterprise-level relationship value\\n\\n9. Green Account (savings): Pairing with EcoCard for bonus APY\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_003\\n   Score: 10.4628\\n   Content: ## Bonus APY with eligible eco cards\\n\\n### How the bonus works\\n- Your Green Account (savings) earns 4.0% on your balance.\\n- When you also hold an EcoCard, you receive an additional bonus of 0.5%.\\n- Your effective APY becomes 4.0% plus 0.5% while eligibility is maintained.\\n\\n### Extra rewards at eco-certified merchants\\n- Eligible purchases at eco-certified merchants can earn an extra cashback bonus of 2.0% when using an EcoCard.\\n\\n## Credit card APY bonuses\\n- Other Rho-Bank credit cards also provide APY bonuses on your Green Account (savings):\\n  - Bronze Rewards Card: +0%\\n  - Silver Rewards Card: +0.45%\\n  - Gold Rewards Card: +0%\\n  - Platinum Rewards Card: +0.35%\\n  - Diamond Elite Card: +0.6%\\n  - Green Rewards Card: +0.4%\\n  - Crypto-Cash Back Card: +0%\\n\\n### Maintaining eligibility\\n- Keep your eligible card in good standing and ensure it remains linked to your Green Account (savings).\\n- If the card is closed or unlinked, the bonus of 0.5% and the extra cashback of 2.0% will not apply.\\n\\n10. Green Account (savings) specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_001\\n   Score: 10.1820\\n   Content: ## Key specifications\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $100 |\\n| Ongoing minimum balance | $500 |\\n| Maximum free withdrawals per month | 8 |\\n| Interest compounding frequency | daily |\\n| Paperless statements required | Yes |\\n| Debit card made from recycled ocean plastic | Yes |\\n\\n### Requirements to open\\n- Fund the account with at least $100.\\n- Enroll in paperless statements, as indicated by Yes.\\n\\n### Ongoing maintenance\\n- Keep your balance at or above $500.\\n- Plan withdrawals to stay within 8 each month.\\n\\n### Interest handling\\n- Interest is compounded daily.\\n\\n### Card materials\\n- Your debit card is made from recycled ocean plastic: Yes.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"g