k left in the budget. There's no urgency to decide, but I would recommend the Purple account as it aligns with your priorities despite fees.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"},{\"text\":\"**Structuring account recommendation**\\n\\nI shouldn't imply that a recommendation comes with a lifetime commitment since I only know about the Purple Account for sure. It might be better to create a structured JSON format with multiple fields instead of one long message—maybe using formatted bullets while avoiding markdown outside. I aim for around 220-270 words without making excessive claims. \\n\\nMy recommendation is the Purple Account, as it covers essential benefits like no foreign fees and has a currency wallet, though I can't confirm some details. Additionally, I haven’t found any green benefits. Let's keep the focus on travel strengths as the next step for savings.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"},{\"text\":\"**Clarifying steps for savings confirmation**\\n\\nI need to confirm important information before suggesting the next steps to the user regarding their savings. While it's fine to proceed, I haven’t received confirmation of all their requests. If they ask how much savings they have, I’ll mention that I cannot confirm details unless a transfer occurs. I shouldn't suggest, \\\"I'll confirm,\\\" since there's no tool for that. Instead, I’ll clarify, \\\"I can’t confirm...\\\" but we can continue with the savings discussion for now.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"logprobs\":[],\"text\":\"{\\\"message\\\":\\\"My one checking-account recommendation is the Purple Account. It best matches your main travel priorities, even if you sometimes pay the monthly fee.\\\\n\\\\nWhy I’d choose it for you:\\\\n• No foreign transaction fees on card purchases in foreign currencies.\\\\n• No Rho foreign ATM withdrawal fee, plus reimbursement of ATM operator fees worldwide up to $30 per month. Anything above that cap remains your cost.\\\\n• A multi-currency wallet that holds up to 30 foreign currencies. I still can’t confirm that yen and euros are supported or that your payments can be received directly into those balances—so don’t rely on that feature until those details are confirmed.\\\\n\\\\nFor your budget, I’d plan for the $15 monthly maintenance fee rather than stretch to avoid it. The fee is waived when your minimum daily balance stays at least $3,750. Currency conversions also carry a separate 0.5% markup above the interbank rate.\\\\n\\\\nFor premium extras, Purple includes six complimentary airport lounge visits per year and eligible travel-insurance benefits up to $30,000, subject to coverage terms. Those are more relevant to you than a high-balance account chosen just for exclusivity.\\\\n\\\\nI haven’t found a documented eco-specific benefit for Purple. I’d prioritize its travel features and consider sustainability separately when we choose your savings account.\\\\n\\\\nNext, roughly how much do you expect to keep in savings?\\\"}\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc477fff0c87d18ec05b03e75a751d\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"content\":\"Okay—if you think the **Purple Account** is the one that best fits everything I said, then let’s do it!\\n\\nAnd perfect—now I also need a **savings** account. Let me tell you what I’m looking for there:\\n\\n- I end up tapping into my savings **3–4 times a week**, sometimes more, and I **don’t want fees** for that.\\n- Since I’ll have multiple accounts with you, is there some kind of **relationship bonus rate**?\\n- I can keep about **$5k–$6k** in there, **maybe $7k max**.\\n- I **need daily compounding** — that’s non-negotiable.\\n- I use **out-of-network ATMs** a lot too… any way to get those fees covered (even for savings)?\\n- And I want to earn at least **3% APY** once my balance grows.\\n\\nAlso, side questions (not sure if they matter): is there something “green”? And I’d rather not get something super basic—my friend mentioned **Gold** and **Green** accounts, but I’m not sure what’s what.\",\"role\":\"user\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEePnSX-yJYHYDtaj_SnoKT_nT-CZz2GlhrLVmITotPyIXXE3ykv13KZsOQ3Ff0VuYkuuOfTkI9gv-c1rX0z9RIBGLhz_3LuSdZxX_EuY62jswwh996g2qSqwBurdL4B92t_2xth82iuUWLi_17GGqMB96VPzQaDirEMUTn7WoKZ7dLE-swrfn2750fnKCnMJ-4WiwnQnndZr637238i0Dq8VafE_dv6RKGhQO2B6EYpdGG3ZLqM1VnjHJGQrw7nROX9LLZzsvV7uB4DkgcT7oK7_C2kPs4S_Csc0YfeauKII5-rJ1DRmHqE4TBNgkukBmjCvH_hVfj21Pk-rfhYQY1l04JPna_1SiNCkBQkQS1zn1lTtOxOjDHvCu7ymuB5jC0yVq_p67r2s1MHvis3f5iimUK19lAOoR-g6JnDOQ0WvUZHiX5FaFVZ22XP-7KKaSbjyOkGHOXUQl2GgvnJVPZYVEI51ZbRLotuGtZwKaTa3jQiitMSfSpmIB5KgmeWbCgS1DxVWuDWIxNQWtmPMntR3F5mtY3AamEZZOyU6VsQD6FW2dMvaLvdTAQ7xBNh3QlLW6oHUhprYRTm-Kd0G3VRu_ZY9GwUQG-_Ib6udfQdeukpPpnn_zaDtBY5YBx8qbb6wHfSAbsxCNocIAHCcc3YcLx6XaMP4dcGnflMZcu8wlO0W4gsPfHQAixE1IELOCo_3tOpovyhAMDBnNcM3T7YRkFuUEWp_GmbsebYglrEcR58s4iSTMAVZw9YZX2NanROjU6VdMY6MFxNktnpHD9yUQMDDgjuAADOK-YF5DY6iZUGVcnWZHQO95EbKQFLpSA_2UFp0bgJfY736YfqcuV_1zuUrpyDNdu7Wq5flXOSPFBCEKM5N__M7_u8l8mo10k7SRyEC3fY493KZL_Al_ZiFGzc1gHzFIncIjmWHNcbxkI76VtAvvCjQRLYD-iyQ2hN7Os5vAWC669JY6N5JKkgV7_44jC6Zq7SGWDRsErHCM_M1Eb_3f5RVQSj_fyp2CyitAAGtMmFxfHZjJodRiUeQDjyl1-1f2eiouG-Z4SQvFWpmM3pKDq5bpOS76mWACX_0avBCyh9gsp1op2kn66fF1wW0_W8wAJha3NLBRebBYMz30raA6I2EtkqtWtIH9V_ukro7TPP3YCQdUopWR9HdhqkOyndEFLdZ62VQlqu8pgSgyxMymbspu3GkjmCdNOSy01JtEqnbUUEfwuxkR57uBs_vFHJMWn0nEA0UrMGhjOiBrFmh4qy1Qi8iO6RwzvBc8hV3DaPLGL-8OHyk28TcHaX_8bdSY8QnikxnWR54I3pCWQHSJpDOw88IvFHNS3pnzkAdVsNxwwgOx6SSr6BdKRhagR8LwEtLnQPO1vEP6z1ZhmaWDMN6ceoYKfUGwbGMR-qMgknwMMoaCM3qDO45kQpEzYIjUGJvybDO_sJib0MwX46gsnc9nH-FDVuE4fbk_Z2Eoa0Qv63GdmZOKfql2CGDZBsmVe9FnQmiUz0t0A=\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc478bbdf487d180338744a8446680\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Evaluating savings options**\\n\\nI’m thinking about finding a suitable savings account for the user. I want to make sure it allows for infinite withdrawals and has no fees, as well as having an APY of at least 3%. It seems like the Silver Plus relationship account might be a good fit since it offers unlimited access but requires a minimum of $5,000 to waive fees. I'll need to retrieve more details to confirm this.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"personal savings unlimited withdrawals daily compounding ATM rebates relationship bonus Silver Plus Account\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_kd0MirS5k5ToVm6TnBid63z3\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc478edd6887d19a2d888f7ee84520\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"savings account relationship bonus multiple accounts balance 5000 APY 3% withdrawal fees\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_WM94PyCUCM1llKDwo8TJys9w\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc478edd7887d19f4a42fc8d8ce04d\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_kd0MirS5k5ToVm6TnBid63z3\",\"output\":\"1. Silver Plus: Differences from Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_002\\n   Score: 30.3847\\n   Content: ## What changes with Silver Plus\\n\\n### Tiered APY\\n- Silver Plus offers tiered APY with two levels:\\n  - Tier 1 APY: 3.0% for balances below the Tier 2 threshold.\\n  - Tier 2 APY: 4.5% for balances at or above the Tier 2 threshold.\\n\\n### Withdrawal flexibility\\n- Increased access with up to 15 free withdrawals per month.\\n\\n### ATM fee support\\n- Receive ATM fee rebates up to 25 each month.\\n\\n### Statement delivery\\n- Paper statements are available for Silver Plus Account holders.\\n- The monthly paper statement fee is $0.00. You can enable paper statements in your account settings.\\n- Paperless statements are NOT required for this account (unlike Green Account (savings) which requires paperless).\\n\\n### Relationship benefits\\n- Earn an additional relationship APY bonus of 0.025% when you qualify under the relationship criteria.\\n\\n2. Silver Account: Platinum Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_009\\n   Score: 27.8569\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nSilver Account holders who also have a Platinum Rewards Card receive enhanced withdrawal privileges. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 5 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 10 + 5 = 15 withdrawals per month. This benefit is automatically applied when both accounts are linked under the same customer profile. Combined with the existing 15 ATM fee rebates and 0.025% relationship bonus, Platinum Rewards Card holders get an elevated Silver Account experience.\\n\\n## APY bonuses from credit cards\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.2%\\n- Diamond Elite Card: +0.25%\\n\\n## What you receive as a Platinum Rewards Card holder\\n\\n- Additional free withdrawals: +5 per month on top of your standard 10 free withdrawals\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 10 + 5 = 15\\n- ATM fee relief: Up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month\\n- Earnings boost: An additional 0.025% relationship bonus added to your APY when eligible\\n\\n## Activation and eligibility\\n\\n- The enhanced withdrawal limit is automatically applied when your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile.\\n- The 0.025% relationship bonus and 15 ATM fee rebates apply in the same profile-linked setup.\\n\\n### How to confirm your accounts are linked\\n\\n1. Sign in to Rho-Bank Online Banking or the mobile app.\\n2. Open your customer profile and review your list of accounts and cards.\\n3. Verify that your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card appear under the same customer profile.\\n4. If you do not see both products under one profile, consolidate them to a single profile or contact us for assistance.\\n\\n## Using your monthly withdrawal allowance\\n\\n- Counting method: Any transaction classified as a withdrawal under your Silver Account terms counts toward your monthly total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Cycle timing: Your free withdrawal count resets at the start of each monthly statement cycle.\\n- Beyond the limit: Transactions above your free monthly total may be subject to standard Silver Account withdrawal charges.\\n\\nExample:\\n- You make 12 withdrawals in a month: all 12 are free.\\n- You make 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n- You make 16 withdrawals in a month: the first 15 are free; the 16th may incur standard charges.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You are eligible for up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- Rebates apply after ATM fees post to your Silver Account; check your transaction history for the corresponding credit within the same month.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- When your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile, an additional 0.025% is added to your APY as a relationship bonus.\\n- The relationship bonus is reflected in your APY while eligibility is maintained.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting and tips\\n\\n- If you do not see the extra withdrawals or 0.025% reflected, confirm both products are under the same customer profile.\\n- Check that you are within the current monthly statement cycle for the added withdrawals to apply.\\n- Review your transaction history to verify ATM fee charges and corresponding rebates up to 15 for the month.\\n\\n3. Gold Account: Gold Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_013\\n   Score: 26.5295\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nGold Account holders who also have a Gold Rewards Card receive exclusive benefits that make the account more accessible. The standard minimum balance requirement of $10,000 is reduced to $5,000 for Gold Rewards Card holders. Additionally, you receive a 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base 5.5% rate. Combined with the existing 30 ATM fee rebates and 20 monthly withdrawals, Gold Rewards Card holders enjoy a premium savings experience with lower balance requirements.\\n\\n## Benefits summary for Gold Rewards Card holders\\n\\n- Reduced minimum balance: $5,000 (down from $10,000)\\n- Relationship bonus APY: 0.025% on top of the base 5.5%\\n- ATM fee rebates: Up to $30 per month\\n- Monthly withdrawals: Up to 20 per month\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Gold Rewards Card holder value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $5,000 (standard: $10,000) |\\n| APY rate | 5.5% + 0.025% |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly max) | $30 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 20 |\\n\\n## Reduced minimum balance\\n\\n- If you hold a Gold Rewards Card, your required minimum balance to maintain the Gold Account is automatically reduced to $5,000.\\n- The standard minimum balance for the Gold Account remains $10,000, but the override applies as long as your Gold Rewards Card is active and associated with your account.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Without the card: Minimum balance requirement is $10,000.\\n- With the card: Minimum balance requirement is $5,000.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- Your Gold Account earns the base 5.5% APY.\\n- As a Gold Rewards Card holder, you receive an additional 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base rate.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Base APY: 5.5%\\n- Relationship bonus APY: +0.025%\\n- Total APY with the bonus: 6.0%\\n\\nNotes:\\n- The relationship bonus is additive to the base rate; it is not a multiplier.\\n- The bonus applies while your Gold Rewards Card remains active and associated with your Gold Account.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates and monthly withdrawals\\n\\n- You continue to receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- You are allowed up to 20 withdrawals per month.\\n\\n## How to confirm your benefits are active\\n\\n- Check your account details to verify:\\n  - The minimum balance requirement displays as $5,000.\\n  - The APY displays as 5.5% plus a 0.025% relationship bonus.\\n  - Your monthly limits show up to $30 in ATM fee rebates and up to 20 withdrawals.\\n\\n4. Bluest Account exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_003\\n   Score: 24.3344\\n   Content: ## What you get with Bluest Account\\n\\n- Higher yield on your checking balance: 2.25% APY\\n- Complimentary domestic outgoing wires each month: 10\\n- Incoming domestic wires at no charge: $0.00\\n- Dedicated personal banker assigned: Yes\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates, up to: $50\\n- Complimentary personal check orders per year: 3\\n- Safe deposit box rental discount: 75.0%\\n- Stop payment requests at no charge: $0\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00\\n- Boosts on linked savings:\\n  - Silver Savings APY boost: 0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings APY boost: 0.7%\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Included |\\n|---|---|\\n| Checking APY | 2.25% |\\n| Free domestic outgoing wires (per month) | 10 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Dedicated personal banker | Yes |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly cap) | $50 |\\n| Complimentary check orders (per year) | 3 |\\n| Safe deposit box discount | 75.0% |\\n| Stop payment fee | $0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Silver Savings APY boost | 0.45% |\\n| Bronze Savings APY boost | 0.7% |\\n\\n## Referral rewards\\n\\nShare the Bluest experience and earn rewards:\\n- Referrer bonus: $75 per successful referral\\n- New member bonus: $50 for the person you refer\\n- Annual limit: 8 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n- Qualifying requirement: Referred person must deposit $2,000 within 90 days\\n- Eligibility: Referrers must have established their Rho-Bank checking relationship at least 60 days prior.\\n\\n## How to use your benefits\\n\\n### Complimentary wire transfers\\n- Send up to 10 domestic wire transfers per calendar month at no charge.\\n- Incoming domestic wires post with a $0.00 fee.\\n\\n### Dedicated personal banker\\n- A dedicated banker is assigned to your account (Yes). Use this single point of contact for complex transactions, expedited support, and account planning.\\n\\n### ATM fee rebates\\n- When you incur third-party ATM fees, you are rebated up to $50 per monthly statement cycle.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Withdraw from ATMs abroad with no Rho-Bank fee: $0.00. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n### Complimentary check orders\\n- Place up to 3 personal check orders each year at no cost.\\n\\n### Safe deposit box discount\\n- Receive a 75.0% discount on an eligible safe deposit box rental.\\n\\n### Stop payments\\n- Submit stop payment requests with a waived fee of $0.\\n\\n### Enhanced yields\\n- Earn 2.25% APY on your Bluest Account balance.\\n- Link eligible savings to activate boosts:\\n  - Silver Savings: +0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings: +0.7%\\n\\n5. Green Account (savings): EcoCard holder exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_009\\n   Score: 22.7488\\n   Content: ## EcoCard holder benefits overview\\n\\nGreen Account (savings) holders who also have an EcoCard receive enhanced benefits that make eco-conscious banking even more rewarding. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 7 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 8 + 7 = 15 withdrawals per month. You also receive 20 in ATM fee rebates monthly. Combined with the existing 0.5% bonus APY for EcoCard holders on top of the base 4.0% rate, this creates a comprehensive eco-friendly savings experience with maximum flexibility.\\n\\n## What you get as an EcoCard holder\\n\\n- Increased monthly free withdrawals: 8 + 7 = 15 total free withdrawals per month\\n- ATM fee rebates: up to $20 in rebates each month\\n- Rate boost: 0.5% bonus APY on top of the base 4.0% rate (example total: 4.75%)\\n\\n## Increased free withdrawals\\n\\n- Your free withdrawal allowance increases by 7 each month, for a total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Examples:\\n  - 10 withdrawals in a month: all 10 are free.\\n  - 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n  - More than 15 withdrawals in a month: any withdrawals beyond 15 are not free.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You receive up to $20 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- If total ATM operator fees in a month exceed $20, the excess amount is not rebated.\\n- Tip: Keep your receipts or review your statements to track how much of the $20 monthly cap you have used.\\n\\n## Bonus APY for EcoCard holders\\n\\n- Your Green Account earns the base 4.0% APY plus a 0.5% bonus when you hold an EcoCard.\\n- Example: 4.0% + 0.5% = 4.75% APY.\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 8 + 7 = 15\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: $20\\n- APY boost: 4.0% base + 0.5% bonus\\n\\n6. Silver Plus Saver Account: Complete Guide\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_plus_saver_001\\n   Score: 22.5487\\n   Content: ## Eligibility and Minimum Balance\\n- You must maintain a minimum balance of $5,000 to keep the Silver Plus Saver account in good standing.\\n- If your balance is anticipated to dip below $5,000, consider timing deposits and withdrawals to avoid falling under the requirement.\\n\\n## Interest and APY Structure\\n- Balances below the tier 2 threshold earn 2.5% APY.\\n- Balances above the tier 2 threshold earn 4.0% APY.\\n\\n### Relationship APY Bonuses\\nIf you hold an eligible Business Rewards Card, an APY bonus is added to your base APY:\\n- Business Silver Rewards Card: +0.18% APY\\n- Business Gold Rewards Card: +0.38% APY\\n- Business Platinum Rewards Card: +0.62% APY\\n\\nThe bonus applies to the base APY for the balance tier you qualify for.\\n\\n### Example APYs With Relationship Bonuses\\nBelow are example total APYs when a relationship bonus applies:\\n\\n- Balance below tier 2 threshold (base 2.5%):\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card: 2.68% (2.5% + 0.18%)\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card: 2.88% (2.5% + 0.38%)\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card: 3.12% (2.5% + 0.62%)\\n\\n- Balance above tier 2 threshold (base 4.0%):\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card: 4.18% (4.0% + 0.18%)\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card: 4.38% (4.0% + 0.38%)\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card: 4.62% (4.0% + 0.62%)\\n\\n## Withdrawals and Transfers\\nSilver Plus Saver offers higher withdrawal limits and improved transfer capabilities compared to Silver Saver. To make the most of these enhancements:\\n- Plan large withdrawals in advance to ensure smooth processing.\\n- Use scheduled transfers for recurring payments to maintain your target balance above $5,000.\\n- For unusually large or time-sensitive transfers, initiate earlier in the business day to reduce the risk of delays.\\n\\n## Upgrading from Silver Saver\\nIf you are moving up from Silver Saver:\\n- Confirm you can maintain at least $5,000 in Silver Plus Saver.\\n- Request an upgrade through your online banking or by contacting support. Your balances will begin earning at the Silver Plus Saver rates as soon as the upgrade is completed.\\n\\n## How to Verify Your Current APY and Bonus\\n- In online banking, open the Silver Plus Saver account details to view:\\n  - Your current balance tier (below or above the tier 2 threshold)\\n  - Base APY for that tier (2.5% or 4.0%)\\n  - Any relationship APY bonus applied (e.g., 0.38%) \\n- Review after any balance change or card status update to confirm your effective APY.\\n\\n7. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 21.5264\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n8. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 19.9105\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n9. Silver Plus Account: Credit Card APY Bonuses\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_009\\n   Score: 19.4480\\n   Content: ## Credit card APY bonuses for Silver Plus Account holders\\n\\nHolding certain Rho-Bank credit cards provides bonus APY on your Silver Plus Account balance. These bonuses are automatically applied when you hold both the credit card and savings account under the same customer profile.\\n\\n### Available credit card APY bonuses\\n\\n| Credit Card | APY Bonus |\\n|---|---|\\n| Bronze Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Silver Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Gold Rewards Card | +0.2% |\\n| Platinum Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Diamond Elite Card | +0.4% |\\n| EcoCard | +0.45% |\\n| Green Rewards Card | +0.1% |\\n| Crypto-Cash Back Card | +0% |\\n\\n### How to qualify\\n\\n1. Open or maintain a Silver Plus Account.\\n2. Hold an eligible Rho-Bank credit card under the same customer profile.\\n3. The APY bonus is automatically applied to your Silver Plus Account earnings.\\n\\n10. FAQ: Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_005\\n   Score: 19.3044\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions\\n\\n### What APY does the Silver Account pay?\\n- Your APY depends on your balance tier. The lower tier pays 2.5%, and the higher tier pays 4.0%.\\n\\n### What minimum balance should I keep, and what happens if I don't meet it?\\n- Keep at least $1,000 in your account to meet the minimum balance requirement. If you do not meet this requirement for a statement cycle, a monthly maintenance fee of $5.00 applies.\\n\\n### Is there a cost if I make too many withdrawals?\\n- Yes. If you exceed the monthly withdrawal limit for your account, an excess withdrawal fee of $2.00 applies to each additional withdrawal.\\n\\n### Do I get a bonus for having multiple Rho-Bank products?\\n- Yes. Eligible customers receive a relationship APY bonus of 0.025% added to the base Silver APY.\\n\\n### Do you rebate ATM fees?\\n- Yes. You can receive ATM fee rebates up to 15 each month.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=3ms, reranking=0ms, total=3ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_WM94PyCUCM1llKDwo8TJys9w\",\"output\":\"1. Linked Checking Account APY Boost: Selection Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_046\\n   Score: 22.3735\\n   Content: ## Multiple Checking Account APY Boost Selection Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank checking accounts that each provide an APY boost on their savings account, the boosts do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable checking account APY boost is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank checking accounts linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each checking account, the corresponding APY boost for the savings account type is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST checking account APY boost is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other checking account boosts are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer with a Gold Savings Account holds:\\n- Green Account (checking): +0.75% APY boost\\n- Purple Account (checking): +0.1% APY boost\\n\\nThe customer receives only the Green Account boost of +0.75% (the highest), not the sum of both.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Checking account APY boosts do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, checking account APY boosts DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Credit card APY bonuses (only highest credit card bonus applies)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium checking accounts while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n### Agent Responsibility\\n\\nWhen investigating interest discrepancies for customers with multiple checking accounts, agents must:\\n1. Identify all checking accounts the customer holds\\n2. Determine which checking account provides the highest APY boost for the savings account type\\n3. Verify that the system is applying the highest boost, not a lower one\\n4. If the system selected the wrong checking account, calculate the correct APY and apply an interest correction\\n\\n2. Silver Account: Platinum Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_009\\n   Score: 20.3290\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nSilver Account holders who also have a Platinum Rewards Card receive enhanced withdrawal privileges. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 5 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 10 + 5 = 15 withdrawals per month. This benefit is automatically applied when both accounts are linked under the same customer profile. Combined with the existing 15 ATM fee rebates and 0.025% relationship bonus, Platinum Rewards Card holders get an elevated Silver Account experience.\\n\\n## APY bonuses from credit cards\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.2%\\n- Diamond Elite Card: +0.25%\\n\\n## What you receive as a Platinum Rewards Card holder\\n\\n- Additional free withdrawals: +5 per month on top of your standard 10 free withdrawals\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 10 + 5 = 15\\n- ATM fee relief: Up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month\\n- Earnings boost: An additional 0.025% relationship bonus added to your APY when eligible\\n\\n## Activation and eligibility\\n\\n- The enhanced withdrawal limit is automatically applied when your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile.\\n- The 0.025% relationship bonus and 15 ATM fee rebates apply in the same profile-linked setup.\\n\\n### How to confirm your accounts are linked\\n\\n1. Sign in to Rho-Bank Online Banking or the mobile app.\\n2. Open your customer profile and review your list of accounts and cards.\\n3. Verify that your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card appear under the same customer profile.\\n4. If you do not see both products under one profile, consolidate them to a single profile or contact us for assistance.\\n\\n## Using your monthly withdrawal allowance\\n\\n- Counting method: Any transaction classified as a withdrawal under your Silver Account terms counts toward your monthly total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Cycle timing: Your free withdrawal count resets at the start of each monthly statement cycle.\\n- Beyond the limit: Transactions above your free monthly total may be subject to standard Silver Account withdrawal charges.\\n\\nExample:\\n- You make 12 withdrawals in a month: all 12 are free.\\n- You make 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n- You make 16 withdrawals in a month: the first 15 are free; the 16th may incur standard charges.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You are eligible for up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- Rebates apply after ATM fees post to your Silver Account; check your transaction history for the corresponding credit within the same month.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- When your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile, an additional 0.025% is added to your APY as a relationship bonus.\\n- The relationship bonus is reflected in your APY while eligibility is maintained.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting and tips\\n\\n- If you do not see the extra withdrawals or 0.025% reflected, confirm both products are under the same customer profile.\\n- Check that you are within the current monthly statement cycle for the added withdrawals to apply.\\n- Review your transaction history to verify ATM fee charges and corresponding rebates up to 15 for the month.\\n\\n3. Credit Card APY Bonuses: Stacking Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_045\\n   Score: 20.2464\\n   Content: ## Credit Card APY Bonus Stacking Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank credit cards that each provide an APY bonus on their savings account, the bonuses do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable credit card APY bonus is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank credit cards linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each credit card, the corresponding APY bonus is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST credit card APY bonus is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other credit card bonuses are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer holds:\\n- Gold Rewards Card: +0.025% APY bonus\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.15% APY bonus\\n- EcoCard: +0.6% APY bonus\\n\\nThe customer receives only the EcoCard bonus of +0.6% (the highest), not the sum of all three.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Credit card APY bonuses do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, credit card APY bonuses DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Checking account APY boosts (e.g., Green Account checking boost)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium credit cards while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n4. Internal: Submitting Interest Discrepancy Reports\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_044\\n   Score: 20.1347\\n   Content: When a customer's savings account interest calculation is incorrect, agents must submit an interest discrepancy report to the backend team for investigation. Use the submit_interest_discrepancy_report_7294 tool to create this report.\\n\\nWhen to Submit a Report:\\n\\n1. Missing APY Boost: Customer has a qualifying checking-savings account pairing but the linked checking APY boost was not applied to their interest calculation.\\n\\n2. Incorrect Tier Rate: Customer's balance qualifies for a higher APY tier but the lower tier rate was applied.\\n\\n3. Missing Relationship Bonus: Customer maintains multiple Rho-Bank products but the relationship bonus was not applied.\\n\\n4. System Calculation Error: Any other discrepancy between expected and actual interest credited.\\n\\nTool: submit_interest_discrepancy_report_7294\\nParameters:\\n- account_id (string): The savings account ID with the discrepancy\\n- user_id (string): The customer's unique identifier\\n- expected_apy (number): The APY percentage the customer should have received (e.g., 2.775 for 2.775%)\\n- actual_apy (number): The APY percentage that was actually applied (e.g., 2.5 for 2.5%)\\n- amount_difference (number): The dollar amount difference between expected and actual interest credited\\n\\nProcedure:\\n1) Verify the customer's identity and account ownership\\n2) Look up the customer's accounts using get_all_user_accounts_by_user_id_3847\\n3) Check transaction history using get_bank_account_transactions_9173 to find the interest credit\\n4) Review documentation for the savings account type to determine all applicable APY components (base rate, tier rate, linked checking boost, credit card bonuses, relationship bonus)\\n5) Calculate the expected APY by adding all applicable components\\n6) Calculate the discrepancy between expected and actual interest\\n7) If a discrepancy exists, first apply a credit using apply_savings_account_credit_6831 to correct the customer's account\\n8) Then submit the discrepancy report using submit_interest_discrepancy_report_7294\\n\\nImportant: Always apply the credit to the customer's account BEFORE submitting the report. The report is for backend investigation to fix the underlying system issue, while the credit immediately resolves the customer's concern.\\n\\n5. Gold Account: Gold Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_013\\n   Score: 19.9655\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nGold Account holders who also have a Gold Rewards Card receive exclusive benefits that make the account more accessible. The standard minimum balance requirement of $10,000 is reduced to $5,000 for Gold Rewards Card holders. Additionally, you receive a 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base 5.5% rate. Combined with the existing 30 ATM fee rebates and 20 monthly withdrawals, Gold Rewards Card holders enjoy a premium savings experience with lower balance requirements.\\n\\n## Benefits summary for Gold Rewards Card holders\\n\\n- Reduced minimum balance: $5,000 (down from $10,000)\\n- Relationship bonus APY: 0.025% on top of the base 5.5%\\n- ATM fee rebates: Up to $30 per month\\n- Monthly withdrawals: Up to 20 per month\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Gold Rewards Card holder value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $5,000 (standard: $10,000) |\\n| APY rate | 5.5% + 0.025% |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly max) | $30 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 20 |\\n\\n## Reduced minimum balance\\n\\n- If you hold a Gold Rewards Card, your required minimum balance to maintain the Gold Account is automatically reduced to $5,000.\\n- The standard minimum balance for the Gold Account remains $10,000, but the override applies as long as your Gold Rewards Card is active and associated with your account.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Without the card: Minimum balance requirement is $10,000.\\n- With the card: Minimum balance requirement is $5,000.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- Your Gold Account earns the base 5.5% APY.\\n- As a Gold Rewards Card holder, you receive an additional 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base rate.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Base APY: 5.5%\\n- Relationship bonus APY: +0.025%\\n- Total APY with the bonus: 6.0%\\n\\nNotes:\\n- The relationship bonus is additive to the base rate; it is not a multiplier.\\n- The bonus applies while your Gold Rewards Card remains active and associated with your Gold Account.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates and monthly withdrawals\\n\\n- You continue to receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- You are allowed up to 20 withdrawals per month.\\n\\n## How to confirm your benefits are active\\n\\n- Check your account details to verify:\\n  - The minimum balance requirement displays as $5,000.\\n  - The APY displays as 5.5% plus a 0.025% relationship bonus.\\n  - Your monthly limits show up to $30 in ATM fee rebates and up to 20 withdrawals.\\n\\n6. Silver Plus Saver Account: Relationship bonuses explained\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_plus_saver_003\\n   Score: 19.4538\\n   Content: ## How the relationship bonus works\\n- When you qualify based on holding multiple eligible Rho-Bank products, your Silver Plus Saver APY receives an additive bonus of 0.025%.\\n- The relationship bonus is applied on top of the APY you earn from your balance tier.\\n\\n### Applying the bonus to your account\\n- Eligibility is evaluated based on your relationship status with Rho-Bank.\\n- Once eligible, the 0.025% increment is added to the APY associated with your current tier for the period you qualify.\\n- If eligibility changes, the bonus adjusts prospectively.\\n\\n### Fee considerations\\n- If you do not meet the minimum balance requirement, a monthly maintenance fee of $10.00 is assessed according to your account terms.\\n- The relationship bonus affects your APY; it does not change how the monthly maintenance fee is determined.\\n\\n### Practical tips\\n- Periodically review your product holdings to ensure you continue to qualify for the relationship bonus.\\n- Monitor your balance relative to the minimum requirement so that any potential $10.00 does not reduce your interest gains, especially when the 0.025% is active.\\n\\n7. FAQ: Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_005\\n   Score: 19.1248\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions\\n\\n### What APY does the Silver Account pay?\\n- Your APY depends on your balance tier. The lower tier pays 2.5%, and the higher tier pays 4.0%.\\n\\n### What minimum balance should I keep, and what happens if I don't meet it?\\n- Keep at least $1,000 in your account to meet the minimum balance requirement. If you do not meet this requirement for a statement cycle, a monthly maintenance fee of $5.00 applies.\\n\\n### Is there a cost if I make too many withdrawals?\\n- Yes. If you exceed the monthly withdrawal limit for your account, an excess withdrawal fee of $2.00 applies to each additional withdrawal.\\n\\n### Do I get a bonus for having multiple Rho-Bank products?\\n- Yes. Eligible customers receive a relationship APY bonus of 0.025% added to the base Silver APY.\\n\\n### Do you rebate ATM fees?\\n- Yes. You can receive ATM fee rebates up to 15 each month.\\n\\n8. Linking Silver Account with a Rho checking account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_002\\n   Score: 18.1499\\n   Content: ## What linking does\\n- When you link your Silver Account to a Rho-Bank checking account, your Silver APY receives an additional [[linked_checking_apy_bonus]].\\n- If you maintain multiple Rho-Bank products, you may also qualify for a relationship bonus of 0.025% that stacks on top of your base Silver APY.\\n\\n## How to link your accounts\\n- From your Rho-Bank dashboard, open your Silver Account and choose the option to link a Rho checking account.\\n- Confirm both accounts are under the same ownership and tax ID.\\n- Complete the on-screen authorization to finalize the link; APY adjustments typically appear shortly after linking.\\n\\n## Ongoing eligibility\\n- Keep both accounts open and in good standing. Unlinking the checking account can remove the [[linked_checking_apy_bonus]] and may affect your eligibility for the 0.025%.\\n\\n9. Bronze Saver Account: Withdrawal limits explained\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_bronze_saver_account_008\\n   Score: 17.3910\\n   Content: ## Your monthly limit\\n- You are allowed up to 12 free withdrawals each month.\\n\\n## Fees after the limit\\n- Each withdrawal that exceeds 12 in a month will incur an excess withdrawal fee of $3.00.\\n\\n## What typically counts as a withdrawal\\n- Transfers from your savings to external banks via ACH\\n- Outgoing wire transfers\\n- Internal transfers from savings to other accounts\\n- Cash withdrawals initiated against this account\\n\\n## Tips to avoid excess withdrawal fees\\n- Consolidate multiple small transfers into fewer withdrawals when appropriate.\\n- Plan recurring payments to stay within 12 per month.\\n- Monitor your activity near the end of each statement cycle to avoid unintentional overages.\\n\\n10. Silver Plus: Differences from Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_002\\n   Score: 17.0036\\n   Content: ## What changes with Silver Plus\\n\\n### Tiered APY\\n- Silver Plus offers tiered APY with two levels:\\n  - Tier 1 APY: 3.0% for balances below the Tier 2 threshold.\\n  - Tier 2 APY: 4.5% for balances at or above the Tier 2 threshold.\\n\\n### Withdrawal flexibility\\n- Increased access with up to 15 free withdrawals per month.\\n\\n### ATM fee support\\n- Receive ATM fee rebates up to 25 each month.\\n\\n### Statement delivery\\n- Paper statements are available for Silver Plus Account holders.\\n- The monthly paper statement fee is $0.00. You can enable paper statements in your account settings.\\n- Paperless statements are NOT required for this account (unlike Green Account (savings) which requires paperless).\\n\\n### Relationship benefits\\n- Earn an additional relationship APY bonus of 0.025% when you qualify under the relationship criteria.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEeXpr5A6InWVwRNq53GtSN7QSRjOyDbRevYLxQRPlJlb8ukSMhVcgZDAJlhJ6QXc8CecHgEkOpXjwHY6uZFFTSq9njf2wdtOmwpDEz44jPzb5knF1_oxB6h9xw7NZ5BDgQNgYWeW-d9KoQRqKECpJX7VlxoPLQFv3SKo7qMebFcgaB9LVr_RCPpv8pZSYXhgS79q_mfvAmPmd9_-DQzLCk6r18n8M17i5pwrinmnVLny4d-ksZwDnqyHfdreYdL5gzl_ZWSrbwT-Wtt_sHmVG5EKSiLwpP9OA9WeBWsAHfo2EBtInFfoMAE8FMZGgVdpp7IvhEWBw15mUyMMazGNP1j4I0v97qp687kvFF_LLFf-GDGKhVKuOOAGNk85NiFLvxZgi4NAbAVFa85J4E15fW3thGr9QrEZg2W7byqVAcwVt94vkGBrFfivnQyxAUEBHGVNOpg162r_CDxaPF8ggVgJ5BDSLl27oln4DttxP8dj6Yr4Pp3GzccEj8Q668olYNDQxy8qOQufD7wJHV8rX_sfXcoUsmTakibooY9cZLJcbO3LJY0DdyOD9TEvMRpYCcAj3qUEsGWppwffxX4qoNm5A4kHuorSfRQH4TyEez2BieSJDfz8TtND3TaVhqOiYU_RtniOCTFD3BXvW0HY_4O8V19N8y_0o604cwOLBY09DxwMeoGURGvqI0BYdU15u9WMh4wVWU5LC5RoGi6EhVRKTfH4uOP39WTQbcI5SJlZzvREIv0dM9v3x4UO3wCFRVCad72vNu9N-4aamGQaYCpGS4OBE6unm3c-1Avj4-vtCbS8TFkOkhRR1krj4fJXZ5RDFA1vMHvBEfeeN5SAV7s4h23MCY5ixUYynJYnEZB2LfB4x9HmchF3q9QKkGfaJhOGDcVsbrEFhN_IMoAAhJgVjK3x0Q14rDX3VA2yV1kXTq3E1H3IB7dU4P97Xc0Je2aDJhdL3WbF0IKiqFuFsc57GzD1tXPHLgMCYtRJMCsOR-1lmJya5IjMeQkkiY-s8ZhlNsfzdbW66KLatRnUpF8BDKbLFQo3oWZyh_auZ7FYGC4xYyVF8c20NW6YDIaSRhBIuiPtJzfitdTmTndx3KLtHnXWva3WeCRs8N3qTV6SFAD_a6nRCChnrae4LXiL0CsJbGakylp8-P6-V8NsXmxvnDFHS66DZWF-KyyqIcwIIoAopz5v-CBEqRjz7ZSFuM78y-B1aS-5YsCrScGT5Ku3z8yjhOHiS_d6hkzX6YqRKjJuxNIlUGaT2KmYBQbbgM6VLQYu0Z9XLFTGRausUjX92PrDA-pbu6qrT7QxVYSeDE2DdAMFoexfUelStaqJZhUTrPRBnvCZloYKfpb003Z_a9D4hfi7LuPvWzEGWL8Sm4qu24lJ_Zg9SG8DjFm_0CmEYJmKlFQ0-E5JdfdsQ27osq9NzsBgUALXRr6pzlCFHuq0TSFe4s2d4ijPp87QYYBLf1uNv7CnJmLh6UNzg6nw0XoWNvCNN3qwQb7KhN7osSviw8usJOmoyVucyKUuXhI3k6kHdQl2Jl7D1pkJAQZixNuMgEDAdPn3zUD3Lgil5qVT8zp6iAKUElmp6QxMH04wEZPkwavVg-vRAV7EB6h-KaDbuIGHdoz6F1zRDpfDT1sBe-Sy2a2ycA_H1wv5GRA24Hzz5BV5jTKKafemprZvmmafzc6OVpZNkl4tzQRK4kH52eaqiy0kUZD-LurchdpmaTvvBW6OlgAut4ukOGyrhkAajzcTbBWCRkn8aljlqAIAweStqSmvIwrhIz4G06E44EVyg9yparxtLfN43vWah1O9dM_C5qZE67wnHHy3BzeHJN2e9nTLoHT7dvtgm3SrAiZcs3B0xJe-O38H1GpCgtinWnSm9fci8f1n4GvxeJ6Y9oLaX22sFDQog4bRvnpclkJCuehlKWrpapMSDw-2AaFFFBWuhFz_SGAGKkf4q50AtiTjcAoD-2NJbcVCo7FtEu0-kHMmQC3DZ8vHOielw==\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47915fac87d1a89ee3db26af553f\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Exploring card options**\\n\\nI’m considering various credit card tiers like Silver, Gold, and possibly Bronze or Diamond cards, and their unlimited benefits. There’s a lot of information that can be contradictory, especially concerning arithmetic and limits. The user hasn’t mentioned a new credit card, but it seems they might qualify for Gold rewards, which could fit their needs. Also, I want to ensure I account for any potential savings requirements tied to higher tiers without excess fees. I’ll need to do some specific research here.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"personal savings account unlimited withdrawals no excess withdrawal fee\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_qjNuvlWxy6FlXtcCn7GpkTMI\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc4796fac487d18c42d25875828222\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Silver Plus Account specifications requirements fees withdrawal compounding\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_kQRzgnFf3FxOy1Du5OWdVs2W\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc4796fae087d185cf5dfca7c18b99\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"savings frequent withdrawals unlimited card holder benefits minimum balance\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_IZCEg1bAr5mNsh1NB7QNWWZu\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc4796faec87d1984d50c54ba1d051\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_qjNuvlWxy6FlXtcCn7GpkTMI\",\"output\":\"1. Bronze Saver Account: Withdrawal limits explained\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_bronze_saver_account_008\\n   Score: 20.3305\\n   Content: ## Your monthly limit\\n- You are allowed up to 12 free withdrawals each month.\\n\\n## Fees after the limit\\n- Each withdrawal that exceeds 12 in a month will incur an excess withdrawal fee of $3.00.\\n\\n## What typically counts as a withdrawal\\n- Transfers from your savings to external banks via ACH\\n- Outgoing wire transfers\\n- Internal transfers from savings to other accounts\\n- Cash withdrawals initiated against this account\\n\\n## Tips to avoid excess withdrawal fees\\n- Consolidate multiple small transfers into fewer withdrawals when appropriate.\\n- Plan recurring payments to stay within 12 per month.\\n- Monitor your activity near the end of each statement cycle to avoid unintentional overages.\\n\\n2. Bluest Account exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_003\\n   Score: 18.0016\\n   Content: ## What you get with Bluest Account\\n\\n- Higher yield on your checking balance: 2.25% APY\\n- Complimentary domestic outgoing wires each month: 10\\n- Incoming domestic wires at no charge: $0.00\\n- Dedicated personal banker assigned: Yes\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates, up to: $50\\n- Complimentary personal check orders per year: 3\\n- Safe deposit box rental discount: 75.0%\\n- Stop payment requests at no charge: $0\\n- No foreign ATM withdrawal fees: $0.00\\n- Boosts on linked savings:\\n  - Silver Savings APY boost: 0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings APY boost: 0.7%\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Included |\\n|---|---|\\n| Checking APY | 2.25% |\\n| Free domestic outgoing wires (per month) | 10 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Dedicated personal banker | Yes |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly cap) | $50 |\\n| Complimentary check orders (per year) | 3 |\\n| Safe deposit box discount | 75.0% |\\n| Stop payment fee | $0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Silver Savings APY boost | 0.45% |\\n| Bronze Savings APY boost | 0.7% |\\n\\n## Referral rewards\\n\\nShare the Bluest experience and earn rewards:\\n- Referrer bonus: $75 per successful referral\\n- New member bonus: $50 for the person you refer\\n- Annual limit: 8 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n- Qualifying requirement: Referred person must deposit $2,000 within 90 days\\n- Eligibility: Referrers must have established their Rho-Bank checking relationship at least 60 days prior.\\n\\n## How to use your benefits\\n\\n### Complimentary wire transfers\\n- Send up to 10 domestic wire transfers per calendar month at no charge.\\n- Incoming domestic wires post with a $0.00 fee.\\n\\n### Dedicated personal banker\\n- A dedicated banker is assigned to your account (Yes). Use this single point of contact for complex transactions, expedited support, and account planning.\\n\\n### ATM fee rebates\\n- When you incur third-party ATM fees, you are rebated up to $50 per monthly statement cycle.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Withdraw from ATMs abroad with no Rho-Bank fee: $0.00. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n### Complimentary check orders\\n- Place up to 3 personal check orders each year at no cost.\\n\\n### Safe deposit box discount\\n- Receive a 75.0% discount on an eligible safe deposit box rental.\\n\\n### Stop payments\\n- Submit stop payment requests with a waived fee of $0.\\n\\n### Enhanced yields\\n- Earn 2.25% APY on your Bluest Account balance.\\n- Link eligible savings to activate boosts:\\n  - Silver Savings: +0.45%\\n  - Bronze Savings: +0.7%\\n\\n3. Why am I being charged a fee on my Bronze Account?\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_bronze_account_005\\n   Score: 17.9126\\n   Content: ## First, rule out monthly maintenance fees\\n- The Bronze Savings Account has a monthly maintenance fee of $0.00 and a minimum balance requirement of $0. If the monthly maintenance fee is $0, you will not be charged a monthly maintenance fee, regardless of your balance.\\n\\n## Common reasons you may see a fee\\n- Excess withdrawal activity: After 6 withdrawals in a monthly cycle, each additional withdrawal may incur an excess withdrawal fee of $3.00.\\n- Paper statement delivery: If you are enrolled in paper statements, a paper statement fee of $2.00 may apply each month you receive a paper statement.\\n\\n## How to verify the fee\\n- Review your recent transactions and look for line items labeled as excess withdrawal fees or paper statement fees.\\n- Count the number of withdrawals in your current cycle to see if you exceeded 6.\\n- Check your statement delivery preference; switch to digital statements to avoid the $2.00 paper statement fee.\\n\\n## If you still have questions\\n- Compare the fee description on your statement with the categories above.\\n- Contact support with the transaction date and description for clarification on the specific charge.\\n\\n4. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 16.3090\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n5. Silver Saver Account: What Happens If I Exceed Withdrawal Limits?\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_saver_account_003\\n   Score: 15.5161\\n   Content: ## Your monthly limit and fees\\n\\n| Item | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly free withdrawals | 6 |\\n| Fee for each excess withdrawal | $5.00 |\\n\\n### After you reach the limit\\n- Each additional withdrawal in the same calendar month incurs a $5.00 charge at posting.\\n- The charge appears as a separate line item on your activity and statement.\\n\\n### What typically counts as a withdrawal\\n- External transfers out\\n- ACH debits you authorize to other institutions\\n- ATM or in-branch cash withdrawals\\n- Internal transfers moving funds out of this account\\n\\n### Ways to avoid excess withdrawal fees\\n- Consolidate multiple payments into a single transfer when appropriate.\\n- Use internal transfers only when necessary.\\n- Plan recurring payments to stay within 6 each month.\\n\\n6. Platinum Savings Account: Complete Guide\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_platinum_account_001\\n   Score: 15.2321\\n   Content: ## Balance requirements\\n- Maintain at least $50,000 to preserve Platinum benefits.\\n- If your balance dips below $50,000, a monthly maintenance fee of $25.00 may apply until you restore the required balance.\\n\\n## Earnings\\n- Your account earns 6.5% APY on the balance you maintain.\\n\\n## Withdrawals and transfers\\n- Monthly withdrawal limit: -1 (for Platinum, this indicates unlimited withdrawals).\\n- Domestic wire transfer fees waived: Yes.\\n\\n### Tips for smooth transfers\\n- For time‑sensitive disbursements, consider a domestic wire since fees are waived and settlement is typically faster than standard external transfers.\\n- Always confirm recipient details before sending, as wires generally cannot be reversed.\\n\\n## Concierge banking\\n- Dedicated personal banker available: Yes.\\n- How to use it:\\n  - Request tailored support for complex transactions or financial planning within your account's secure messaging.\\n  - Ask for proactive account check‑ins or portfolio reviews based on your preferences.\\n\\n## Day‑to‑day management\\n- Set balance alerts so you stay above $50,000.\\n- If you anticipate a large withdrawal, consider timing additional deposits to maintain your required balance and avoid the $25.00 charge.\\n\\n7. Green Account (savings): EcoCard holder exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_009\\n   Score: 14.5013\\n   Content: ## EcoCard holder benefits overview\\n\\nGreen Account (savings) holders who also have an EcoCard receive enhanced benefits that make eco-conscious banking even more rewarding. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 7 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 8 + 7 = 15 withdrawals per month. You also receive 20 in ATM fee rebates monthly. Combined with the existing 0.5% bonus APY for EcoCard holders on top of the base 4.0% rate, this creates a comprehensive eco-friendly savings experience with maximum flexibility.\\n\\n## What you get as an EcoCard holder\\n\\n- Increased monthly free withdrawals: 8 + 7 = 15 total free withdrawals per month\\n- ATM fee rebates: up to $20 in rebates each month\\n- Rate boost: 0.5% bonus APY on top of the base 4.0% rate (example total: 4.75%)\\n\\n## Increased free withdrawals\\n\\n- Your free withdrawal allowance increases by 7 each month, for a total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Examples:\\n  - 10 withdrawals in a month: all 10 are free.\\n  - 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n  - More than 15 withdrawals in a month: any withdrawals beyond 15 are not free.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You receive up to $20 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- If total ATM operator fees in a month exceed $20, the excess amount is not rebated.\\n- Tip: Keep your receipts or review your statements to track how much of the $20 monthly cap you have used.\\n\\n## Bonus APY for EcoCard holders\\n\\n- Your Green Account earns the base 4.0% APY plus a 0.5% bonus when you hold an EcoCard.\\n- Example: 4.0% + 0.5% = 4.75% APY.\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 8 + 7 = 15\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: $20\\n- APY boost: 4.0% base + 0.5% bonus\\n\\n8. Silver Plus Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_001\\n   Score: 14.4743\\n   Content: ## Account parameters\\n\\n| Item | Detail |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $1,000 |\\n| Ongoing minimum balance | $2,500 |\\n| Interest compounding | daily |\\n| Tier 2 balance threshold | $15,000 |\\n| Free withdrawals per month | 15 |\\n\\n### Opening and maintaining your account\\n- Fund your new account with at least $1,000 to open it.\\n- Keep your balance at or above $2,500 to meet the ongoing requirement.\\n\\n### Interest structure\\n- Interest is compounded daily to help maximize earnings.\\n- Balances at or above $15,000 qualify for Tier 2 interest; lower balances earn the Tier 1 rate.\\n\\n### Withdrawal access\\n- You have up to 15 free withdrawals each month.\\n- Transactions beyond this free limit may be subject to an excess withdrawal fee per our fee schedule.\\n\\n9. Why am I being charged a fee on my Bronze Saver Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_bronze_saver_account_003\\n   Score: 14.1920\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you may see a fee\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: The Bronze Saver monthly maintenance fee is $0.00. If you see a line item labeled as a maintenance fee, confirm whether it reflects an adjustment or a different service charge.\\n- Excess withdrawals: If you make more than 12 withdrawals in a statement cycle, an excess withdrawal fee of $3.00 applies to each additional withdrawal.\\n- Paper statements: If you elect paper statements, a paper statement fee of $3.00 may appear on your statement for that cycle.\\n\\n## How to confirm the fee type on your statement\\n- Check the description next to the charge; look for terms such as “Excess withdrawal fee” or “Paper statement fee.”\\n- Compare the posting date to your recent activity to see which transaction triggered the fee.\\n\\n## Tips to avoid fees\\n- Keep withdrawals within 12 per month.\\n- Enroll in e-statements if you want to avoid the paper statement fee of $3.00.\\n- Monitor your monthly activity and plan transfers to reduce the chance of triggering excess withdrawal fees.\\n\\n10. Internal: Opening Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_002\\n   Score: 13.9058\\n   Content: ## Scope and Focus\\n\\nProcedure for opening personal savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one active Rho-Bank checking account, 3) Cannot have more than 5 personal savings accounts, 4) Must not have any accounts in collections or with negative balances, 5) Must have held their checking account for at least 14 days. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer, 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account (note: account_class must use the full official name ending with 'Account', e.g., 'Silver Plus Account', 'Gold Account'), 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements (Internal Checklist)\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified in our systems.\\n- Customer has at least one active Rho-Bank checking account.\\n- Customer currently holds fewer than 5 personal savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts in collections and no negative balances.\\n- The customer’s checking account tenure is at least 14 days.\\n\\nDo not proceed if any item above is not met.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify identity\\n- Authenticate the customer and confirm identity verification status on file.\\n\\n2) Check eligibility\\n- Confirm an active checking account exists and meets the 14-day tenure requirement.\\n- Count existing personal savings accounts; ensure the customer is below the 5 limit.\\n- Review account status; there must be no collections activity and no negative balances.\\n\\n3) Confirm account selection\\n- Discuss available personal savings account options with the customer.\\n- Capture the exact account_class string. It must be the full official name ending with “Account” (for example, “Silver Plus Account”, “Gold Account”).\\n\\n4) Open the savings account (agent action)\\n- Use the open_bank_account_4821 tool with account_type set to 'savings' and the confirmed account_class.\\n\\n5) Arrange opening deposit\\n- Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now.\\n  - If yes: use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount from the customer’s checking account to the newly opened savings account.\\n  - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n6) Confirm completion\\n- Provide the new account details and confirm the funding status or the funding deadline.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Usage (Internal Only)\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not ask the customer to call tools or provide tool parameters.\\n\\n- Tool: open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n  - When to call: After steps 1–3, once eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected an account_class.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - user_id: the authenticated customer’s user identifier.\\n    - account_type: 'savings' for personal savings accounts.\\n    - account_class: the full official account name ending with 'Account' exactly as confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Creates a new personal savings account for the customer.\\n\\n- Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n  - When to call: In step 5, only if the customer authorizes an immediate transfer for the opening deposit.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - source_account_id: the customer's Rho-Bank checking account to be debited.\\n    - destination_account_id: the newly opened personal savings account to be credited.\\n    - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Moves funds from checking to savings to complete the opening deposit.\\n\\n## Decision Points and Handling\\n\\n- Exceeds savings account limit: If the customer already has 5 personal savings accounts, do not open a new one. Inform the customer they have reached the maximum.\\n- Insufficient checking tenure: If the checking account has been open fewer than 14 days, advise the customer when they will become eligible.\\n- Collections or negative balances: Resolve these issues first; do not proceed until all accounts are in good standing.\\n- Customer defers funding: Clearly communicate the 30-day funding window and the consequence of closure if unfunded. Document the acknowledgment in the interaction notes.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_kQRzgnFf3FxOy1Du5OWdVs2W\",\"output\":\"1. Bronze Saver Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_bronze_saver_account_002\\n   Score: 17.0921\\n   Content: ## Specifications\\n| Item | Details |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $0 |\\n| Interest compounding frequency | daily |\\n| Linked Rho-Bank business checking required | Yes |\\n\\n## Requirements guidance\\n- Ensure a linked Rho-Bank business checking account remains active if Yes is required for your setup.\\n- Confirm your compounding preference is set to daily in your account details.\\n- Verify the initial funding meets or exceeds $0.\\n\\n2. Silver Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_001\\n   Score: 16.8644\\n   Content: ## Key specifications\\n\\n| Specification | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $500 |\\n| Ongoing minimum balance | $1,000 |\\n| Free withdrawals per statement cycle | 10 |\\n| Interest compounding | daily |\\n| Balance threshold for higher APY tier | $10,000 |\\n\\n## Requirements to open and maintain\\n- Fund at least $500 when you open the account.\\n- Maintain at least $1,000 each statement cycle to meet account requirements and avoid monthly fees.\\n- Track your withdrawal activity; transactions beyond 10 in a cycle may incur an excess withdrawal fee as described in your account disclosures.\\n- To qualify for the higher APY tier, keep your balance at or above $10,000.\\n- Interest is compounded daily.\\n\\n## Helpful tips\\n- Set up balance alerts to help you stay above $1,000 and, if desired, above $10,000.\\n- If you expect frequent withdrawals, consider spacing them to remain within 10 per cycle.\\n\\n3. Gold Plus Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_plus_account_001\\n   Score: 16.6475\\n   Content: ## Key specifications\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Opening deposit minimum | $10,000 |\\n| Minimum balance to maintain | $25,000 |\\n| Interest compounding frequency | daily |\\n| Automatic investment sweep threshold | $50,000 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 25 withdrawals |\\n\\n## Requirements to open and maintain\\n\\n- Fund the account with at least $10,000 at opening.\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $25,000 to keep account benefits active.\\n- When your end-of-day available balance exceeds $50,000, excess funds may be moved automatically to your linked investment account according to sweep settings.\\n- Plan cash flows so you do not exceed 25 withdrawals in a month.\\n- Interest accrues daily; keeping funds on deposit helps you benefit from compounding.\\n\\n\\n4. Silver Plus Saver vs Silver Saver Account: What is the difference?\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_plus_saver_002\\n   Score: 16.2250\\n   Content: ## Key differences when you upgrade to Silver Plus Saver\\n\\n### Monthly withdrawal allowance\\n- Silver Plus Saver provides up to 20 free withdrawals per month.\\n- This higher allowance is designed to support growing operational needs.\\n- If you exceed the free withdrawal allowance, standard excess-withdrawal handling applies per your account terms.\\n\\n### Tier 2 eligibility threshold\\n- On Silver Plus Saver, you become eligible for the higher APY tier once your balance reaches $25,000.\\n- Hitting this threshold allows you to earn the elevated tier rate for the days your balance qualifies.\\n- Silver Saver uses a different threshold disclosed in that account’s terms; the Silver Plus Saver threshold above applies specifically to your upgraded account.\\n\\n5. Silver Plus: Differences from Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_002\\n   Score: 14.9225\\n   Content: ## What changes with Silver Plus\\n\\n### Tiered APY\\n- Silver Plus offers tiered APY with two levels:\\n  - Tier 1 APY: 3.0% for balances below the Tier 2 threshold.\\n  - Tier 2 APY: 4.5% for balances at or above the Tier 2 threshold.\\n\\n### Withdrawal flexibility\\n- Increased access with up to 15 free withdrawals per month.\\n\\n### ATM fee support\\n- Receive ATM fee rebates up to 25 each month.\\n\\n### Statement delivery\\n- Paper statements are available for Silver Plus Account holders.\\n- The monthly paper statement fee is $0.00. You can enable paper statements in your account settings.\\n- Paperless statements are NOT required for this account (unlike Green Account (savings) which requires paperless).\\n\\n### Relationship benefits\\n- Earn an additional relationship APY bonus of 0.025% when you qualify under the relationship criteria.\\n\\n6. Internal: Business Savings Account Promotion - October 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_016\\n   Score: 14.4893\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 10/12/2025 TO 11/12/2025: When recommending business savings accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Gold Plus Saver should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Silver Plus Saver should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Gold Plus Saver nor Silver Plus Saver meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our investment-focused and enhanced-tier business savings offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n7. Internal: Business Savings Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_015\\n   Score: 13.9537\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business savings accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Gold Saver Account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Silver Plus Saver should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Gold Saver Account nor Silver Plus Saver meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our premium and enhanced-tier business savings offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n8. Internal: Closing Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_006\\n   Score: 13.6447\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Bronze Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $20 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 1 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Silver Account, Silver Plus Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $35 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 5 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Gold Account, Gold Plus Account, Gold Years Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $75 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 10 days\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Platinum Account, Platinum Plus Account, Diamond Elite Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $150 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval before proceeding.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n9. Green Account (savings) specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_001\\n   Score: 13.3930\\n   Content: ## Key specifications\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $100 |\\n| Ongoing minimum balance | $500 |\\n| Maximum free withdrawals per month | 8 |\\n| Interest compounding frequency | daily |\\n| Paperless statements required | Yes |\\n| Debit card made from recycled ocean plastic | Yes |\\n\\n### Requirements to open\\n- Fund the account with at least $100.\\n- Enroll in paperless statements, as indicated by Yes.\\n\\n### Ongoing maintenance\\n- Keep your balance at or above $500.\\n- Plan withdrawals to stay within 8 each month.\\n\\n### Interest handling\\n- Interest is compounded daily.\\n\\n### Card materials\\n- Your debit card is made from recycled ocean plastic: Yes.\\n\\n10. Silver Plus Account: Credit Card APY Bonuses\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_009\\n   Score: 13.2099\\n   Content: ## Credit card APY bonuses for Silver Plus Account holders\\n\\nHolding certain Rho-Bank credit cards provides bonus APY on your Silver Plus Account balance. These bonuses are automatically applied when you hold both the credit card and savings account under the same customer profile.\\n\\n### Available credit card APY bonuses\\n\\n| Credit Card | APY Bonus |\\n|---|---|\\n| Bronze Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Silver Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Gold Rewards Card | +0.2% |\\n| Platinum Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Diamond Elite Card | +0.4% |\\n| EcoCard | +0.45% |\\n| Green Rewards Card | +0.1% |\\n| Crypto-Cash Back Card | +0% |\\n\\n### How to qualify\\n\\n1. Open or maintain a Silver Plus Account.\\n2. Hold an eligible Rho-Bank credit card under the same customer profile.\\n3. The APY bonus is automatically applied to your Silver Plus Account earnings.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_IZCEg1bAr5mNsh1NB7QNWWZu\",\"output\":\"1. Gold Account: Gold Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_013\\n   Score: 16.1316\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nGold Account holders who also have a Gold Rewards Card receive exclusive benefits that make the account more accessible. The standard minimum balance requirement of $10,000 is reduced to $5,000 for Gold Rewards Card holders. Additionally, you receive a 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base 5.5% rate. Combined with the existing 30 ATM fee rebates and 20 monthly withdrawals, Gold Rewards Card holders enjoy a premium savings experience with lower balance requirements.\\n\\n## Benefits summary for Gold Rewards Card holders\\n\\n- Reduced minimum balance: $5,000 (down from $10,000)\\n- Relationship bonus APY: 0.025% on top of the base 5.5%\\n- ATM fee rebates: Up to $30 per month\\n- Monthly withdrawals: Up to 20 per month\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Gold Rewards Card holder value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $5,000 (standard: $10,000) |\\n| APY rate | 5.5% + 0.025% |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly max) | $30 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 20 |\\n\\n## Reduced minimum balance\\n\\n- If you hold a Gold Rewards Card, your required minimum balance to maintain the Gold Account is automatically reduced to $5,000.\\n- The standard minimum balance for the Gold Account remains $10,000, but the override applies as long as your Gold Rewards Card is active and associated with your account.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Without the card: Minimum balance requirement is $10,000.\\n- With the card: Minimum balance requirement is $5,000.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- Your Gold Account earns the base 5.5% APY.\\n- As a Gold Rewards Card holder, you receive an additional 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base rate.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Base APY: 5.5%\\n- Relationship bonus APY: +0.025%\\n- Total APY with the bonus: 6.0%\\n\\nNotes:\\n- The relationship bonus is additive to the base rate; it is not a multiplier.\\n- The bonus applies while your Gold Rewards Card remains active and associated with your Gold Account.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates and monthly withdrawals\\n\\n- You continue to receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- You are allowed up to 20 withdrawals per month.\\n\\n## How to confirm your benefits are active\\n\\n- Check your account details to verify:\\n  - The minimum balance requirement displays as $5,000.\\n  - The APY displays as 5.5% plus a 0.025% relationship bonus.\\n  - Your monthly limits show up to $30 in ATM fee rebates and up to 20 withdrawals.\\n\\n2. Green Account (savings): EcoCard holder exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_009\\n   Score: 14.3801\\n   Content: ## EcoCard holder benefits overview\\n\\nGreen Account (savings) holders who also have an EcoCard receive enhanced benefits that make eco-conscious banking even more rewarding. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 7 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 8 + 7 = 15 withdrawals per month. You also receive 20 in ATM fee rebates monthly. Combined with the existing 0.5% bonus APY for EcoCard holders on top of the base 4.0% rate, this creates a comprehensive eco-friendly savings experience with maximum flexibility.\\n\\n## What you get as an EcoCard holder\\n\\n- Increased monthly free withdrawals: 8 + 7 = 15 total free withdrawals per month\\n- ATM fee rebates: up to $20 in rebates each month\\n- Rate boost: 0.5% bonus APY on top of the base 4.0% rate (example total: 4.75%)\\n\\n## Increased free withdrawals\\n\\n- Your free withdrawal allowance increases by 7 each month, for a total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Examples:\\n  - 10 withdrawals in a month: all 10 are free.\\n  - 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n  - More than 15 withdrawals in a month: any withdrawals beyond 15 are not free.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You receive up to $20 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- If total ATM operator fees in a month exceed $20, the excess amount is not rebated.\\n- Tip: Keep your receipts or review your statements to track how much of the $20 monthly cap you have used.\\n\\n## Bonus APY for EcoCard holders\\n\\n- Your Green Account earns the base 4.0% APY plus a 0.5% bonus when you hold an EcoCard.\\n- Example: 4.0% + 0.5% = 4.75% APY.\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 8 + 7 = 15\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: $20\\n- APY boost: 4.0% base + 0.5% bonus\\n\\n3. Business Bronze Saver: Complete Guide\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_bronze_saver_account_001\\n   Score: 11.9752\\n   Content: ## Account Snapshot\\n\\n- APY: 2.0%\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $0.00\\n- Minimum opening deposit: $0\\n- Ongoing minimum balance: Not required\\n- Withdrawals: Generous monthly limits designed for frequent access\\n\\n## Opening Your Account\\n\\n1. Start your application online and select Business Bronze Saver.\\n2. Review and accept the account terms and disclosures.\\n3. Fund the account with at least $0 (you can open with $0 and add funds anytime).\\n4. Set your preferred funding source for future deposits and transfers.\\n\\nTips:\\n- If you plan to fund later, set up a reminder so your balance begins earning 2.0% as soon as funds arrive.\\n- Add authorized users who will help manage deposits and withdrawals.\\n\\n## Funding and Earning Interest\\n\\n- You earn 2.0% on your available balance.\\n- Make deposits via transfer from your business banking source of choice.\\n- Larger, less frequent deposits generally help you maintain a higher average balance, which increases your total interest earned at the same APY.\\n\\nBest practices:\\n- Schedule periodic transfers that match your cash-flow cycle (weekly, biweekly, or monthly).\\n- Keep funds in the account for as long as possible during the month to maximize interest at 2.0%.\\n\\n## APY Bonuses with Business Rewards Cards\\n\\nIf you hold an eligible Business Rewards Card, your APY increases by the corresponding bonus. The bonus is added to 2.0%.\\n\\n- Business Silver Rewards Card: 0.15% (approx. total APY 2.15%)\\n- Business Gold Rewards Card: 0.35% (approx. total APY 2.35%)\\n- Business Platinum Rewards Card: 0.65% (approx. total APY 2.65%)\\n\\nHow to apply the bonus:\\n- Ensure your card is active and in the same business profile as your savings account.\\n- The APY bonus reflects automatically once eligibility is recognized.\\n\\n## Managing Withdrawals\\n\\n- Initiate withdrawals through your online banking transfers.\\n- Plan multiple smaller withdrawals within the generous monthly limit if you foresee periodic cash needs.\\n- When moving larger sums, consider consolidating into fewer transfers to stay comfortably within the monthly allowance.\\n- Schedule withdrawals toward the end of your billing cycle when possible to keep funds earning 2.0% longer.\\n\\n## Example Earnings\\n\\nApproximate annual interest if your average balance remains constant:\\n\\n- $10,000 average balance\\n  - Base APY 2.0%: about $200/year\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card bonus: about $215/year\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card bonus: about $235/year\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card bonus: about $265/year\\n\\n- $25,000 average balance\\n  - Base APY 2.0%: about $500/year\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card bonus: about $537.50/year\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card bonus: about $587.50/year\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card bonus: about $662.50/year\\n\\nThese estimates assume the APY remains the same and the balance does not change during the period.\\n\\n## Common Questions\\n\\n- Is there a monthly maintenance fee?\\n  - No. The monthly maintenance fee is $0.00.\\n\\n- What is the minimum to open the account?\\n  - $0. You can open now and fund later.\\n\\n- How do the APY bonuses work with cards?\\n  - If you hold an eligible Business Rewards Card, your APY increases by the applicable bonus: 0.15%, 0.35%, or 0.65%.\\n\\n4. Gold Plus Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_plus_account_001\\n   Score: 11.1233\\n   Content: ## Key specifications\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Opening deposit minimum | $10,000 |\\n| Minimum balance to maintain | $25,000 |\\n| Interest compounding frequency | daily |\\n| Automatic investment sweep threshold | $50,000 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 25 withdrawals |\\n\\n## Requirements to open and maintain\\n\\n- Fund the account with at least $10,000 at opening.\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $25,000 to keep account benefits active.\\n- When your end-of-day available balance exceeds $50,000, excess funds may be moved automatically to your linked investment account according to sweep settings.\\n- Plan cash flows so you do not exceed 25 withdrawals in a month.\\n- Interest accrues daily; keeping funds on deposit helps you benefit from compounding.\\n\\n\\n5. Business Platinum Rewards Card: Premium Travel Benefits and Insurance Coverage\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_business_platinum_rewards_card_006\\n   Score: 10.6358\\n   Content: ## Airport Lounge Access\\n- Unlimited lounge visits included: Yes\\n\\n## Annual Travel Credits\\n- Annual travel credits available: $400\\n- Apply credits to eligible travel purchases as outlined in your benefits guide.\\n\\n## Travel Insurance\\n- Maximum coverage per trip: $62,500\\n- Use your card for eligible travel purchases to activate coverage.\\n- Keep receipts and confirmations; contact the claims administrator promptly after an incident.\\n\\n## Purchase Protection\\n- Maximum per claim: $17,500\\n- Coverage applies to eligible items purchased with your card and within the stated benefit window.\\n\\n## International Purchases\\n- Foreign transaction fee on international purchases: 0%\\n- Pay in local currency where appropriate to maximize acceptance and clarity of charges.\\n\\n6. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 10.6010\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n7. Silver Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_001\\n   Score: 10.1096\\n   Content: ## Key specifications\\n\\n| Specification | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $500 |\\n| Ongoing minimum balance | $1,000 |\\n| Free withdrawals per statement cycle | 10 |\\n| Interest compounding | daily |\\n| Balance threshold for higher APY tier | $10,000 |\\n\\n## Requirements to open and maintain\\n- Fund at least $500 when you open the account.\\n- Maintain at least $1,000 each statement cycle to meet account requirements and avoid monthly fees.\\n- Track your withdrawal activity; transactions beyond 10 in a cycle may incur an excess withdrawal fee as described in your account disclosures.\\n- To qualify for the higher APY tier, keep your balance at or above $10,000.\\n- Interest is compounded daily.\\n\\n## Helpful tips\\n- Set up balance alerts to help you stay above $1,000 and, if desired, above $10,000.\\n- If you expect frequent withdrawals, consider spacing them to remain within 10 per cycle.\\n\\n8. Gold Account: Credit Card APY Bonuses\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_014\\n   Score: 9.7996\\n   Content: ## Credit card APY bonuses for Gold Account holders\\n\\nHolding certain Rho-Bank credit cards provides bonus APY on your Gold Account balance. These bonuses are automatically applied when you hold both the credit card and savings account under the same customer profile.\\n\\n### Available credit card APY bonuses\\n\\n| Credit Card | APY Bonus |\\n|---|---|\\n| Bronze Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Silver Rewards Card | +0.2% |\\n| Gold Rewards Card | +0.025% |\\n| Platinum Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Diamond Elite Card | +0.3% |\\n| EcoCard | +0.6% |\\n| Green Rewards Card | +0.35% |\\n| Crypto-Cash Back Card | +0% |\\n\\n### Additional Gold Rewards Card benefits\\n\\nGold Rewards Card holders receive an additional benefit: the minimum balance requirement is reduced from $10,000 to $5,000.\\n\\n### How to qualify\\n\\n1. Open or maintain a Gold Account.\\n2. Hold an eligible Rho-Bank credit card under the same customer profile.\\n3. The APY bonus is automatically applied to your Gold Account earnings.\\n\\n9. True Blue Account: Interest and APY Explained\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_008\\n   Score: 9.7006\\n   Content: ## Your APY\\n- The account earns an Annual Percentage Yield (APY) of 2.0% on eligible balances.\\n\\n## How interest accrues\\n- Interest compounds daily, which increases the amount of interest credited over time compared to less frequent compounding.\\n\\n## Crediting\\n- Interest is calculated on collected balances and credited according to the account terms.\\n\\n## Maximizing what you earn\\n- Keep funds in the account continuously so more of your balance benefits from daily compounding at 2.0%.\\n- Avoid unnecessary transfers out of the account if you aim to maximize compounding effects.\\n\\n10. Silver Plus Saver Account: Same-day ACH and interest compounding\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_plus_saver_006\\n   Score: 9.1624\\n   Content: ## Same-day ACH availability\\n- Same-day ACH is available for this account tier: Yes.\\n\\n### How to request same-day ACH\\n- When scheduling an ACH transfer, select the same-day delivery option if available for your transfer type and destination.\\n- Ensure sufficient available funds before submission to avoid reversals.\\n- Monitor your transfer activity for confirmation that the same-day request was accepted.\\n\\n## Interest compounding\\n- Interest on your Silver Plus Saver account is compounded daily.\\n\\n### Practical tips\\n- If you anticipate frequent time-sensitive payments, enable notifications so you can choose same-day when it suits your cash flow.\\n- Keep your balance steady to maximize the benefits of interest compounded daily.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEej64Ny6de6aeK5EXIIncCcaT-Wgs7n0CbNSO56LKQeTeiJ6Obm158o1CI4qXkj77wDb2mUNDmNKmHEK7FfARKdMGokX04VcA70vQRgaxh0eFi0O7XHuSKG43gJCHFhxcmnxY4fCUpVjADVzNZO0xvpJeQRTv1NztbcqFw4yqavgzCmBjEcSVNYQMNKEu4I_hfzC5acNvfGnOFR1BCnK6PFWZF5PKImDMBJ_RhAABlGtcA1CdNuZsn3IwAL0K650VzhQst55hSBZ09k3ddb1O32znW0bMm8adYsBVE6WvdS8lnk3dSjDdZPoYBVjW7HJ3p_jrtkFSsfju4JYPoxvSn9hHP-5muWDdAbyih0fgafKOH9aHxji64i5KMpMmosQBIueZga2meWv16-VnKKOa-vHYt05M5DdCn9mrtw_bZP0npuXdCcgSmzfk1mPC9v_sv0vKkdILAJ_MUE_DfBuKp4v1qK2ko_1yBwLpoyA3aaZ4MWl9R8LqDHS4yx0QpLy1N_VdBsdS5Msl7nlcP2LwZUo7MIWxWYZoxulMfyUADuEAgXoKDLdqgIIFT186_XDoejHr6egJ4Kz6LOa4T1u90x0C_-SLUBJIXRYxYXPi-SN7N7gjqhHKWfh3QoA3rmGGsPXsCxlwCpRD6TZ9V-LrKM6M4rHkoe_UK6QAAoHbIGmEU4iqFMtu9WX1F44h33gPjq0R77BxfvfUdDtF1Ms36gDP_vp-d4zHDlchH37YmRE4tBOaM4hShGXAVPQtBSXRsKNpLjWtfzzj0tp-x1QDtCPIMu2CY-iro1dPR1LoeJ426IEyVW23KByPXxbaOjaoPQJYS0eqVCOZNnG2g4ZUeEzQ-qC737RT-tvTirKGtdftqcNlgSlOnh-MLefr09lZsKo-3kB-0GFgT1grL91ZEkC2-7cJVGQXSuFNxL8-91MLaMwOOg29jhJ9FMBZYaQVyjmovJ_J6IGDISc_OCr1jSnoXnZ2zDuBZksXyB7DsLymBy6sAFvqjK94CDPxS7CP28So2-Zn-vF6p2suSw3OfCaNYr37LDUezl1C2YBryIfGk4F8uVZ9FtQTm4efESgVloXM27kPkP4TGw4rIxYz_2aagaWysZjcHk2g16IXaLCat4S1mbiRVBOxwCfoT7cErAfDdGbhEyuK5WVjt8RVAaMBFLbSESlK49sKutmU2G28uaqf3MLBJZs6B9ue9cc6X1xqjPtoWPwyiQkTuUGgOyeHUlC7CRvP_jVRvgUzeli8LdF2uh2_e2esv72cDOMAxnWNjh3xnmdqsTlM3-NqZehlFsL_y1LJtgs-AFF5PCevoHwjWNef6kD3LTyTHobLu-ras0FoqnanAgEtANyIsrI-D7_Ogdk8jMS1Quftdnvl7VnJsBSeh6EzSsmd-tam9pnFkvuO2Mor6DKGfoy62rMO5JzUdGBwg4Vv3CYKa3SSI=\",\"id\":\"rs_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47a0c3f487d1ae81eb225659e269\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Exploring Silver Plus options**\\n\\nI’m thinking about the five queries I used, and while none seem perfect, I’m considering if Silver Plus might allow withdrawals along with its rewards. Maybe there’s a special or frequent fee waiver available? I need to dig deeper into search terms related to Silver Plus benefits to find out more about the card options. I’m curious about whether I can find anything useful!\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Silver Plus Account free withdrawal fee waiver unlimited\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_vZqZ4qSlN97vcpY7bYQoNuaR\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47a3893c87d1a867b219a3000a06\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Gold Account withdrawals fees relationship bonus Green checking\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_r76c6GVqNJkeXJOCoQ2gdUlG\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47a3895087d1b4443266566f9bda\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Green Account savings fees environmental relationship bonus ATM\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_73Fz9RPzlQVx49NgmqYpHJ1t\",\"id\":\"fc_08d780c1cdf4eab9016abc47a3895887d1a5dff6c3b1761e0f\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_vZqZ4qSlN97vcpY7bYQoNuaR\",\"output\":\"1. Silver Plus Saver vs Silver Saver Account: What is the difference?\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_plus_saver_002\\n   Score: 20.7536\\n   Content: ## Key differences when you upgrade to Silver Plus Saver\\n\\n### Monthly withdrawal allowance\\n- Silver Plus Saver provides up to 20 free withdrawals per month.\\n- This higher allowance is designed to support growing operational needs.\\n- If you exceed the free withdrawal allowance, standard excess-withdrawal handling applies per your account terms.\\n\\n### Tier 2 eligibility threshold\\n- On Silver Plus Saver, you become eligible for the higher APY tier once your balance reaches $25,000.\\n- Hitting this threshold allows you to earn the elevated tier rate for the days your balance qualifies.\\n- Silver Saver uses a different threshold disclosed in that account’s terms; the Silver Plus Saver threshold above applies specifically to your upgraded account.\\n\\n2. Silver Plus: Differences from Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_002\\n   Score: 19.4767\\n   Content: ## What changes with Silver Plus\\n\\n### Tiered APY\\n- Silver Plus offers tiered APY with two levels:\\n  - Tier 1 APY: 3.0% for balances below the Tier 2 threshold.\\n  - Tier 2 APY: 4.5% for balances at or above the Tier 2 threshold.\\n\\n### Withdrawal flexibility\\n- Increased access with up to 15 free withdrawals per month.\\n\\n### ATM fee support\\n- Receive ATM fee rebates up to 25 each month.\\n\\n### Statement delivery\\n- Paper statements are available for Silver Plus Account holders.\\n- The monthly paper statement fee is $0.00. You can enable paper statements in your account settings.\\n- Paperless statements are NOT required for this account (unlike Green Account (savings) which requires paperless).\\n\\n### Relationship benefits\\n- Earn an additional relationship APY bonus of 0.025% when you qualify under the relationship criteria.\\n\\n3. Silver Account: Platinum Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_009\\n   Score: 16.4104\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nSilver Account holders who also have a Platinum Rewards Card receive enhanced withdrawal privileges. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 5 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 10 + 5 = 15 withdrawals per month. This benefit is automatically applied when both accounts are linked under the same customer profile. Combined with the existing 15 ATM fee rebates and 0.025% relationship bonus, Platinum Rewards Card holders get an elevated Silver Account experience.\\n\\n## APY bonuses from credit cards\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.2%\\n- Diamond Elite Card: +0.25%\\n\\n## What you receive as a Platinum Rewards Card holder\\n\\n- Additional free withdrawals: +5 per month on top of your standard 10 free withdrawals\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 10 + 5 = 15\\n- ATM fee relief: Up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month\\n- Earnings boost: An additional 0.025% relationship bonus added to your APY when eligible\\n\\n## Activation and eligibility\\n\\n- The enhanced withdrawal limit is automatically applied when your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile.\\n- The 0.025% relationship bonus and 15 ATM fee rebates apply in the same profile-linked setup.\\n\\n### How to confirm your accounts are linked\\n\\n1. Sign in to Rho-Bank Online Banking or the mobile app.\\n2. Open your customer profile and review your list of accounts and cards.\\n3. Verify that your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card appear under the same customer profile.\\n4. If you do not see both products under one profile, consolidate them to a single profile or contact us for assistance.\\n\\n## Using your monthly withdrawal allowance\\n\\n- Counting method: Any transaction classified as a withdrawal under your Silver Account terms counts toward your monthly total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Cycle timing: Your free withdrawal count resets at the start of each monthly statement cycle.\\n- Beyond the limit: Transactions above your free monthly total may be subject to standard Silver Account withdrawal charges.\\n\\nExample:\\n- You make 12 withdrawals in a month: all 12 are free.\\n- You make 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n- You make 16 withdrawals in a month: the first 15 are free; the 16th may incur standard charges.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You are eligible for up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- Rebates apply after ATM fees post to your Silver Account; check your transaction history for the corresponding credit within the same month.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- When your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile, an additional 0.025% is added to your APY as a relationship bonus.\\n- The relationship bonus is reflected in your APY while eligibility is maintained.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting and tips\\n\\n- If you do not see the extra withdrawals or 0.025% reflected, confirm both products are under the same customer profile.\\n- Check that you are within the current monthly statement cycle for the added withdrawals to apply.\\n- Review your transaction history to verify ATM fee charges and corresponding rebates up to 15 for the month.\\n\\n4. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 14.7323\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n5. Silver Plus Account: Credit Card APY Bonuses\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_009\\n   Score: 13.2099\\n   Content: ## Credit card APY bonuses for Silver Plus Account holders\\n\\nHolding certain Rho-Bank credit cards provides bonus APY on your Silver Plus Account balance. These bonuses are automatically applied when you hold both the credit card and savings account under the same customer profile.\\n\\n### Available credit card APY bonuses\\n\\n| Credit Card | APY Bonus |\\n|---|---|\\n| Bronze Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Silver Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Gold Rewards Card | +0.2% |\\n| Platinum Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Diamond Elite Card | +0.4% |\\n| EcoCard | +0.45% |\\n| Green Rewards Card | +0.1% |\\n| Crypto-Cash Back Card | +0% |\\n\\n### How to qualify\\n\\n1. Open or maintain a Silver Plus Account.\\n2. Hold an eligible Rho-Bank credit card under the same customer profile.\\n3. The APY bonus is automatically applied to your Silver Plus Account earnings.\\n\\n6. Green Account (savings): EcoCard holder exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_009\\n   Score: 13.1509\\n   Content: ## EcoCard holder benefits overview\\n\\nGreen Account (savings) holders who also have an EcoCard receive enhanced benefits that make eco-conscious banking even more rewarding. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 7 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 8 + 7 = 15 withdrawals per month. You also receive 20 in ATM fee rebates monthly. Combined with the existing 0.5% bonus APY for EcoCard holders on top of the base 4.0% rate, this creates a comprehensive eco-friendly savings experience with maximum flexibility.\\n\\n## What you get as an EcoCard holder\\n\\n- Increased monthly free withdrawals: 8 + 7 = 15 total free withdrawals per month\\n- ATM fee rebates: up to $20 in rebates each month\\n- Rate boost: 0.5% bonus APY on top of the base 4.0% rate (example total: 4.75%)\\n\\n## Increased free withdrawals\\n\\n- Your free withdrawal allowance increases by 7 each month, for a total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Examples:\\n  - 10 withdrawals in a month: all 10 are free.\\n  - 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n  - More than 15 withdrawals in a month: any withdrawals beyond 15 are not free.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You receive up to $20 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- If total ATM operator fees in a month exceed $20, the excess amount is not rebated.\\n- Tip: Keep your receipts or review your statements to track how much of the $20 monthly cap you have used.\\n\\n## Bonus APY for EcoCard holders\\n\\n- Your Green Account earns the base 4.0% APY plus a 0.5% bonus when you hold an EcoCard.\\n- Example: 4.0% + 0.5% = 4.75% APY.\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 8 + 7 = 15\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: $20\\n- APY boost: 4.0% base + 0.5% bonus\\n\\n7. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 12.6627\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n8. Silver Plus Saver Account: Complete Guide\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_plus_saver_001\\n   Score: 12.6314\\n   Content: ## Eligibility and Minimum Balance\\n- You must maintain a minimum balance of $5,000 to keep the Silver Plus Saver account in good standing.\\n- If your balance is anticipated to dip below $5,000, consider timing deposits and withdrawals to avoid falling under the requirement.\\n\\n## Interest and APY Structure\\n- Balances below the tier 2 threshold earn 2.5% APY.\\n- Balances above the tier 2 threshold earn 4.0% APY.\\n\\n### Relationship APY Bonuses\\nIf you hold an eligible Business Rewards Card, an APY bonus is added to your base APY:\\n- Business Silver Rewards Card: +0.18% APY\\n- Business Gold Rewards Card: +0.38% APY\\n- Business Platinum Rewards Card: +0.62% APY\\n\\nThe bonus applies to the base APY for the balance tier you qualify for.\\n\\n### Example APYs With Relationship Bonuses\\nBelow are example total APYs when a relationship bonus applies:\\n\\n- Balance below tier 2 threshold (base 2.5%):\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card: 2.68% (2.5% + 0.18%)\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card: 2.88% (2.5% + 0.38%)\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card: 3.12% (2.5% + 0.62%)\\n\\n- Balance above tier 2 threshold (base 4.0%):\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card: 4.18% (4.0% + 0.18%)\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card: 4.38% (4.0% + 0.38%)\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card: 4.62% (4.0% + 0.62%)\\n\\n## Withdrawals and Transfers\\nSilver Plus Saver offers higher withdrawal limits and improved transfer capabilities compared to Silver Saver. To make the most of these enhancements:\\n- Plan large withdrawals in advance to ensure smooth processing.\\n- Use scheduled transfers for recurring payments to maintain your target balance above $5,000.\\n- For unusually large or time-sensitive transfers, initiate earlier in the business day to reduce the risk of delays.\\n\\n## Upgrading from Silver Saver\\nIf you are moving up from Silver Saver:\\n- Confirm you can maintain at least $5,000 in Silver Plus Saver.\\n- Request an upgrade through your online banking or by contacting support. Your balances will begin earning at the Silver Plus Saver rates as soon as the upgrade is completed.\\n\\n## How to Verify Your Current APY and Bonus\\n- In online banking, open the Silver Plus Saver account details to view:\\n  - Your current balance tier (below or above the tier 2 threshold)\\n  - Base APY for that tier (2.5% or 4.0%)\\n  - Any relationship APY bonus applied (e.g., 0.38%) \\n- Review after any balance change or card status update to confirm your effective APY.\\n\\n9. Silver Plus Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_001\\n   Score: 12.0949\\n   Content: ## Account parameters\\n\\n| Item | Detail |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $1,000 |\\n| Ongoing minimum balance | $2,500 |\\n| Interest compounding | daily |\\n| Tier 2 balance threshold | $15,000 |\\n| Free withdrawals per month | 15 |\\n\\n### Opening and maintaining your account\\n- Fund your new account with at least $1,000 to open it.\\n- Keep your balance at or above $2,500 to meet the ongoing requirement.\\n\\n### Interest structure\\n- Interest is compounded daily to help maximize earnings.\\n- Balances at or above $15,000 qualify for Tier 2 interest; lower balances earn the Tier 1 rate.\\n\\n### Withdrawal access\\n- You have up to 15 free withdrawals each month.\\n- Transactions beyond this free limit may be subject to an excess withdrawal fee per our fee schedule.\\n\\n10. Troubleshooting: Unexpected Charges on Cobalt Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_009\\n   Score: 12.0290\\n   Content: ## Identify the charge\\n- Review the exact transaction description on your statement or in your transaction history (e.g., “Monthly Maintenance Fee,” “Wire Transfer – Domestic,” “ATM Fee,” “International ATM Withdrawal Fee,” “Excess Transaction Fee”).\\n- Note the posting date, amount, and any memo or terminal/location details.\\n- Compare the posting date to your recent account activity (wires sent, ATM withdrawals, transaction volume, month-end).\\n\\n## Common Cobalt Blue charges that may appear\\n| Line item on statement | Why it appears | How to confirm | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your account did not meet the balance waiver requirement during the statement period. | Check the Fee Summary on your statement and verify whether your balance met $2,500 for the period. | $20.00 |\\n| Excess Transaction Fee | You exceeded your monthly free transaction limit. | Count your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your free allowance; the fee line often notes the number of excess items. | $0.25 per excess transaction |\\n| Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic | You initiated a domestic wire transfer. | Confirm a wire was submitted on or near the posting date in your transfer history. | $20.00 |\\n| ATM Fee – Out of Network | You used a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | Match the fee date to an ATM withdrawal at a non‑Rho terminal. Note: the ATM owner may also assess a separate surcharge. | $2.00 per ATM transaction |\\n| International ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at a foreign (international) ATM. | Match the fee date/location to an overseas ATM withdrawal. | 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $4.00 |\\n\\nNote: Cobalt Blue does not assess overdraft fees. If you see a charge that appears to be an overdraft fee, review the line’s exact description—it may correspond to one of the fees above. If still unclear, request a review.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting by charge type\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee posted unexpectedly\\n- Verify whether your account met the waiver balance requirement of $2,500 during the statement period.\\n- Check if the fee posted at or just after the statement cycle date.\\n- Compare your balance history for the full period; large debits near period‑end can affect waiver eligibility.\\n- If you believe you qualified for the waiver, request a fee review and include your statement period dates and balance evidence.\\n\\n### Excess Transaction Fee you didn’t anticipate\\n- Add up your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your plan’s free monthly transaction limit.\\n- Open the fee detail to see how many items were assessed at $0.25 each.\\n- If the count appears off, provide a list of the transactions you believe were miscounted when requesting a review.\\n\\n### Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic you didn’t expect\\n- Confirm whether a domestic wire was sent on the fee date (or one business day prior).\\n- Distinguish wires from other transfers by the transaction description (“Wire,” routing via Fedwire, etc.).\\n- If you did not authorize a wire, report immediately for investigation. Otherwise, the standard fee is $20.00.\\n\\n### ATM fees: domestic vs. international\\n- Out‑of‑network (domestic) ATM usage: Expect $2.00 per ATM transaction. This is separate from any surcharge by the ATM owner, which can appear as a separate line item.\\n- Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals: The fee is 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00. Example: for a withdrawal, multiply the amount by 2.5%; if that result is less than $4.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\n## Quick checklist before requesting a review\\n- Match the fee’s posting date to a specific action (wire, ATM withdrawal, month‑end, spike in transaction volume).\\n- Capture screenshots of:\\n  - The fee line item (showing date, amount, and description)\\n  - Any related transaction (wire confirmation, ATM withdrawal)\\n  - The relevant statement page (Fee Summary and balance history for the period)\\n- Briefly explain why the fee appears incorrect (e.g., you met $2,500 during the period, transaction count appears miscalculated, withdrawal was domestic vs. international, etc.).\\n\\n## Requesting a review or dispute\\n- Contact us as soon as you notice the charge.\\n- Include: account name, last 4 digits, statement period, fee date/amount/description, and your supporting screenshots or documents.\\n- We will investigate and correct any misapplied fees. If additional information is needed (e.g., to verify ATM location or wire authorization), we will follow up.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_r76c6GVqNJkeXJOCoQ2gdUlG\",\"output\":\"1. Gold Account: Gold Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_013\\n   Score: 20.0257\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nGold Account holders who also have a Gold Rewards Card receive exclusive benefits that make the account more accessible. The standard minimum balance requirement of $10,000 is reduced to $5,000 for Gold Rewards Card holders. Additionally, you receive a 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base 5.5% rate. Combined with the existing 30 ATM fee rebates and 20 monthly withdrawals, Gold Rewards Card holders enjoy a premium savings experience with lower balance requirements.\\n\\n## Benefits summary for Gold Rewards Card holders\\n\\n- Reduced minimum balance: $5,000 (down from $10,000)\\n- Relationship bonus APY: 0.025% on top of the base 5.5%\\n- ATM fee rebates: Up to $30 per month\\n- Monthly withdrawals: Up to 20 per month\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Gold Rewards Card holder value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $5,000 (standard: $10,000) |\\n| APY rate | 5.5% + 0.025% |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly max) | $30 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 20 |\\n\\n## Reduced minimum balance\\n\\n- If you hold a Gold Rewards Card, your required minimum balance to maintain the Gold Account is automatically reduced to $5,000.\\n- The standard minimum balance for the Gold Account remains $10,000, but the override applies as long as your Gold Rewards Card is active and associated with your account.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Without the card: Minimum balance requirement is $10,000.\\n- With the card: Minimum balance requirement is $5,000.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- Your Gold Account earns the base 5.5% APY.\\n- As a Gold Rewards Card holder, you receive an additional 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base rate.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Base APY: 5.5%\\n- Relationship bonus APY: +0.025%\\n- Total APY with the bonus: 6.0%\\n\\nNotes:\\n- The relationship bonus is additive to the base rate; it is not a multiplier.\\n- The bonus applies while your Gold Rewards Card remains active and associated with your Gold Account.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates and monthly withdrawals\\n\\n- You continue to receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- You are allowed up to 20 withdrawals per month.\\n\\n## How to confirm your benefits are active\\n\\n- Check your account details to verify:\\n  - The minimum balance requirement displays as $5,000.\\n  - The APY displays as 5.5% plus a 0.025% relationship bonus.\\n  - Your monthly limits show up to $30 in ATM fee rebates and up to 20 withdrawals.\\n\\n2. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 18.8813\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n3. Credit Card APY Bonuses: Stacking Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_045\\n   Score: 17.5018\\n   Content: ## Credit Card APY Bonus Stacking Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank credit cards that each provide an APY bonus on their savings account, the bonuses do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable credit card APY bonus is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank credit cards linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each credit card, the corresponding APY bonus is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST credit card APY bonus is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other credit card bonuses are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer holds:\\n- Gold Rewards Card: +0.025% APY bonus\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.15% APY bonus\\n- EcoCard: +0.6% APY bonus\\n\\nThe customer receives only the EcoCard bonus of +0.6% (the highest), not the sum of all three.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Credit card APY bonuses do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, credit card APY bonuses DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Checking account APY boosts (e.g., Green Account checking boost)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium credit cards while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n4. Linked Checking Account APY Boost: Selection Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_046\\n   Score: 17.1072\\n   Content: ## Multiple Checking Account APY Boost Selection Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank checking accounts that each provide an APY boost on their savings account, the boosts do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable checking account APY boost is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank checking accounts linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each checking account, the corresponding APY boost for the savings account type is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST checking account APY boost is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other checking account boosts are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer with a Gold Savings Account holds:\\n- Green Account (checking): +0.75% APY boost\\n- Purple Account (checking): +0.1% APY boost\\n\\nThe customer receives only the Green Account boost of +0.75% (the highest), not the sum of both.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Checking account APY boosts do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, checking account APY boosts DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Credit card APY bonuses (only highest credit card bonus applies)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium checking accounts while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n### Agent Responsibility\\n\\nWhen investigating interest discrepancies for customers with multiple checking accounts, agents must:\\n1. Identify all checking accounts the customer holds\\n2. Determine which checking account provides the highest APY boost for the savings account type\\n3. Verify that the system is applying the highest boost, not a lower one\\n4. If the system selected the wrong checking account, calculate the correct APY and apply an interest correction\\n\\n5. Silver Plus: Differences from Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_002\\n   Score: 16.6657\\n   Content: ## What changes with Silver Plus\\n\\n### Tiered APY\\n- Silver Plus offers tiered APY with two levels:\\n  - Tier 1 APY: 3.0% for balances below the Tier 2 threshold.\\n  - Tier 2 APY: 4.5% for balances at or above the Tier 2 threshold.\\n\\n### Withdrawal flexibility\\n- Increased access with up to 15 free withdrawals per month.\\n\\n### ATM fee support\\n- Receive ATM fee rebates up to 25 each month.\\n\\n### Statement delivery\\n- Paper statements are available for Silver Plus Account holders.\\n- The monthly paper statement fee is $0.00. You can enable paper statements in your account settings.\\n- Paperless statements are NOT required for this account (unlike Green Account (savings) which requires paperless).\\n\\n### Relationship benefits\\n- Earn an additional relationship APY bonus of 0.025% when you qualify under the relationship criteria.\\n\\n6. Silver Plus Saver Account: Complete Guide\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_plus_saver_001\\n   Score: 16.1650\\n   Content: ## Eligibility and Minimum Balance\\n- You must maintain a minimum balance of $5,000 to keep the Silver Plus Saver account in good standing.\\n- If your balance is anticipated to dip below $5,000, consider timing deposits and withdrawals to avoid falling under the requirement.\\n\\n## Interest and APY Structure\\n- Balances below the tier 2 threshold earn 2.5% APY.\\n- Balances above the tier 2 threshold earn 4.0% APY.\\n\\n### Relationship APY Bonuses\\nIf you hold an eligible Business Rewards Card, an APY bonus is added to your base APY:\\n- Business Silver Rewards Card: +0.18% APY\\n- Business Gold Rewards Card: +0.38% APY\\n- Business Platinum Rewards Card: +0.62% APY\\n\\nThe bonus applies to the base APY for the balance tier you qualify for.\\n\\n### Example APYs With Relationship Bonuses\\nBelow are example total APYs when a relationship bonus applies:\\n\\n- Balance below tier 2 threshold (base 2.5%):\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card: 2.68% (2.5% + 0.18%)\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card: 2.88% (2.5% + 0.38%)\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card: 3.12% (2.5% + 0.62%)\\n\\n- Balance above tier 2 threshold (base 4.0%):\\n  - With Business Silver Rewards Card: 4.18% (4.0% + 0.18%)\\n  - With Business Gold Rewards Card: 4.38% (4.0% + 0.38%)\\n  - With Business Platinum Rewards Card: 4.62% (4.0% + 0.62%)\\n\\n## Withdrawals and Transfers\\nSilver Plus Saver offers higher withdrawal limits and improved transfer capabilities compared to Silver Saver. To make the most of these enhancements:\\n- Plan large withdrawals in advance to ensure smooth processing.\\n- Use scheduled transfers for recurring payments to maintain your target balance above $5,000.\\n- For unusually large or time-sensitive transfers, initiate earlier in the business day to reduce the risk of delays.\\n\\n## Upgrading from Silver Saver\\nIf you are moving up from Silver Saver:\\n- Confirm you can maintain at least $5,000 in Silver Plus Saver.\\n- Request an upgrade through your online banking or by contacting support. Your balances will begin earning at the Silver Plus Saver rates as soon as the upgrade is completed.\\n\\n## How to Verify Your Current APY and Bonus\\n- In online banking, open the Silver Plus Saver account details to view:\\n  - Your current balance tier (below or above the tier 2 threshold)\\n  - Base APY for that tier (2.5% or 4.0%)\\n  - Any relationship APY bonus applied (e.g., 0.38%) \\n- Review after any balance change or card status update to confirm your effective APY.\\n\\n7. Silver Account: Platinum Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_009\\n   Score: 15.3542\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nSilver Account holders who also have a Platinum Rewards Card receive enhanced withdrawal privileges. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 5 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 10 + 5 = 15 withdrawals per month. This benefit is automatically applied when both accounts are linked under the same customer profile. Combined with the existing 15 ATM fee rebates and 0.025% relationship bonus, Platinum Rewards Card holders get an elevated Silver Account experience.\\n\\n## APY bonuses from credit cards\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.2%\\n- Diamond Elite Card: +0.25%\\n\\n## What you receive as a Platinum Rewards Card holder\\n\\n- Additional free withdrawals: +5 per month on top of your standard 10 free withdrawals\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 10 + 5 = 15\\n- ATM fee relief: Up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month\\n- Earnings boost: An additional 0.025% relationship bonus added to your APY when eligible\\n\\n## Activation and eligibility\\n\\n- The enhanced withdrawal limit is automatically applied when your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile.\\n- The 0.025% relationship bonus and 15 ATM fee rebates apply in the same profile-linked setup.\\n\\n### How to confirm your accounts are linked\\n\\n1. Sign in to Rho-Bank Online Banking or the mobile app.\\n2. Open your customer profile and review your list of accounts and cards.\\n3. Verify that your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card appear under the same customer profile.\\n4. If you do not see both products under one profile, consolidate them to a single profile or contact us for assistance.\\n\\n## Using your monthly withdrawal allowance\\n\\n- Counting method: Any transaction classified as a withdrawal under your Silver Account terms counts toward your monthly total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Cycle timing: Your free withdrawal count resets at the start of each monthly statement cycle.\\n- Beyond the limit: Transactions above your free monthly total may be subject to standard Silver Account withdrawal charges.\\n\\nExample:\\n- You make 12 withdrawals in a month: all 12 are free.\\n- You make 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n- You make 16 withdrawals in a month: the first 15 are free; the 16th may incur standard charges.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You are eligible for up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- Rebates apply after ATM fees post to your Silver Account; check your transaction history for the corresponding credit within the same month.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- When your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile, an additional 0.025% is added to your APY as a relationship bonus.\\n- The relationship bonus is reflected in your APY while eligibility is maintained.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting and tips\\n\\n- If you do not see the extra withdrawals or 0.025% reflected, confirm both products are under the same customer profile.\\n- Check that you are within the current monthly statement cycle for the added withdrawals to apply.\\n- Review your transaction history to verify ATM fee charges and corresponding rebates up to 15 for the month.\\n\\n8. Gold Plus Account: Credit Card APY Bonuses\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_plus_account_009\\n   Score: 14.3344\\n   Content: ## Credit card APY bonuses for Gold Plus Account holders\\n\\nHolding certain Rho-Bank credit cards provides bonus APY on your Gold Plus Account balance. These bonuses are automatically applied when you hold both the credit card and savings account under the same customer profile.\\n\\n### Available credit card APY bonuses\\n\\n| Credit Card | APY Bonus |\\n|---|---|\\n| Bronze Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Silver Rewards Card | +0.1% |\\n| Gold Rewards Card | +0.35% |\\n| Platinum Rewards Card | +0.2% |\\n| Diamond Elite Card | +0.25% |\\n| EcoCard | +0.1% |\\n| Green Rewards Card | +0.05% |\\n| Crypto-Cash Back Card | +0.3% |\\n\\n### How to qualify\\n\\n1. Open or maintain a Gold Plus Account.\\n2. Hold an eligible Rho-Bank credit card under the same customer profile.\\n3. The APY bonus is automatically applied to your Gold Plus Account earnings.\\n\\n9. Green Fee-Free Account Referral Program\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_007\\n   Score: 14.3277\\n   Content: ## Refer and earn\\n\\nHelp others discover the Green Fee-Free Account and earn rewards for successful referrals.\\n\\n### Bonus structure\\n- Your reward: $20 per successful referral\\n- New member reward: $35 welcome bonus\\n- Annual limit: 4 referrals per year\\n\\n### Qualification requirements\\nFor a referral to count as successful:\\n- The new account holder must deposit at least $300\\n- This deposit must be made within 60 days of opening their account\\n- Your Rho-Bank checking relationship must span at least 30 days.\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n| Detail | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| You earn | $20 |\\n| They earn | $35 |\\n| Max per year | 4 |\\n| Required deposit | $300 |\\n| Deposit deadline | 60 days |\\n| Referrer eligibility | 30 days |\\n\\n### How to participate\\n1. Access your referral link from your account dashboard\\n2. Share with potential new members\\n3. Track your referrals and bonuses in the rewards section\\n\\n10. Gold Account: Credit Card APY Bonuses\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_014\\n   Score: 14.2758\\n   Content: ## Credit card APY bonuses for Gold Account holders\\n\\nHolding certain Rho-Bank credit cards provides bonus APY on your Gold Account balance. These bonuses are automatically applied when you hold both the credit card and savings account under the same customer profile.\\n\\n### Available credit card APY bonuses\\n\\n| Credit Card | APY Bonus |\\n|---|---|\\n| Bronze Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Silver Rewards Card | +0.2% |\\n| Gold Rewards Card | +0.025% |\\n| Platinum Rewards Card | +0.15% |\\n| Diamond Elite Card | +0.3% |\\n| EcoCard | +0.6% |\\n| Green Rewards Card | +0.35% |\\n| Crypto-Cash Back Card | +0% |\\n\\n### Additional Gold Rewards Card benefits\\n\\nGold Rewards Card holders receive an additional benefit: the minimum balance requirement is reduced from $10,000 to $5,000.\\n\\n### How to qualify\\n\\n1. Open or maintain a Gold Account.\\n2. Hold an eligible Rho-Bank credit card under the same customer profile.\\n3. The APY bonus is automatically applied to your Gold Account earnings.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_73Fz9RPzlQVx49NgmqYpHJ1t\",\"output\":\"1. Silver Plus: Differences from Silver Account\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_002\\n   Score: 17.3493\\n   Content: ## What changes with Silver Plus\\n\\n### Tiered APY\\n- Silver Plus offers tiered APY with two levels:\\n  - Tier 1 APY: 3.0% for balances below the Tier 2 threshold.\\n  - Tier 2 APY: 4.5% for balances at or above the Tier 2 threshold.\\n\\n### Withdrawal flexibility\\n- Increased access with up to 15 free withdrawals per month.\\n\\n### ATM fee support\\n- Receive ATM fee rebates up to 25 each month.\\n\\n### Statement delivery\\n- Paper statements are available for Silver Plus Account holders.\\n- The monthly paper statement fee is $0.00. You can enable paper statements in your account settings.\\n- Paperless statements are NOT required for this account (unlike Green Account (savings) which requires paperless).\\n\\n### Relationship benefits\\n- Earn an additional relationship APY bonus of 0.025% when you qualify under the relationship criteria.\\n\\n2. Gold Account: Gold Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_gold_account_013\\n   Score: 17.2811\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nGold Account holders who also have a Gold Rewards Card receive exclusive benefits that make the account more accessible. The standard minimum balance requirement of $10,000 is reduced to $5,000 for Gold Rewards Card holders. Additionally, you receive a 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base 5.5% rate. Combined with the existing 30 ATM fee rebates and 20 monthly withdrawals, Gold Rewards Card holders enjoy a premium savings experience with lower balance requirements.\\n\\n## Benefits summary for Gold Rewards Card holders\\n\\n- Reduced minimum balance: $5,000 (down from $10,000)\\n- Relationship bonus APY: 0.025% on top of the base 5.5%\\n- ATM fee rebates: Up to $30 per month\\n- Monthly withdrawals: Up to 20 per month\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Benefit | Gold Rewards Card holder value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $5,000 (standard: $10,000) |\\n| APY rate | 5.5% + 0.025% |\\n| ATM fee rebates (monthly max) | $30 |\\n| Monthly withdrawal limit | 20 |\\n\\n## Reduced minimum balance\\n\\n- If you hold a Gold Rewards Card, your required minimum balance to maintain the Gold Account is automatically reduced to $5,000.\\n- The standard minimum balance for the Gold Account remains $10,000, but the override applies as long as your Gold Rewards Card is active and associated with your account.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Without the card: Minimum balance requirement is $10,000.\\n- With the card: Minimum balance requirement is $5,000.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- Your Gold Account earns the base 5.5% APY.\\n- As a Gold Rewards Card holder, you receive an additional 0.025% relationship bonus APY on top of the base rate.\\n\\nExample:\\n- Base APY: 5.5%\\n- Relationship bonus APY: +0.025%\\n- Total APY with the bonus: 6.0%\\n\\nNotes:\\n- The relationship bonus is additive to the base rate; it is not a multiplier.\\n- The bonus applies while your Gold Rewards Card remains active and associated with your Gold Account.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates and monthly withdrawals\\n\\n- You continue to receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- You are allowed up to 20 withdrawals per month.\\n\\n## How to confirm your benefits are active\\n\\n- Check your account details to verify:\\n  - The minimum balance requirement displays as $5,000.\\n  - The APY displays as 5.5% plus a 0.025% relationship bonus.\\n  - Your monthly limits show up to $30 in ATM fee rebates and up to 20 withdrawals.\\n\\n3. Evergreen Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_evergreen_account_001\\n   Score: 16.5088\\n   Content: ## Key highlights\\n- One tree planted for every $750 you spend with your debit card\\n- Automatic carbon offset on purchases: $1.25 g CO2 per $1 spent\\n- Earn 0.05% APY on your checking balance\\n- Extra rewards at partner eco-friendly brands: +1.75% cashback\\n- Early direct deposit: get your paycheck up to 2 days early\\n- Mobile check deposit daily limit: $3,500\\n\\n### Linked savings boosts\\n- Link a Green Account (savings): +0.55% APY boost\\n- Link a Diamond Elite Savings Account: +0.15% APY boost\\n\\n### How tree planting works (at a glance)\\n- For every $750 in eligible spending, we plant one tree on your behalf.\\n- Example: Spend $750 → 1 tree planted; spend 5× that amount → 5 trees planted.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00 per transaction.\\n- Third-party ATM operator fees may also apply.\\n\\n### Refer and grow the green community\\n- Refer others to join Evergreen and earn $35 per successful referral\\n- New members receive $25 as a welcome bonus\\n- Earn up to 6 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n| Feature | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Tree planting threshold | $750 per tree |\\n| Carbon offset rate | $1.25 g per $1 |\\n| Checking APY | 0.05% |\\n| Eco brand cashback bonus | +1.75% |\\n| Early direct deposit | Up to 2 days early |\\n| Mobile deposit daily limit | $3,500 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 2% (min $3.00) |\\n| Green Savings APY boost | +0.55% |\\n| Diamond Elite Savings APY boost | +0.15% |\\n| Referral bonus (you earn) | $35 |\\n| Referral bonus (they receive) | $25 |\\n| Max referrals per year | 6 |\\n\\n4. Credit Card APY Bonuses: Stacking Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_045\\n   Score: 15.8354\\n   Content: ## Credit Card APY Bonus Stacking Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank credit cards that each provide an APY bonus on their savings account, the bonuses do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable credit card APY bonus is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank credit cards linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each credit card, the corresponding APY bonus is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST credit card APY bonus is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other credit card bonuses are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer holds:\\n- Gold Rewards Card: +0.025% APY bonus\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.15% APY bonus\\n- EcoCard: +0.6% APY bonus\\n\\nThe customer receives only the EcoCard bonus of +0.6% (the highest), not the sum of all three.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Credit card APY bonuses do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, credit card APY bonuses DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Checking account APY boosts (e.g., Green Account checking boost)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium credit cards while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n5. Green Account (savings): EcoCard holder exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_009\\n   Score: 15.2207\\n   Content: ## EcoCard holder benefits overview\\n\\nGreen Account (savings) holders who also have an EcoCard receive enhanced benefits that make eco-conscious banking even more rewarding. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 7 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 8 + 7 = 15 withdrawals per month. You also receive 20 in ATM fee rebates monthly. Combined with the existing 0.5% bonus APY for EcoCard holders on top of the base 4.0% rate, this creates a comprehensive eco-friendly savings experience with maximum flexibility.\\n\\n## What you get as an EcoCard holder\\n\\n- Increased monthly free withdrawals: 8 + 7 = 15 total free withdrawals per month\\n- ATM fee rebates: up to $20 in rebates each month\\n- Rate boost: 0.5% bonus APY on top of the base 4.0% rate (example total: 4.75%)\\n\\n## Increased free withdrawals\\n\\n- Your free withdrawal allowance increases by 7 each month, for a total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Examples:\\n  - 10 withdrawals in a month: all 10 are free.\\n  - 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n  - More than 15 withdrawals in a month: any withdrawals beyond 15 are not free.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You receive up to $20 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- If total ATM operator fees in a month exceed $20, the excess amount is not rebated.\\n- Tip: Keep your receipts or review your statements to track how much of the $20 monthly cap you have used.\\n\\n## Bonus APY for EcoCard holders\\n\\n- Your Green Account earns the base 4.0% APY plus a 0.5% bonus when you hold an EcoCard.\\n- Example: 4.0% + 0.5% = 4.75% APY.\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 8 + 7 = 15\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: $20\\n- APY boost: 4.0% base + 0.5% bonus\\n\\n6. Silver Account: Platinum Rewards Card holder benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_account_009\\n   Score: 15.0155\\n   Content: ## Overview\\n\\nSilver Account holders who also have a Platinum Rewards Card receive enhanced withdrawal privileges. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 5 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 10 + 5 = 15 withdrawals per month. This benefit is automatically applied when both accounts are linked under the same customer profile. Combined with the existing 15 ATM fee rebates and 0.025% relationship bonus, Platinum Rewards Card holders get an elevated Silver Account experience.\\n\\n## APY bonuses from credit cards\\n- Platinum Rewards Card: +0.2%\\n- Diamond Elite Card: +0.25%\\n\\n## What you receive as a Platinum Rewards Card holder\\n\\n- Additional free withdrawals: +5 per month on top of your standard 10 free withdrawals\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 10 + 5 = 15\\n- ATM fee relief: Up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month\\n- Earnings boost: An additional 0.025% relationship bonus added to your APY when eligible\\n\\n## Activation and eligibility\\n\\n- The enhanced withdrawal limit is automatically applied when your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile.\\n- The 0.025% relationship bonus and 15 ATM fee rebates apply in the same profile-linked setup.\\n\\n### How to confirm your accounts are linked\\n\\n1. Sign in to Rho-Bank Online Banking or the mobile app.\\n2. Open your customer profile and review your list of accounts and cards.\\n3. Verify that your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card appear under the same customer profile.\\n4. If you do not see both products under one profile, consolidate them to a single profile or contact us for assistance.\\n\\n## Using your monthly withdrawal allowance\\n\\n- Counting method: Any transaction classified as a withdrawal under your Silver Account terms counts toward your monthly total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Cycle timing: Your free withdrawal count resets at the start of each monthly statement cycle.\\n- Beyond the limit: Transactions above your free monthly total may be subject to standard Silver Account withdrawal charges.\\n\\nExample:\\n- You make 12 withdrawals in a month: all 12 are free.\\n- You make 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n- You make 16 withdrawals in a month: the first 15 are free; the 16th may incur standard charges.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You are eligible for up to 15 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- Rebates apply after ATM fees post to your Silver Account; check your transaction history for the corresponding credit within the same month.\\n\\n## Relationship bonus APY\\n\\n- When your Silver Account and Platinum Rewards Card are linked under the same customer profile, an additional 0.025% is added to your APY as a relationship bonus.\\n- The relationship bonus is reflected in your APY while eligibility is maintained.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting and tips\\n\\n- If you do not see the extra withdrawals or 0.025% reflected, confirm both products are under the same customer profile.\\n- Check that you are within the current monthly statement cycle for the added withdrawals to apply.\\n- Review your transaction history to verify ATM fee charges and corresponding rebates up to 15 for the month.\\n\\n7. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 14.7622\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n8. Linked Checking Account APY Boost: Selection Policy\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_046\\n   Score: 14.6250\\n   Content: ## Multiple Checking Account APY Boost Selection Policy\\n\\nWhen a customer holds multiple Rho-Bank checking accounts that each provide an APY boost on their savings account, the boosts do NOT stack. Only the highest applicable checking account APY boost is applied to the customer's savings account.\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n1. The system identifies all active Rho-Bank checking accounts linked to the customer's profile.\\n2. For each checking account, the corresponding APY boost for the savings account type is determined.\\n3. Only the HIGHEST checking account APY boost is applied to the savings account.\\n4. Other checking account boosts are not added on top.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\nIf a customer with a Gold Savings Account holds:\\n- Green Account (checking): +0.75% APY boost\\n- Purple Account (checking): +0.1% APY boost\\n\\nThe customer receives only the Green Account boost of +0.75% (the highest), not the sum of both.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n\\n- Checking account APY boosts do NOT stack with each other.\\n- However, checking account APY boosts DO stack with other types of bonuses, such as:\\n  - Credit card APY bonuses (only highest credit card bonus applies)\\n  - Relationship bonuses for holding multiple Rho-Bank products\\n  - Account tier bonuses\\n\\n### Why this policy exists\\n\\nThis policy ensures that customers receive a meaningful benefit for holding premium checking accounts while maintaining sustainable interest rates across the product portfolio.\\n\\n### Agent Responsibility\\n\\nWhen investigating interest discrepancies for customers with multiple checking accounts, agents must:\\n1. Identify all checking accounts the customer holds\\n2. Determine which checking account provides the highest APY boost for the savings account type\\n3. Verify that the system is applying the highest boost, not a lower one\\n4. If the system selected the wrong checking account, calculate the correct APY and apply an interest correction\\n\\n9. FAQ: Green Account (savings)\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_005\\n   Score: 14.1892\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions\\n\\n### What APY does the Green Account (savings) earn?\\n- 4.0%\\n\\n### Do I need to maintain a minimum balance?\\n- Yes. The minimum balance requirement is $500.\\n\\n### Is there a monthly maintenance fee if I do not meet the minimum balance?\\n- $0.00\\n\\n### Can I boost my APY by pairing with an EcoCard or Green Rewards Card?\\n- Yes. You can receive a bonus of 0.5%.\\n\\n### Does Rho-Bank match donations to partner environmental charities?\\n- Yes. Rho-Bank matches at 50%.\\n\\n### How do I confirm my rate and benefits?\\n- Review your account details in online or mobile banking to see your current APY of 4.0% and any applicable bonus of 0.5%.\\n\\n10. Green Account (checking) at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_account_(checking)_001\\n   Score: 13.9498\\n   Content: ## Highlights\\n- No overdraft fees and no overdraft coverage; transactions that exceed your available balance are declined\\n- Earn 0.11% APY on your checking balance\\n- Get direct deposits up to 1 day early\\n- Mobile check deposits up to $3,000 per day\\n- Boost a linked savings account's APY: Gold +0.75% or Silver +0.25%\\n\\n## Fees and limits\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum daily balance to waive fee | $1,350 |\\n| Paper statement fee (monthly) | $2.50 |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $3.00 |\\n| Returned deposit fee | $17.50 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire (receive) | $15.00 |\\n| APY on balance | 0.11% |\\n| Daily mobile check deposit limit | $3,000 |\\n| Early direct deposit | Up to 1 day early |\\n\\n## Referral program\\nRefer friends and family to open a Green Account and earn rewards:\\n- You earn: $20 per successful referral\\n- They receive: $30 welcome bonus\\n- Maximum referrals per year: 5\\n- Qualifying deposit required: $500 within 60 days\\n- Account tenure requirement: 30 days since becoming a Rho-Bank checking customer.\\n\\n## Important details\\n- To avoid the monthly maintenance fee, maintain a minimum daily balance of $1,350 each statement cycle\\n- If you opt for paper statements, a $2.50 monthly fee applies\\n- Using a non-network ATM incurs a $3.00 fee; the ATM owner may charge additional fees\\n- Deposited checks returned unpaid result in a $17.50 fee\\n- Receiving a domestic wire transfer costs $15.00\\n- Early direct deposit availability depends on when your payer submits the deposit; funds can post up to 1 day early\\n- Savings APY boosts apply when you link an eligible Gold or Silver Savings Account: +0.75% or +0.25% respectively\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEe2yq8QJD1jqUUQxGL5xBvaBosgkfC0yryloi2asT3hDzjWwkfJrSkW1rtYf-sPJ4SNvzNKGw